{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791377769722,"sessionID":"ses_ee997d19effeg3ZWpbO7vo4zhQ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_00_o2dhMvg4mk0DGNHzgHs85891","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Implementation: theme on login\n\nid: create\nstatus: open\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nThe white surface on the login page under the Nord theme is caused by literal\nwhite utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) on the auth cards. Single-mode\nthemes never add the `.dark` class, so the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback\nnever fires and the card stays white (`--color-white` under Nord is the\nnear-white `#eceff4`). That exact fix was already delivered on `main` by commit\n`70f6236` (Job: `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) and is present on this branch\nvia the `main` merge, so **no additional product code change was required**. The\ntasks in `tasks.md` predate that merge and are stale relative to the current\ntree; this is documented in `notes.md`.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: Captured the environment/code facts in\n  `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md`. Confirmed the code mechanism and\n  that the fix is already an ancestor of `HEAD` (`git merge-base --is-ancestor\n  70f6236 HEAD`). The production-browser facts the task requests (LocalStorage\n  `theme`, `documentElement.className`, computed card background, deployed\n  version) cannot be read by an unattended agent from another origin. No product\n  code changed.\n\nTASK-2: No change needed — verified all six auth cards already carry\n  `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72/100,\n  reset-password:72/85/105, logout:27, verify:44), the exact swap the task asks\n  for. The two secondary substitutions from the analyst\n  (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`, and\n  `border-white/5` → token border) were deliberately **not** applied: with the\n  card now themed, labels inherit a correctly themed color from\n  `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` (`text-c-neutral-8` /\n  `dark:text-c-neutral-2`), and replacing the border would change default\n  light/dark rendering, which TASK-2 explicitly requires to stay\n  pixel-identical (and no target token was specified).\n\nTASK-3: No change needed — `src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte` already\n  uses `bg-c-bg-modal` (the popup was fixed by the same commit `70f6236`).\n  This was the task's open question; it is resolved as already fixed.\n\nTASK-4: Verification was limited to static, code/commit review. `node_modules`\n  is not installed in this environment, so `npm run check`, `npm run lint`,\n  `npm test`, and build/preview could not be run; per the project rule no\n  packages were installed. No rendered screenshots were produced.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- Rendered verification (themes × default light/dark) still needs to be done\n  once dependencies and a backend are available. Nothing in the diff should\n  change rendering (the branch adds no product code relative to `main`).\n- Production is most likely running a build older than `70f6236`; deploying\n  current `main` (which this branch already contains) resolves the white card.\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale (it describes the pre-merge\n  auth-card classes). It was left as the analyst's artifact and committed for\n  worktree hygiene; the corrected picture is in `notes.md`.\n- Open follow-ups inherited from `tasks.md` (not in scope here): pre-paint theme\n  script (FOUC hardening), `html` background-color rule, account-synced theme\n  setting, `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`.\n","filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implem