{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791393955143,"sessionID":"ses_ee89c3d70ffePPWoBsm219uqmf","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_00_tPJC9EcqTcSJdCraB20R6600","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","content":"# Implementation: theme on login\n\nid: create\nstatus: open\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nThe white surface on the login page under the Nord theme is caused by literal\nwhite utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) on the auth cards. Single-mode\nthemes never add the `.dark` class, so the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback\nnever fires and the card stays white (`--color-white` under Nord is the\nnear-white `#eceff4`). That exact fix was already delivered on `main` by commit\n`70f6236` (Job: `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) and reached this branch via the\n`main` merge (`8c0ad30`), so **no additional product code change was required**.\nThe tasks in `tasks.md` predate that merge and describe the pre-fix tree; the\ncorrected picture is documented in `notes.md`.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: Captured the environment/code facts in\n  `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md`. Confirmed the code mechanism and\n  that the fix is an ancestor of `HEAD` (`git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236\n  HEAD`). The production-browser facts the task asks for (LocalStorage `theme`,\n  `documentElement.className`, computed card background, deployed version) cannot\n  be read by an unattended agent from another origin, so only local code/commit\n  facts were captured. No product code changed.\n\nTASK-2: No change needed for the primary fix — verified all six auth cards\n  already carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72/100,\n  reset-password:72/85/105, logout:27, verify:44), the exact swap the task asks\n  for. The two secondary substitutions were deliberately **not** applied:\n  - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: with the card now\n    themed, labels already inherit a correctly themed color from\n    `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` (`text-c-neutral-8` /\n    `dark:text-c-neutral-2`), so there is no washed-out-text bug. Adding an\n    explicit light-mode token would change default light rendering\n    (`--color-c-neutral-8` gray-800 → `--color-c-neutral-9` gray-900), which\n    TASK-2 explicitly requires to stay pixel-identical.\n  - `border-white/5` → token border: the same `border-2 border-white/5\n    bg-c-bg-surface` card pattern is also used by `/setup` (3 instances), so\n    changing only the auth cards would make them inconsistent; and the border is\n    decorative, so a swap would alter default rendering. No target token was\n    specified.\n\nTASK-3: No change needed — `src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte:63` already\n  uses `bg-c-bg-modal` (fixed by the same commit `70f6236`). This resolves the\n  task's open question.\n\nTASK-4: Static verification only. `node_modules` is not installed in this\n  environment, so `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, and build/preview\n  could not be run; per the project hard rule no packages were installed. No\n  dependency was available to install/substitute. `git diff --check` is clean and\n  the branch adds no product code relative to `main`, so there is no rendering\n  change introduced by this job to verify.\n\n## Worktree note\n\nAn earlier, interrupted run of this job left uncommitted cosmetic edits on four\nauth pages (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`). They were\nreverted for the reasons in TASK-2 above so the worktree matches the\nalready-fixed, committed state. The branch's only changes relative to `main` are\nthe job's own docs (`git diff --name-only main...HEAD`).\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- Rendered verification (themes × default light/dark) still needs to be done\n  once dependencies and a backend are available. Nothing in the branch should\n  change rendering (it adds no product code relative to `main`).\n- Production is most likely running a build older than `70f6236`; deploying\n  current `main` (which this branch already contains) resolves the white card.\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale: it describes the pre-merge\n  auth-card classes. It was left as the analyst's artifact; the corrected picture\n  is in `notes.md`.\n- Optional consistency follow-up (not in scope): auth-page headings/labels use a\n  bare `dark:text-white` while the rest of the app mostly uses\n  `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`. Aligning them would be a cosmetic change\n  that alters default light rendering.\n- Open follow-ups inherited from `tasks.md` (not in scope here): pre-paint theme\n  script (FOUC hardening), `html` background-color rule, account-synced theme\n  setting, `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`.\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791393955108,"end":1791393955130}},"id":"prt_117666e17001E6tbIh27Dcx8T6","sessionID":"ses_ee89c3d70ffePPWoBsm219uqmf","messageID":"msg_117665d91001jrEilCrg2DyQKZ"}}
