{"type":"text","timestamp":1791393975112,"sessionID":"ses_ee89c3d70ffePPWoBsm219uqmf","part":{"id":"prt_11766c22f001soKVVodsxbBot2","messageID":"msg_11766b6cc0019iYhocN5c3mnep","sessionID":"ses_ee89c3d70ffePPWoBsm219uqmf","type":"text","text":"All tasks resolved. Summary of the work:\n\n## What the job was\n\nThe brief asked why the login page shows a white background under Nord on production while it looks correct locally. The analyst's `tasks.md` (rev 4) laid out TASK-1 → TASK-4.\n\n## What I found\n\n- The white surface is the auth **card** (not the page background). It was caused by the literal pair `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2`; single-mode themes remove the `.dark` class, so the themed fallback never fires and the card stays white.\n- **That exact fix already exists on this branch.** Commit `70f6236` (\"nord theme bug with todos\", 2026-08-25) swapped every auth card to `bg-c-bg-surface` and the TimePicker popup to `bg-c-bg-modal`. It reached this branch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`.\n- Therefore no product code change is required. The branch's only changes vs. `main` are the job docs — production is almost certainly running a build older than `70f6236`, and redeploying current `main` fixes it.\n\n## What I changed\n\n- **TASK-1:** environment/code facts are in the committed `notes.md` (prod-browser facts are not readable by an unattended agent).\n- **TASK-2:** verified all six auth cards already use `bg-c-bg-surface`. I deliberately did **not** apply the two secondary swaps: the label swap would change default light rendering (gray-800 → gray-900), violating TASK-2's own \"default must stay pixel-identical\" constraint, and the border swap would make the auth cards inconsistent with the identical `/setup` cards and alter default rendering.\n- **TASK-3:** `TimePicker.svelte` already uses `bg-c-bg-modal` — already fixed.\n- **TASK-4:** `node_modules` is not installed and the project hard rule forbids installing packages, so `check`/`lint`/`test`/build-preview could not run. `git diff --check` is clean and the branch adds no product code, so there is no new rendering to verify.\n- **Worktree hygiene:** an interrupted earlier run had left uncommitted cosmetic label edits on 4 auth pages. I reverted them and documented why, then committed the updated `implementation.md` and the job `session.log`. The source tree is clean.\n\n## One caveat\n\nThe harness keeps appending to `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log` as I work, so it can become modified again after my final commit; the surrounding `mg done` sweep handles that. Nothing under `src/` is uncommitted.","time":{"start":1791393972783,"end":1791393975107}}}
