{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791394075751,"sessionID":"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6","part":{"id":"prt_117685463001WlyEVBAcww6dDh","messageID":"msg_117684fab0015OTV4ARXCg9ZFc","sessionID":"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791394076658,"sessionID":"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_l0dKLLY3atxXRTVFc7V90906","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Notes: theme on login (TASK-1 environment facts + findings)\n2: \n3: id: create\n4: author: developer\n5: date: 2026-10-07\n6: \n7: ## TL;DR\n8: \n9: The white login surface reported in `brief.md` is caused by literal white\n10: utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) that do not react to single-mode\n11: themes. That exact pattern on the auth cards **has already been fixed on `main`**\n12: and is present on this branch after the merge (`8c0ad30`), so no further product\n13: change is required for TASK-2. This job is effectively a duplicate of the earlier\n14: fix; see \"Evidence\" below.\n15: \n16: ## Code facts (verified in this checkout)\n17: \n18: - Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false` (`src/lib/config/themes.ts`)\n19:   and `ThemeState.apply()` calls `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n20:   for them (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`). The `dark:` Tailwind variant\n21:   therefore never fires under Nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox,\n22:   dracula, terminal, paper, atari.\n23: - The app's correct themed-surface pattern is the semantic `--color-c-*` tokens\n24:   (`bg-c-bg`, `bg-c-bg-surface`, `bg-c-bg-modal`, `bg-c-bg-elevated`), which every\n25:   `static/themes/*/*.css` overrides at `:root`.\n26: - All six auth cards already use `bg-c-bg-surface` (the fix), not\n27:   `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`:\n28:   - `src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte:110`\n29:   - `src/routes/auth/register/+page.svelte:92`\n30:   - `src/routes/auth/forgot-password/+page.svelte:72,100`\n31:   - `src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte:72,85,105`\n32:   - `src/routes/auth/logout/+page.svelte:27`\n33:   - `src/routes/auth/verify/[user_id]/[token]/+page.svelte:44`\n34: - `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` returns **nothing** — the\n35:   problematic class pair has been fully swept from the codebase.\n36: - Inputs are not a source of white: `@tailwindcss/forms`' default white input\n37:   background is already overridden by `src/styles/components/forms.css` to\n38:   `background-color: var(--color-c-bg-elevated)`, which is themed\n39:   (Nord: `#434c5e`).\n40: - Label text is not a source of white either: `src/styles/base.css` sets the root\n41:   text to `text-c-neutral-7` (`dark:text-white`), and\n42:   `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` re-scopes it to `text-c-neutral-8`\n43:   (`dark:text-c-neutral-2`), so labels inherit a correctly themed color on the\n44:   now-themed card. The analyst's `dark:text-white` concern applied to the old\n45:   near-white card, which no longer exists.\n46: \n47: ## Evidence that the fix predates this branch's merge\n48: \n49: `git show 70f6236` (`nord theme bug with todos`, Job:\n50: `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25) changed exactly these auth-card\n51: lines from `... bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `... bg-c-bg-surface ...`\n52: (plus the TimePicker popup from `bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-3` to\n53: `bg-c-bg-modal`). `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true: the\n54: commit is in this branch via the `main` merge parent. `git diff main...HEAD`\n55: shows only the job's own docs — the branch adds no code relative to `main`.\n56: \n57: ## Hypothesis resolution (from tasks.md)\n58: \n59: - **Hypothesis A (different stored theme):** confirmed as a local reproduction\n60:   path — with the pre-70f6236 code, `theme=nord` on localhost shows the white\n61:   card because `bg-white` no longer has a `dark:` override. This is the same root\n62:   cause now fixed in code.\n63: - **Hypothesis B (version skew):** also consistent — prod is simply running a\n64:   frontend build older than `70f6236`, where the auth cards still had\n65:   `bg-white`. A deploy of current `main`/this branch resolves the white card.\n66: \n67: Both hypotheses converge on the same remedy already in the tree; no code change\n68: distinguishes them.\n69: \n70: ## Not capturable by an unattended agent\n71: \n72: TASK-1 asks for facts from the production browser: `localStorage.getItem('theme')`,\n73: `document.documentElement.className`, the computed card background, and the\n74: deployed frontend version. This session has no browser/prod access and cannot\n75: read another origin's LocalStorage, so only the local code/commit facts above\n76: were captured.\n77: \n78: ## Verification (TASK-4) limitation\n79: \n80: `node_modules` is not installed in this environment, so `npm run check`,\n81: `npm run lint`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, and `npm run preview` could not be\n82: run. Per the project hard rule (\"NEVER install packages without asking\") no\n83: packages were installed. The remaining verification is a code/commit review, not\n84: a rendered check. Recommended once dependencies and a backend are available:\n85: preview `/auth/login` and `/auth/register` under default light, default dark, and\n86: each single-mode theme (nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula,\n87: terminal, paper, atari) and confirm there are no white cards.\n\n(End of file - total 87 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Notes: theme on login (TASK-1 environment facts + findings)\n\nid: create\nauthor: developer\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n## TL;DR\n\nThe white login surface reported in `brief.md` is caused by literal white\nutilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) that do not react to single-mode\nthemes. That exact pattern on the auth cards **has already been fixed on `main`**\nand is present on this branch after the merge (`8c0ad30`), so no further product\nchange is required for TASK-2. This job is effectively a duplicate of the earlier\nfix; see \"Evidence\" below.\n\n## Code facts (verified in this checkout)\n\n- Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false` (`src/lib/config/themes.ts`)\n  and `ThemeState.apply()` calls `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n  for them (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`). The `dark:` Tailwind variant","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md","text":"# Notes: theme on login (TASK-1 environment facts + findings)\n\nid: create\nauthor: developer\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n## TL;DR\n\nThe white login surface reported in `brief.md` is caused by literal white\nutilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) that do not react to single-mode\nthemes. That exact pattern on the auth cards **has already been fixed on `main`**\nand is present on this branch after the merge (`8c0ad30`), so no further product\nchange is required for TASK-2. This job is effectively a duplicate of the earlier\nfix; see \"Evidence\" below.\n\n## Code facts (verified in this checkout)\n\n- Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false` (`src/lib/config/themes.ts`)\n  and `ThemeState.apply()` calls `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n  for them (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`). The `dark:` Tailwind variant\n  therefore never fires under Nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox,\n  dracula, terminal, paper, atari.\n- The app's correct themed-surface pattern is the semantic `--color-c-*` tokens\n  (`bg-c-bg`, `bg-c-bg-surface`, `bg-c-bg-modal`, `bg-c-bg-elevated`), which every\n  `static/themes/*/*.css` overrides at `:root`.\n- All six auth cards already use `bg-c-bg-surface` (the fix), not\n  `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`:\n  - `src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte:110`\n  - `src/routes/auth/register/+page.svelte:92`\n  - `src/routes/auth/forgot-password/+page.svelte:72,100`\n  - `src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte:72,85,105`\n  - `src/routes/auth/logout/+page.svelte:27`\n  - `src/routes/auth/verify/[user_id]/[token]/+page.svelte:44`\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` returns **nothing** — the\n  problematic class pair has been fully swept from the codebase.\n- Inputs are not a source of white: `@tailwindcss/forms`' default white input\n  background is already overridden by `src/styles/components/forms.css` to\n  `background-color: var(--color-c-bg-elevated)`, which is themed\n  (Nord: `#434c5e`).\n- Label text is not a source of white either: `src/styles/base.css` sets the root\n  text to `text-c-neutral-7` (`dark:text-white`), and\n  `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` re-scopes it to `text-c-neutral-8`\n  (`dark:text-c-neutral-2`), so labels inherit a correctly themed color on the\n  now-themed card. The analyst's `dark:text-white` concern applied to the old\n  near-white card, which no longer exists.\n\n## Evidence that the fix predates this branch's merge\n\n`git show 70f6236` (`nord theme bug with todos`, Job:\n`role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25) changed exactly these auth-card\nlines from `... bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `... bg-c-bg-surface ...`\n(plus the TimePicker popup from `bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-3` to\n`bg-c-bg-modal`). `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true: the\ncommit is in this branch via the `main` merge parent. `git diff main...HEAD`\nshows only the job's own docs — the branch adds no code relative to `main`.\n\n## Hypothesis resolution (from tasks.md)\n\n- **Hypothesis A (different stored theme):** confirmed as a local reproduction\n  path — with the pre-70f6236 code, `theme=nord` on localhost shows the white\n  card because `bg-white` no longer has a `dark:` override. This is the same root\n  cause now fixed in code.\n- **Hypothesis B (version skew):** also consistent — prod is simply running a\n  frontend build older than `70f6236`, where the auth cards still had\n  `bg-white`. A deploy of current `main`/this branch resolves the white card.\n\nBoth hypotheses converge on the same remedy already in the tree; no code change\ndistinguishes them.\n\n## Not capturable by an unattended agent\n\nTASK-1 asks for facts from the production browser: `localStorage.getItem('theme')`,\n`document.documentElement.className`, the computed card background, and the\ndeployed frontend version. This session has no browser/prod access and cannot\nread another origin's LocalStorage, so only the local code/commit facts above\nwere captured.\n\n## Verification (TASK-4) limitation\n\n`node_modules` is not installed in this environment, so `npm run check`,\n`npm run lint`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, and `npm run preview` could not be\nrun. Per the project hard rule (\"NEVER install packages without asking\") no\npackages were installed. The remaining verification is a code/commit review, not\na rendered check. Recommended once dependencies and a backend are available:\npreview `/auth/login` and `/auth/register` under default light, default dark, and\neach single-mode theme (nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula,\nterminal, paper, atari) and confirm there are no white cards.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":87,"totalLines":87,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md","time":{"start":1791394076403,"end":1791394076603}},"id":"prt_117685682001gqFf9zPrHPtlOp","sessionID":"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6","messageID":"msg_117684fab0015OTV4ARXCg9ZFc"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791394076659,"sessionID":"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_MjqL3nn0wrPI5sUekdNC3145","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Implementation: theme on login\n2: \n3: id: create\n4: status: open\n5: developer: deepseek-v4-flash\n6: date: 2026-10-07\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n9: \n10: ## Summary\n11: \n12: The white surface on the login page under the Nord theme is caused by literal\n13: white utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) on the auth cards. Single-mode\n14: themes never add the `.dark` class, so the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback\n15: never fires and the card stays white (`--color-white` under Nord is the\n16: near-white `#eceff4`). That exact fix was already delivered on `main` by commit\n17: `70f6236` (Job: `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) and reached this branch via the\n18: `main` merge (`8c0ad30`), so **no additional product code change was required**.\n19: The tasks in `tasks.md` predate that merge and describe the pre-fix tree; the\n20: corrected picture is documented in `notes.md`.\n21: \n22: ## Changes\n23: \n24: TASK-1: Captured the environment/code facts in\n25:   `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md`. Confirmed the code mechanism and\n26:   that the fix is an ancestor of `HEAD` (`git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236\n27:   HEAD`). The production-browser facts the task asks for (LocalStorage `theme`,\n28:   `documentElement.className`, computed card background, deployed version) cannot\n29:   be read by an unattended agent from another origin, so only local code/commit\n30:   facts were captured. No product code changed.\n31: \n32: TASK-2: No change needed for the primary fix — verified all six auth cards\n33:   already carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72/100,\n34:   reset-password:72/85/105, logout:27, verify:44), the exact swap the task asks\n35:   for. The two secondary substitutions were deliberately **not** applied:\n36:   - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: with the card now\n37:     themed, labels already inherit a correctly themed color from\n38:     `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` (`text-c-neutral-8` /\n39:     `dark:text-c-neutral-2`), so there is no washed-out-text bug. Adding an\n40:     explicit light-mode token would change default light rendering\n41:     (`--color-c-neutral-8` gray-800 → `--color-c-neutral-9` gray-900), which\n42:     TASK-2 explicitly requires to stay pixel-identical.\n43:   - `border-white/5` → token border: the same `border-2 border-white/5\n44:     bg-c-bg-surface` card pattern is also used by `/setup` (3 instances), so\n45:     changing only the auth cards would make them inconsistent; and the border is\n46:     decorative, so a swap would alter default rendering. No target token was\n47:     specified.\n48: \n49: TASK-3: No change needed — `src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte:63` already\n50:   uses `bg-c-bg-modal` (fixed by the same commit `70f6236`). This resolves the\n51:   task's open question.\n52: \n53: TASK-4: Static verification only. `node_modules` is not installed in this\n54:   environment, so `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, and build/preview\n55:   could not be run; per the project hard rule no packages were installed. No\n56:   dependency was available to install/substitute. `git diff --check` is clean and\n57:   the branch adds no product code relative to `main`, so there is no rendering\n58:   change introduced by this job to verify.\n59: \n60: ## Re-verification (second developer pass, 2026-10-07)\n61: \n62: Independently reconfirmed the above against the committed tree:\n63: \n64: - `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff --name-only\n65:   main...HEAD` lists only `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/*` (no product code).\n66: - All nine auth card blocks use `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92,\n67:   forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44).\n68: - `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/` returns only six decorative hits, none on the auth\n69:   routes: `ui/icons/IconPlate.svelte` (×3) and `todos/ScoreBar.svelte` (×3).\n70:   `TimePicker.svelte:63` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\n71: - `static/themes/nord/nord.css:34` defines `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252`; the\n72:   Nord `--color-white: #eceff4` (line 48) is what made the old literal `bg-white`\n73:   cards near-white. `src/styles/tokens.css` / `default.css` confirm the token\n74:   maps to `#ffffff` (light default) and `s-dark-2` (dark default).\n75: - No dev server, `node_modules`, or `build/` is present, so no rendered\n76:   `shot`/`preview` verification was possible in this environment; only static\n77:   verification. No product change was made in either pass.\n78: \n79: ## Worktree note\n80: \n81: An earlier, interrupted run of this job left uncommitted cosmetic edits on four\n82: auth pages (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`). They were\n83: reverted for the reasons in TASK-2 above so the worktree matches the\n84: already-fixed, committed state. The branch's only changes relative to `main` are\n85: the job's own docs (`git diff --name-only main...HEAD`).\n86: \n87: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n88: \n89: - Rendered verification (themes × default light/dark) still needs to be done\n90:   once dependencies and a backend are available. Nothing in the branch should\n91:   change rendering (it adds no product code relative to `main`).\n92: - Production is most likely running a build older than `70f6236`; deploying\n93:   current `main` (which this branch already contains) resolves the white card.\n94: - `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale: it describes the pre-merge\n95:   auth-card classes. It was left as the analyst's artifact; the corrected picture\n96:   is in `notes.md`.\n97: - Optional consistency follow-up (not in scope): auth-page headings/labels use a\n98:   bare `dark:text-white` while the rest of the app mostly uses\n99:   `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`. Aligning them would be a cosmetic change\n100:   that alters default light rendering.\n101: - Open follow-ups inherited from `tasks.md` (not in scope here): pre-paint theme\n102:   script (FOUC hardening), `html` background-color rule, account-synced theme\n103:   setting, `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`.\n\n(End of file - total 103 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation: theme on login\n\nid: create\nstatus: open\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nThe white surface on the login page under the Nord theme is caused by literal\nwhite utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) on the auth cards. Single-mode\nthemes never add the `.dark` class, so the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback\nnever fires and the card stays white (`--color-white` under Nord is the\nnear-white `#eceff4`). That exact fix was already delivered on `main` by commit\n`70f6236` (Job: `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) and reached this branch via the\n`main` merge (`8c0ad30`), so **no additional product code change was required**.\nThe tasks in `tasks.md` predate that merge and describe the pre-fix tree; the\ncorrected picture is documented in `notes.md`.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","text":"# Implementation: theme on login\n\nid: create\nstatus: open\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nThe white surface on the login page under the Nord theme is caused by literal\nwhite utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) on the auth cards. Single-mode\nthemes never add the `.dark` class, so the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback\nnever fires and the card stays white (`--color-white` under Nord is the\nnear-white `#eceff4`). That exact fix was already delivered on `main` by commit\n`70f6236` (Job: `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) and reached this branch via the\n`main` merge (`8c0ad30`), so **no additional product code change was required**.\nThe tasks in `tasks.md` predate that merge and describe the pre-fix tree; the\ncorrected picture is documented in `notes.md`.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: Captured the environment/code facts in\n  `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md`. Confirmed the code mechanism and\n  that the fix is an ancestor of `HEAD` (`git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236\n  HEAD`). The production-browser facts the task asks for (LocalStorage `theme`,\n  `documentElement.className`, computed card background, deployed version) cannot\n  be read by an unattended agent from another origin, so only local code/commit\n  facts were captured. No product code changed.\n\nTASK-2: No change needed for the primary fix — verified all six auth cards\n  already carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72/100,\n  reset-password:72/85/105, logout:27, verify:44), the exact swap the task asks\n  for. The two secondary substitutions were deliberately **not** applied:\n  - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: with the card now\n    themed, labels already inherit a correctly themed color from\n    `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` (`text-c-neutral-8` /\n    `dark:text-c-neutral-2`), so there is no washed-out-text bug. Adding an\n    explicit light-mode token would change default light rendering\n    (`--color-c-neutral-8` gray-800 → `--color-c-neutral-9` gray-900), which\n    TASK-2 explicitly requires to stay pixel-identical.\n  - `border-white/5` → token border: the same `border-2 border-white/5\n    bg-c-bg-surface` card pattern is also used by `/setup` (3 instances), so\n    changing only the auth cards would make them inconsistent; and the border is\n    decorative, so a swap would alter default rendering. No target token was\n    specified.\n\nTASK-3: No change needed — `src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte:63` already\n  uses `bg-c-bg-modal` (fixed by the same commit `70f6236`). This resolves the\n  task's open question.\n\nTASK-4: Static verification only. `node_modules` is not installed in this\n  environment, so `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, and build/preview\n  could not be run; per the project hard rule no packages were installed. No\n  dependency was available to install/substitute. `git diff --check` is clean and\n  the branch adds no product code relative to `main`, so there is no rendering\n  change introduced by this job to verify.\n\n## Re-verification (second developer pass, 2026-10-07)\n\nIndependently reconfirmed the above against the committed tree:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff --name-only\n  main...HEAD` lists only `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/*` (no product code).\n- All nine auth card blocks use `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92,\n  forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44).\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/` returns only six decorative hits, none on the auth\n  routes: `ui/icons/IconPlate.svelte` (×3) and `todos/ScoreBar.svelte` (×3).\n  `TimePicker.svelte:63` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\n- `static/themes/nord/nord.css:34` defines `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252`; the\n  Nord `--color-white: #eceff4` (line 48) is what made the old literal `bg-white`\n  cards near-white. `src/styles/tokens.css` / `default.css` confirm the token\n  maps to `#ffffff` (light default) and `s-dark-2` (dark default).\n- No dev server, `node_modules`, or `build/` is present, so no rendered\n  `shot`/`preview` verification was possible in this environment; only static\n  verification. No product change was made in either pass.\n\n## Worktree note\n\nAn earlier, interrupted run of this job left uncommitted cosmetic edits on four\nauth pages (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`). They were\nreverted for the reasons in TASK-2 above so the worktree matches the\nalready-fixed, committed state. The branch's only changes relative to `main` are\nthe job's own docs (`git diff --name-only main...HEAD`).\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- Rendered verification (themes × default light/dark) still needs to be done\n  once dependencies and a backend are available. Nothing in the branch should\n  change rendering (it adds no product code relative to `main`).\n- Production is most likely running a build older than `70f6236`; deploying\n  current `main` (which this branch already contains) resolves the white card.\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale: it describes the pre-merge\n  auth-card classes. It was left as the analyst's artifact; the corrected picture\n  is in `notes.md`.\n- Optional consistency follow-up (not in scope): auth-page headings/labels use a\n  bare `dark:text-white` while the rest of the app mostly uses\n  `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`. Aligning them would be a cosmetic change\n  that alters default light rendering.\n- Open follow-ups inherited from `tasks.md` (not in scope here): pre-paint theme\n  script (FOUC hardening), `html` background-color rule, account-synced theme\n  setting, `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":103,"totalLines":103,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791394076475,"end":1791394076607}},"id":"prt_1176856fa001WcEZ9DYYO64s31","sessionID":"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6","messageID":"msg_117684fab0015OTV4ARXCg9ZFc"}}
