{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791394144075,"sessionID":"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_03_jrIwH5ffJP2dqecMC52Z3458","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Implementation: theme on login\n2: \n3: id: create\n4: status: open\n5: developer: deepseek-v4-flash\n6: date: 2026-10-07\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n9: \n10: ## Summary\n11: \n12: The white surface on the login page under the Nord theme is caused by literal\n13: white utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) on the auth cards. Single-mode\n14: themes never add the `.dark` class, so the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback\n15: never fires and the card stays white (`--color-white` under Nord is the\n16: near-white `#eceff4`). That exact fix was already delivered on `main` by commit\n17: `70f6236` (Job: `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) and reached this branch via the\n18: `main` merge (`8c0ad30`), so **no additional product code change was required**.\n19: The tasks in `tasks.md` predate that merge and describe the pre-fix tree; the\n20: corrected picture is documented in `notes.md`.\n21: \n22: ## Changes\n23: \n24: TASK-1: Captured the environment/code facts in\n25:   `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md`. Confirmed the code mechanism and\n26:   that the fix is an ancestor of `HEAD` (`git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236\n27:   HEAD`). The production-browser facts the task asks for (LocalStorage `theme`,\n28:   `documentElement.className`, computed card background, deployed version) cannot\n29:   be read by an unattended agent from another origin, so only local code/commit\n30:   facts were captured. No product code changed.\n31: \n32: TASK-2: No change needed for the primary fix — verified all six auth cards\n33:   already carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72/100,\n34:   reset-password:72/85/105, logout:27, verify:44), the exact swap the task asks\n35:   for. The two secondary substitutions were deliberately **not** applied:\n36:   - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: with the card now\n37:     themed, labels already inherit a correctly themed color from\n38:     `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` (`text-c-neutral-8` /\n39:     `dark:text-c-neutral-2`), so there is no washed-out-text bug. Adding an\n40:     explicit light-mode token would change default light rendering\n41:     (`--color-c-neutral-8` gray-800 → `--color-c-neutral-9` gray-900), which\n42:     TASK-2 explicitly requires to stay pixel-identical.\n43:   - `border-white/5` → token border: the same `border-2 border-white/5\n44:     bg-c-bg-surface` card pattern is also used by `/setup` (3 instances), so\n45:     changing only the auth cards would make them inconsistent; and the border is\n46:     decorative, so a swap would alter default rendering. No target token was\n47:     specified.\n48: \n49: TASK-3: No change needed — `src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte:63` already\n50:   uses `bg-c-bg-modal` (fixed by the same commit `70f6236`). This resolves the\n51:   task's open question.\n52: \n53: TASK-4: Static verification only. `node_modules` is not installed in this\n54:   environment, so `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, and build/preview\n55:   could not be run; per the project hard rule no packages were installed. No\n56:   dependency was available to install/substitute. `git diff --check` is clean and\n57:   the branch adds no product code relative to `main`, so there is no rendering\n58:   change introduced by this job to verify.\n59: \n60: ## Re-verification (second developer pass, 2026-10-07)\n61: \n62: Independently reconfirmed the above against the committed tree:\n63: \n64: - `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff --name-only\n65:   main...HEAD` lists only `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/*` (no product code).\n66: - All nine auth card blocks use `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92,\n67:   forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44).\n68: - `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/` returns only six decorative hits, none on the auth\n69:   routes: `ui/icons/IconPlate.svelte` (×3) and `todos/ScoreBar.svelte` (×3).\n70:   `TimePicker.svelte:63` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\n71: - `static/themes/nord/nord.css:34` defines `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252`; the\n72:   Nord `--color-white: #eceff4` (line 48) is what made the old literal `bg-white`\n73:   cards near-white. `src/styles/tokens.css` / `default.css` confirm the token\n74:   maps to `#ffffff` (light default) and `s-dark-2` (dark default).\n75: - No dev server, `node_modules`, or `build/` is present, so no rendered\n76:   `shot`/`preview` verification was possible in this environment; only static\n77:   verification. No product change was made in either pass.\n78: \n79: ## Final pass (third developer pass, 2026-10-07)\n80: \n81: Re-ran the verification from scratch and reached the same conclusion:\n82: \n83: - `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD` shows\n84:   only `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/*`.\n85: - `70f6236` touched exactly the six auth pages and `TimePicker.svelte`; e.g.\n86:   `src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte` moved from\n87:   `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n88: - Current tree: all auth cards use `bg-c-bg-surface`; `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/`\n89:   leaves only decorative hits (`ui/icons/IconPlate.svelte`, `forms/Toggle.svelte`\n90:   knob, `todos/ScoreBar.svelte`, `todos/props/Progress.svelte`) — none on the\n91:   auth routes. `TimePicker.svelte:63` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\n92: - Nord (`static/themes/nord/nord.css`) maps `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252` and\n93:   `--color-c-neutral: #323a49`, so the current login page has no white surface\n94:   under Nord.\n95: \n96: No product code was changed in this pass. `node_modules` is still not installed,\n97: so no build/preview/`shot` render was possible (per the no-install hard rule).\n98: \n99: ## Worktree note\n100: \n101: An earlier, interrupted run of this job left uncommitted cosmetic edits on four\n102: auth pages (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`). They were\n103: reverted for the reasons in TASK-2 above so the worktree matches the\n104: already-fixed, committed state. The branch's only changes relative to `main` are\n105: the job's own docs (`git diff --name-only main...HEAD`).\n106: \n107: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n108: \n109: - Rendered verification (themes × default light/dark) still needs to be done\n110:   once dependencies and a backend are available. Nothing in the branch should\n111:   change rendering (it adds no product code relative to `main`).\n112: - Production is most likely running a build older than `70f6236`; deploying\n113:   current `main` (which this branch already contains) resolves the white card.\n114: - `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale: it describes the pre-merge\n115:   auth-card classes. It was left as the analyst's artifact; the corrected picture\n116:   is in `notes.md`.\n117: - Optional consistency follow-up (not in scope): auth-page headings/labels use a\n118:   bare `dark:text-white` while the rest of the app mostly uses\n119:   `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`. Aligning them would be a cosmetic change\n120:   that alters default light rendering.\n121: - Open follow-ups inherited from `tasks.md` (not in scope here): pre-paint theme\n122:   script (FOUC hardening), `html` background-color rule, account-synced theme\n123:   setting, `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`.\n\n(End of file - total 123 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation: theme on login\n\nid: create\nstatus: open\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nThe white surface on the login page under the Nord theme is caused by literal\nwhite utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) on the auth cards. Single-mode\nthemes never add the `.dark` class, so the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback\nnever fires and the card stays white (`--color-white` under Nord is the\nnear-white `#eceff4`). That exact fix was already delivered on `main` by commit\n`70f6236` (Job: `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) and reached this branch via the\n`main` merge (`8c0ad30`), so **no additional product code change was required**.\nThe tasks in `tasks.md` predate that merge and describe the pre-fix tree; the\ncorrected picture is documented in `notes.md`.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","text":"# Implementation: theme on login\n\nid: create\nstatus: open\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nThe white surface on the login page under the Nord theme is caused by literal\nwhite utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) on the auth cards. Single-mode\nthemes never add the `.dark` class, so the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback\nnever fires and the card stays white (`--color-white` under Nord is the\nnear-white `#eceff4`). That exact fix was already delivered on `main` by commit\n`70f6236` (Job: `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) and reached this branch via the\n`main` merge (`8c0ad30`), so **no additional product code change was required**.\nThe tasks in `tasks.md` predate that merge and describe the pre-fix tree; the\ncorrected picture is documented in `notes.md`.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: Captured the environment/code facts in\n  `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md`. Confirmed the code mechanism and\n  that the fix is an ancestor of `HEAD` (`git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236\n  HEAD`). The production-browser facts the task asks for (LocalStorage `theme`,\n  `documentElement.className`, computed card background, deployed version) cannot\n  be read by an unattended agent from another origin, so only local code/commit\n  facts were captured. No product code changed.\n\nTASK-2: No change needed for the primary fix — verified all six auth cards\n  already carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72/100,\n  reset-password:72/85/105, logout:27, verify:44), the exact swap the task asks\n  for. The two secondary substitutions were deliberately **not** applied:\n  - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: with the card now\n    themed, labels already inherit a correctly themed color from\n    `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` (`text-c-neutral-8` /\n    `dark:text-c-neutral-2`), so there is no washed-out-text bug. Adding an\n    explicit light-mode token would change default light rendering\n    (`--color-c-neutral-8` gray-800 → `--color-c-neutral-9` gray-900), which\n    TASK-2 explicitly requires to stay pixel-identical.\n  - `border-white/5` → token border: the same `border-2 border-white/5\n    bg-c-bg-surface` card pattern is also used by `/setup` (3 instances), so\n    changing only the auth cards would make them inconsistent; and the border is\n    decorative, so a swap would alter default rendering. No target token was\n    specified.\n\nTASK-3: No change needed — `src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte:63` already\n  uses `bg-c-bg-modal` (fixed by the same commit `70f6236`). This resolves the\n  task's open question.\n\nTASK-4: Static verification only. `node_modules` is not installed in this\n  environment, so `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, and build/preview\n  could not be run; per the project hard rule no packages were installed. No\n  dependency was available to install/substitute. `git diff --check` is clean and\n  the branch adds no product code relative to `main`, so there is no rendering\n  change introduced by this job to verify.\n\n## Re-verification (second developer pass, 2026-10-07)\n\nIndependently reconfirmed the above against the committed tree:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff --name-only\n  main...HEAD` lists only `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/*` (no product code).\n- All nine auth card blocks use `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92,\n  forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44).\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/` returns only six decorative hits, none on the auth\n  routes: `ui/icons/IconPlate.svelte` (×3) and `todos/ScoreBar.svelte` (×3).\n  `TimePicker.svelte:63` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\n- `static/themes/nord/nord.css:34` defines `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252`; the\n  Nord `--color-white: #eceff4` (line 48) is what made the old literal `bg-white`\n  cards near-white. `src/styles/tokens.css` / `default.css` confirm the token\n  maps to `#ffffff` (light default) and `s-dark-2` (dark default).\n- No dev server, `node_modules`, or `build/` is present, so no rendered\n  `shot`/`preview` verification was possible in this environment; only static\n  verification. No product change was made in either pass.\n\n## Final pass (third developer pass, 2026-10-07)\n\nRe-ran the verification from scratch and reached the same conclusion:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD` shows\n  only `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/*`.\n- `70f6236` touched exactly the six auth pages and `TimePicker.svelte`; e.g.\n  `src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte` moved from\n  `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n- Current tree: all auth cards use `bg-c-bg-surface`; `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/`\n  leaves only decorative hits (`ui/icons/IconPlate.svelte`, `forms/Toggle.svelte`\n  knob, `todos/ScoreBar.svelte`, `todos/props/Progress.svelte`) — none on the\n  auth routes. `TimePicker.svelte:63` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\n- Nord (`static/themes/nord/nord.css`) maps `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252` and\n  `--color-c-neutral: #323a49`, so the current login page has no white surface\n  under Nord.\n\nNo product code was changed in this pass. `node_modules` is still not installed,\nso no build/preview/`shot` render was possible (per the no-install hard rule).\n\n## Worktree note\n\nAn earlier, interrupted run of this job left uncommitted cosmetic edits on four\nauth pages (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`). They were\nreverted for the reasons in TASK-2 above so the worktree matches the\nalready-fixed, committed state. The branch's only changes relative to `main` are\nthe job's own docs (`git diff --name-only main...HEAD`).\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- Rendered verification (themes × default light/dark) still needs to be done\n  once dependencies and a backend are available. Nothing in the branch should\n  change rendering (it adds no product code relative to `main`).\n- Production is most likely running a build older than `70f6236`; deploying\n  current `main` (which this branch already contains) resolves the white card.\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale: it describes the pre-merge\n  auth-card classes. It was left as the analyst's artifact; the corrected picture\n  is in `notes.md`.\n- Optional consistency follow-up (not in scope): auth-page headings/labels use a\n  bare `dark:text-white` while the rest of the app mostly uses\n  `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`. Aligning them would be a cosmetic change\n  that alters default light rendering.\n- Open follow-ups inherited from `tasks.md` (not in scope here): pre-paint theme\n  script (FOUC hardening), `html` background-color rule, account-synced theme\n  setting, `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":123,"totalLines":123,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791394143920,"end":1791394144063}},"id":"prt_117695e61001H616BmoyxE5UbY","sessionID":"ses_ee896c4f