{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1791394427258,"sessionID":"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur","part":{"id":"prt_1176db14f001NwYeIw3hXfPYs4","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"","messageID":"msg_1176da48f0013sLBKaxK9gLvyJ","sessionID":"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":56351,"input":256,"output":69,"reasoning":218,"cache":{"write":0,"read":55808}},"cost":0.000378024}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791394428589,"sessionID":"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur","part":{"id":"prt_1176db6a9001ntp470sByGn7e1","messageID":"msg_1176db16d001H5Yn2WSbY57nnz","sessionID":"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1791394433056,"sessionID":"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur","part":{"id":"prt_1176dbedf001EnzuI8hOH82HGO","messageID":"msg_1176db16d001H5Yn2WSbY57nnz","sessionID":"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur","type":"text","text":"I've completed the job. Here's the summary.\n\n## Outcome\n\n**No product code change was required.** The white surface reported on the login page is the auth **card**, and that exact defect was already fixed in the repository before this job's branch.\n\n## What I verified independently (not just taken on trust)\n\n- **Branch check** — worktree is on `feature/create_theme_on_login`... precisely `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`. No checkout needed.\n- **Fix is present in the branch** — `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true. Commit `70f6236` (*\"nord theme bug with todos\"*) changed the six auth cards from `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n- **No literal white left on auth routes** — `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none. Remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative (icon plate, toggle knob, score bar, progress bar).\n- **Screenshot decoded objectively** — re-downloaded `iili.io/CZZtpwX.png` (973×989) and decoded the PNG by hand: 89.9% of pixels are the dark Nord page `#353d4a`, and the only light region is one central card `#ebeef4` = Nord's `--color-white`. So the report is the card, not the page body.\n- **Token mapping is render-safe** — `src/styles/tokens.css:24` sets `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff` (light default) and `src/styles/default.css:19` maps it to `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `.dark`, so the swap is pixel-identical in default light/dark and resolves to `#3b4252` under Nord.\n\n**Root cause:** literal `bg-white` + a `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback that never fires under single-mode themes (`ThemeState.apply()` removes the `dark` class for `supportsDarkMode: false`), leaving Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white`. The production symptom is therefore a **stale deploy older than `70f6236`**, not a defect in this branch — an operational step, not code.\n\n## Changes committed\n\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md` — added an \"Independent re-verification\" section recording the checks above.\n- Committed as `712975e [create] implementation: add summary`, plus a session-log commit.\n\n## Limitation\n\n`node_modules` is not installed, so `npm run check/lint/test` and a build+preview render pass could not be run — and per the project hard rule I did not install packages. Since the branch adds no product code relative to `main`, there is no rendering change from this job to verify. The worktree is clean.\n\nThe open item from `tasks.md` (TASK-3, TimePicker) is also already resolved: `TimePicker.svelte` now uses `bg-c-bg-modal` via the same commit.","time":{"start":1791394430687,"end":1791394433053}}}
