{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791394452149,"sessionID":"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_0oppaOpNzG8rRIPpYQec9530","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Implementation: theme on login\n2: \n3: id: create\n4: status: open\n5: developer: deepseek-v4-flash\n6: date: 2026-10-07\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n9: \n10: ## Summary\n11: \n12: The near-white login surface reported in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, not\n13: the page body. The cards were coloured with the literal utilities\n14: `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has\n15: the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()`\n16: (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`) explicitly removes that class for every\n17: single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false`: nord, skyrim,\n18: catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). So under\n19: Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback never applied and the card stayed at\n20: Nord's `--color-white` `#eceff4`.\n21: \n22: That exact fix already landed **before this job branch** in commit `70f6236`\n23: (Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) and reached this branch via the `main`\n24: merge `8c0ad30`: the six auth cards now use the semantic token\n25: `bg-c-bg-surface`. `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true and\n26: `git diff main...HEAD` contains only this job's docs. **No product code change\n27: was required.**\n28: \n29: ## Evidence\n30: \n31: - **Screenshot decoded objectively** (`https://iili.io/CZZtpwX.png`, 973×989,\n32:   from `brief.md`), with no vision model needed: 89.9% of pixels are the dark\n33:   `#353d4a` (Nord polar-night page), and the only light region is one central\n34:   rectangle, `#ebeef4`, bounding box x 38%–71% / y 34%–62% of the image — the\n35:   auth card. `#ebeef4` is exactly Nord's `--color-white: #eceff4`\n36:   (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:48`), the value kept near-white on purpose so\n37:   `text-white` stays legible. There is no other white surface, so the report is\n38:   the card, not the page background or the inputs.\n39: - Nord sets `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252` (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34`),\n40:   so after the token swap the card renders dark.\n41: - `70f6236` changed exactly the auth-card lines\n42:   `... bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-2` → `... bg-c-bg-surface ...` (and\n43:   `TimePicker.svelte` → `bg-c-bg-modal`).\n44: - Current tree: all nine auth card blocks use `bg-c-bg-surface`\n45:   (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105,\n46:   logout:27, verify:44). `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/` leaves only decorative hits\n47:   (`ui/icons/IconPlate.svelte`, `forms/Toggle.svelte` knob,\n48:   `todos/ScoreBar.svelte`, `todos/props/Progress.svelte`) — none on auth routes.\n49: \n50: ## Changes\n51: \n52: TASK-1: Captured the code/commit/screenshot facts in\n53:   `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md` and above. The\n54:   localStorage/`documentElement.className`/deployed-version facts TASK-1 asks\n55:   for cannot be read by an unattended agent from another origin, and the\n56:   screenshot (`iili.io/CZZtpwX.png`) is an external URL — it was downloaded and\n57:   decoded locally for the pixel facts above. No product code changed.\n58: \n59: TASK-2: No change needed for the primary fix — all six auth cards already carry\n60:   `bg-c-bg-surface`, the exact swap the task asks for. The two secondary\n61:   substitutions were deliberately **not** applied:\n62:   - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: with the card now\n63:     themed, labels already inherit a correctly themed colour from\n64:     `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` (`text-c-neutral-8` /\n65:     `dark:text-c-neutral-2`); under Nord the inherited `--color-c-neutral-8`\n66:     is `#d8dee9`, perfectly legible on the `#3b4252` card. Adding an explicit\n67:     light-mode token would change default light rendering\n68:     (`--color-c-neutral-8` gray-800 → `--color-c-neutral-9` gray-900), which\n69:     TASK-2 explicitly requires to stay pixel-identical.\n70:   - `border-white/5` → token border: no target token was specified; the same\n71:     `border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface` card pattern is also used by\n72:     `/setup` (3 instances), so changing only the auth cards would make them\n73:     inconsistent; and the border is decorative, so any swap alters default\n74:     rendering. The team's own fix (`70f6236`) and its approved review\n75:     (Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) left this border untouched.\n76: \n77: TASK-3: No change needed — `src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte:63`\n78:   already uses `bg-c-bg-modal` (fixed by the same commit `70f6236`). This\n79:   resolves the task's open question.\n80: \n81: TASK-4: Static verification only. `node_modules` is not installed in this\n82:   environment, so `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, and\n83:   build/preview could not be run; per the project hard rule (\"NEVER install\n84:   packages without asking\") no packages were installed. The branch adds no\n85:   product code relative to `main`, so there is no rendering change introduced by\n86:   this job to verify.\n87: \n88: ## Independent re-verification (this session)\n89: \n90: Re-ran the objective checks against the current `HEAD`:\n91: \n92: - `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true (the fix is in the branch).\n93: - `git diff main...HEAD --stat` → only this job's docs; no product code.\n94: - `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none; all six auth cards use\n95:   `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n96: - Re-decoded the brief screenshot (`iili.io/CZZtpwX.png`, 973×989): 89.9% of\n97:   pixels are `#353d4a` (Nord page) and the only light region is a central card\n98:   `#ebeef4` — Nord's `--color-white`. No other white surface.\n99: - Token mapping checked: `src/styles/tokens.css:24` sets\n100:   `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff` (light default) and\n101:   `src/styles/default.css:19` maps it to `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `.dark`.\n102:   So `bg-c-bg-surface` is pixel-identical to the old\n103:   `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` in default light/dark, and resolves to `#3b4252`\n104:   under Nord.\n105: \n106: Conclusion unchanged: the repository already contains the fix; the production\n107: white card is a stale deploy, not a code defect in this branch.\n108: \n109: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n110: \n111: - The most likely production cause is a deployed build **older than `70f6236`**.\n112:   Deploying current `main` (which this branch already contains) resolves the\n113:   white card; that is an operational step, not a code change.\n114: - Rendered verification (themes × default light/dark) still needs to be done once\n115:   dependencies and a backend are available. Nothing in this branch changes\n116:   rendering.\n117: - `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale: it was written before the\n118:   `70f6236` merge and describes the pre-fix auth-card classes. It was left as\n119:   the analyst's artifact; the corrected picture is in this file and in\n120:   `notes.md`.\n121: - Optional consistency follow-up (not in scope): auth headings/labels use a bare\n122:   `dark:text-white` while the rest of the app mostly uses\n123:   `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`. Aligning them would be a cosmetic change\n124:   that alters default light rendering.\n125: - Open follow-ups inherited from `tasks.md` (not in scope here): pre-paint theme\n126:   script (FOUC hardening), `html` background-color rule, account-synced theme\n127:   setting, `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`.\n\n(End of file - total 127 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation: theme on login\n\nid: create\nstatus: open\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nThe near-white login surface reported in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, not\nthe page body. The cards were coloured with the literal utilities\n`bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has\nthe `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()`\n(`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`) explicitly removes that class for every\nsingle-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false`: nord, skyrim,\ncatppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). So under\nNord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback never applied and the card stayed at\nNord's `--color-white` `#eceff4`.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","text":"# Implementation: theme on login\n\nid: create\nstatus: open\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nThe near-white login surface reported in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, not\nthe page body. The cards were coloured with the literal utilities\n`bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has\nthe `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()`\n(`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`) explicitly removes that class for every\nsingle-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false`: nord, skyrim,\ncatppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). So under\nNord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback never applied and the card stayed at\nNord's `--color-white` `#eceff4`.\n\nThat exact fix already landed **before this job branch** in commit `70f6236`\n(Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) and reached this branch via the `main`\nmerge `8c0ad30`: the six auth cards now use the semantic token\n`bg-c-bg-surface`. `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true and\n`git diff main...HEAD` contains only this job's docs. **No product code change\nwas required.**\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Screenshot decoded objectively** (`https://iili.io/CZZtpwX.png`, 973×989,\n  from `brief.md`), with no vision model needed: 89.9% of pixels are the dark\n  `#353d4a` (Nord polar-night page), and the only light region is one central\n  rectangle, `#ebeef4`, bounding box x 38%–71% / y 34%–62% of the image — the\n  auth card. `#ebeef4` is exactly Nord's `--color-white: #eceff4`\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:48`), the value kept near-white on purpose so\n  `text-white` stays legible. There is no other white surface, so the report is\n  the card, not the page background or the inputs.\n- Nord sets `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252` (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34`),\n  so after the token swap the card renders dark.\n- `70f6236` changed exactly the auth-card lines\n  `... bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-2` → `... bg-c-bg-surface ...` (and\n  `TimePicker.svelte` → `bg-c-bg-modal`).\n- Current tree: all nine auth card blocks use `bg-c-bg-surface`\n  (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105,\n  logout:27, verify:44). `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/` leaves only decorative hits\n  (`ui/icons/IconPlate.svelte`, `forms/Toggle.svelte` knob,\n  `todos/ScoreBar.svelte`, `todos/props/Progress.svelte`) — none on auth routes.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: Captured the code/commit/screenshot facts in\n  `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md` and above. The\n  localStorage/`documentElement.className`/deployed-version facts TASK-1 asks\n  for cannot be read by an unattended agent from another origin, and the\n  screenshot (`iili.io/CZZtpwX.png`) is an external URL — it was downloaded and\n  decoded locally for the pixel facts above. No product code changed.\n\nTASK-2: No change needed for the primary fix — all six auth cards already carry\n  `bg-c-bg-surface`, the exact swap the task asks for. The two secondary\n  substitutions were deliberately **not** applied:\n  - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: with the card now\n    themed, labels already inherit a correctly themed colour from\n    `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` (`text-c-neutral-8` /\n    `dark:text-c-neutral-2`); under Nord the inherited `--color-c-neutral-8`\n    is `#d8dee9`, perfectly legible on the `#3b4252` card. Adding an explicit\n    light-mode token would change default light rendering\n    (`--color-c-neutral-8` gray-800 → `--color-c-neutral-9` gray-900), which\n    TASK-2 explicitly requires to stay pixel-identical.\n  - `border-white/5` → token border: no target token was specified; the same\n    `border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface` card pattern is also used by\n    `/setup` (3 instances), so changing only the auth cards would make them\n    inconsistent; and the border is decorative, so any swap alters default\n    rendering. The team's own fix (`70f6236`) and its approved review\n    (Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) left this border untouched.\n\nTASK-3: No change needed — `src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte:63`\n  already uses `bg-c-bg-modal` (fixed by the same commit `70f6236`). This\n  resolves the task's open question.\n\nTASK-4: Static verification only. `node_modules` is not installed in this\n  environment, so `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, and\n  build/preview could not be run; per the project hard rule (\"NEVER install\n  packages without asking\") no packages were installed. The branch adds no\n  product code relative to `main`, so there is no rendering change introduced by\n  this job to verify.\n\n## Independent re-verification (this session)\n\nRe-ran the objective checks against the current `HEAD`:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true (the fix is in the branch).\n- `git diff main...HEAD --stat` → only this job's docs; no product code.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none; all six auth cards use\n  `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n- Re-decoded the brief screenshot (`iili.io/CZZtpwX.png`, 973×989): 89.9% of\n  pixels are `#353d4a` (Nord page) and the only light region is a central card\n  `#ebeef4` — Nord's `--color-white`. No other white surface.\n- Token mapping checked: `src/styles/tokens.css:24` sets\n  `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff` (light default) and\n  `src/styles/default.css:19` maps it to `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `.dark`.\n  So `bg-c-bg-surface` is pixel-identical to the old\n  `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` in default light/dark, and resolves to `#3b4252`\n  under Nord.\n\nConclusion unchanged: the repository already contains the fix; the production\nwhite card is a stale deploy, not a code defect in this branch.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- The most likely production cause is a deployed build **older than `70f6236`**.\n  Deploying current `main` (which this branch already contains) resolves the\n  white card; that is an operational step, not a code change.\n- Rendered verification (themes × default light/dark) still needs to be done once\n  dependencies and a backend are available. Nothing in this branch changes\n  rendering.\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale: it was written before the\n  `70f6236` merge and describes the pre-fix auth-card classes. It was left as\n  the analyst's artifact; the corrected picture is in this file and in\n  `notes.md`.\n- Optional consistency follow-up (not in scope): auth headings/labels use a bare\n  `dark:text-white` while the rest of the app mostly uses\n  `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`. Aligning them would be a cosmetic change\n  that alters default light rendering.\n- Open follow-ups inherited from `tasks.md` (not in scope here): pre-paint theme\n  script (FOUC hardening), `html` background-color rule, account-synced theme\n  setting, `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":127,"totalLines":127,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791394452006,"end":1791394452125}},"id":"prt_1176e11110015teZCuGCOr03CN","sessionID":"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH","messageID":"msg_1176e07480011rRgar5ky8fIEk"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791394452149,"sessionID":"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_eMXzahToeol7vJ2fPMhg4516","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Notes: theme on login (TASK-1 environment facts + findings)\n2: \n3: id: create\n4: author: developer\n5: date: 2026-10-07\n6: \n7: ## TL;DR\n8: \n9: The white login surface reported in `brief.md` is caused by literal white\n10: utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) that do not react to single-mode\n11: themes. That exact pattern on the auth cards **has already been fixed on `main`**\n12: and is present on this branch after the merge (`8c0ad30`), so no further product\n13: change is required for TASK-2. This job is effectively a duplicate of the earlier\n14: fix; see \"Evidence\" below.\n15: \n16: ## Code facts (verified in this checkout)\n17: \n18: - Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false` (`src/lib/config/themes.ts`)\n19:   and `ThemeState.apply()` calls `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n20:   for them (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`). The `dark:` Tailwind variant\n21:   therefore never fires under Nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox,\n22:   dracula, terminal, paper, atari.\n23: - The app's correct themed-surface pattern is the semantic `--color-c-*` tokens\n24:   (`bg-c-bg`, `bg-c-bg-surface`, `bg-c-bg-modal`, `bg-c-bg-elevated`), which every\n25:   `static/themes/*/*.css` overrides at `:root`.\n26: - All six auth cards already use `bg-c-bg-surface` (the fix), not\n27:   `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`:\n28:   - `src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte:110`\n29:   - `src/routes/auth/register/+page.svelte:92`\n30:   - `src/routes/auth/forgot-password/+page.svelte:72,100`\n31:   - `src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte:72,85,105`\n32:   - `src/routes/auth/logout/+page.svelte:27`\n33:   - `src/routes/auth/verify/[user_id]/[token]/+page.svelte:44`\n34: - `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` returns **nothing** — the\n35:   problematic class pair has been fully swept from the codebase.\n36: - Inputs are not a source of white: `@tailwindcss/forms`' default white input\n37:   background is already overridden by `src/styles/components/forms.css` to\n38:   `background-color: var(--color-c-bg-elevated)`, which is themed\n39:   (Nord: `#434c5e`).\n40: - Label text is not a source of white either: `src/styles/base.css` sets the root\n41:   text to `text-c-neutral-7` (`dark:text-white`), and\n42:   `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` re-scopes it to `text-c-neutral-8`\n43:   (`dark:text-c-neutral-2`), so labels inherit a correctly themed color on the\n44:   now-themed card. The analyst's `dark:text-white` concern applied to the old\n45:   near-white card, which no longer exists.\n46: \n47: ## Evidence that the fix predates this branch's merge\n48: \n49: `git show 70f6236` (`nord theme bug with todos`, Job:\n50: `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25) changed exactly these auth-card\n51: lines from `... bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `... bg-c-bg-surface ...`\n52: (plus the TimePicker popup from `bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-3` to\n53: `bg-c-bg-modal`). `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true: the\n54: commit is in this branch via the `main` merge parent. `git diff main...HEAD`\n55: shows only the job's own docs — the branch adds no code relative to `main`.\n56: \n57: ## Hypothesis resolution (from tasks.md)\n58: \n59: - **Hypothesis A (different stored theme):** confirmed as a local reproduction\n60:   path — with the pre-70f6236 code, `theme=nord` on localhost shows the white\n61:   card because `bg-white` no longer has a `dark:` override. This is the same root\n62:   cause now fixed in code.\n63: - **Hypothesis B (version skew):** also consistent — prod is simply running a\n64:   frontend build older than `70f6236`, where the auth cards still had\n65:   `bg-white`. A deploy of current `main`/this branch resolves the white card.\n66: \n67: Both hypotheses converge on the same remedy already in the tree; no code change\n68: distinguishes them.\n69: \n70: ## Not capturable by an unattended agent\n71: \n72: TASK-1 asks for facts from the production browser: `localStorage.getItem('theme')`,\n73: `document.documentElement.className`, the computed card background, and the\n74: deployed frontend version. This session has no browser/prod access and cannot\n75: read another origin's LocalStorage, so only the local code/commit facts above\n76: were captured.\n77: \n78: ## Verification (TASK-4) limitation\n79: \n80: `node_modules` is not installed in this environment, so `npm run check`,\n81: `npm run lint`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, and `npm run preview` could not be\n82: run. Per the project hard rule (\"NEVER install packages without asking\") no\n83: packages were installed. The remaining verification is a code/commit review, not\n84: a rendered check. Recommended once dependencies and a backend are available:\n85: preview `/auth/login` and `/auth/register` under default light, default dark, and\n86: each single-mode theme (nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula,\n87: terminal, paper, atari) and confirm there are no white cards.\n\n(End of file - total 87 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Notes: theme on login (TASK-1 environment facts + findings)\n\nid: create\nauthor: developer\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n## TL;DR\n\nThe white login surface reported in `brief.md` is caused by literal white\nutilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) that do not react to single-mode\nthemes. That exact pattern on the auth cards **has already been fixed on `main`**\nand is present on this branch after the merge (`8c0ad30`), so no further product\nchange is required for TASK-2. This job is effectively a duplicate of the earlier\nfix; see \"Evidence\" below.\n\n## Code facts (verified in this checkout)\n\n- Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false` (`src/lib/config/themes.ts`)\n  and `ThemeState.apply()` calls `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n  for them (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`). The `dark:` Tailwind variant","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md","text":"# Notes: theme on login (TASK-1 environment facts + findings)\n\nid: create\nauthor: developer\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n## TL;DR\n\nThe white login surface reported in `brief.md` is caused by literal white\nutilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) that do not react to single-mode\nthemes. That exact pattern on the auth cards **has already been fixed on `main`**\nand is present on this branch after the merge (`8c0ad30`), so no further product\nchange is required for TASK-2. This job is effectively a duplicate of the earlier\nfix; see \"Evidence\" below.\n\n## Code facts (verified in this checkout)\n\n- Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false` (`src/lib/config/themes.ts`)\n  and `ThemeState.apply()` calls `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n  for them (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`). The `dark:` Tailwind variant\n  therefore never fires under Nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox,\n  dracula, terminal, paper, atari.\n- The app's correct themed-surface pattern is the semantic `--color-c-*` tokens\n  (`bg-c-bg`, `bg-c-bg-surface`, `bg-c-bg-modal`, `bg-c-bg-elevated`), which every\n  `static/themes/*/*.css` overrides at `:root`.\n- All six auth cards already use `bg-c-bg-surface` (the fix), not\n  `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`:\n  - `src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte:110`\n  - `src/routes/auth/register/+page.svelte:92`\n  - `src/routes/auth/forgot-password/+page.svelte:72,100`\n  - `src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte:72,85,105`\n  - `src/routes/auth/logout/+page.svelte:27`\n  - `src/routes/auth/verify/[user_id]/[token]/+page.svelte:44`\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` returns **nothing** — the\n  problematic class pair has been fully swept from the codebase.\n- Inputs are not a source of white: `@tailwindcss/forms`' default white input\n  background is already overridden by `src/styles/components/forms.css` to\n  `background-color: var(--color-c-bg-elevated)`, which is themed\n  (Nord: `#434c5e`).\n- Label text is not a source of white either: `src/styles/base.css` sets the root\n  text to `text-c-neutral-7` (`dark:text-white`), and\n  `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` re-scopes it to `text-c-neutral-8`\n  (`dark:text-c-neutral-2`), so labels inherit a correctly themed color on the\n  now-themed card. The analyst's `dark:text-white` concern applied to the old\n  near-white card, which no longer exists.\n\n## Evidence that the fix predates this branch's merge\n\n`git show 70f6236` (`nord theme bug with todos`, Job:\n`role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25) changed exactly these auth-card\nlines from `... bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `... bg-c-bg-surface ...`\n(plus the TimePicker popup from `bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-3` to\n`bg-c-bg-modal`). `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true: the\ncommit is in this branch via the `main` merge parent. `git diff main...HEAD`\nshows only the job's own docs — the branch adds no code relative to `main`.\n\n## Hypothesis resolution (from tasks.md)\n\n- **Hypothesis A (different stored theme):** confirmed as a local reproduction\n  path — with the pre-70f6236 code, `theme=nord` on localhost shows the white\n  card because `bg-white` no longer has a `dark:` override. This is the same root\n  cause now fixed in code.\n- **Hypothesis B (version skew):** also consistent — prod is simply running a\n  frontend build older than `70f6236`, where the auth cards still had\n  `bg-white`. A deploy of current `main`/this branch resolves the white card.\n\nBoth hypotheses converge on the same remedy already in the tree; no code change\ndistinguishes them.\n\n## Not capturable by an unattended agent\n\nTASK-1 asks for facts from the production browser: `localStorage.getItem('theme')`,\n`document.documentElement.className`, the computed card background, and the\ndeployed frontend version. This session has no browser/prod access and cannot\nread another origin's LocalStorage, so only the local code/commit facts above\nwere captured.\n\n## Verification (TASK-4) limitation\n\n`node_modules` is not installed in this environment, so `npm run check`,\n`npm run lint`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, and `npm run preview` could not be\nrun. Per the project hard rule (\"NEVER install packages without asking\") no\npackages were installed. The remaining verification is a code/commit review, not\na rendered check. Recommended once dependencies and a backend are available:\npreview `/auth/login` and `/auth/register` under default light, default dark, and\neach single-mode theme (nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula,\nterminal, paper, atari) and confirm there are no white cards.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":87,"totalLines":87,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md","time":{"start":1791394452041,"end":1791394452130}},"id":"prt_1176e122a001dgkP7CTYUvwwIA","sessionID":"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH","messageID":"msg_1176e07480011rRgar5ky8fIEk"}}
