{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791394615356,"sessionID":"ses_ee88fe25bffe2xhvlL8jpyAcF9","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_y7ibzcoHXUpq6MDWrrAb2266","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -o '\"type\":\"text\"[^}]*' /workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log | tail -20"},"output":"\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394067121,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee8992534ffeRsL1e6F5QzjEOp\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_117682a0c0010uQEhnANzI5siq\",\"messageID\":\"msg_117681ac0001sv26NZjgEf0UvZ\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee8992534ffeRsL1e6F5QzjEOp\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Work complete. Here's the summary of this session.\\n\\n## Outcome\\n\\nThe job's product fix was **already present on `main`** (commit `70f6236`, \\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\") and reached this branch via the `main` merge (`8c0ad30`). This branch's diff against `main` is docs-only — no additional product code change is required.\\n\\n**Root cause (confirmed):** auth cards used literal white utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`). Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false`, so `ThemeState.apply()` never adds `.dark` and the themed fallback never fires — leaving the card at `--color-white`, which Nord deliberately keeps near-white (`#eceff4`) so `text-white` stays legible. That's the white surface in the production screenshot.\\n\\n**Fix (already in tree):** all nine auth card blocks now use the semantic token `bg-c-bg-surface` (→ `#fff` light default, `s-dark-2` dark default, `#3b4252` Nord), and `TimePicker` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\\n\\n## What I did this pass\\n\\n- Independently re-verified the committed tree: `70f6236` is an ancestor of `HEAD`; `git diff main...HEAD` is docs-only; all auth cards use `bg-c-bg-surface`; `grep bg-white src/` leaves only six decorative, non-auth hits (IconPlate ×3, ScoreBar ×3); Nord token values confirmed.\\n- The two secondary `tasks.md` swaps were deliberately not applied — labels already inherit a themed color (`text-c-neutral-8`/Nord `#d8dee9`) and adding `text-c-neutral-9` would change default light rendering, violating the \\\"pixel-identical\\\" requirement.\\n- Recorded a re-verification section in `implementation.md` and committed the leftover harness artifacts (`session.log`, `tokens.json`) so the worktree is clean.\\n\\n## Verification limits\\n\\nNo `node_modules`, dev server, or `build/` exists in this environment, and installing packages is against project rules, so `npm run check/lint/test`, build/preview, and `shot` rendering were not possible. Verification was static (grep/git/token inspection). Nothing in the branch changes rendering relative to `main`.\\n\\nAll changes are committed (`1b6777e`); worktree is clean. No `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT` required.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394064908,\"end\":1791394067113\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394076744,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_117685659001bsQmzOQjeeM3hO\",\"messageID\":\"msg_117684fab0015OTV4ARXCg9ZFc\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The branch matches. There's prior work — let me review it before doing anything.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394076249,\"end\":1791394076740\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394081907,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_11768691d001Q1I6qQZelmcZGK\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176858b0001HvbmkWM6KhOAvc\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me independently verify the prior findings rather than trust them.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394081053,\"end\":1791394081902\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394085948,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_117687af0001hEmQZXEPo7QsvF\",\"messageID\":\"msg_117686cb5001i0rlN2Q83kubrk\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Prior findings verified. Let me look at the actual auth layout/pages to check for any remaining white-surface mechanism the prior analysis may have missed.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394085616,\"end\":1791394085945\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394099468,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_11768ade0001fDRVpeGHuNpnnn\",\"messageID\":\"msg_11768947b001VeWN4L4Vdtkh30\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me check the theme token definitions — the brief says \\\"white background\\\" which could be the page, not just the card.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394098657,\"end\":1791394099464\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394105350,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_11768c5d7001SEHA0ttW5tHuJA\",\"messageID\":\"msg_11768b14a001QcxmHP7Mka9hdx\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me confirm the earlier fix actually touched the auth cards (not something incidental).\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394104792,\"end\":1791394105346\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394121785,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_11768fef1001u6iBYbDB7CB71T\",\"messageID\":\"msg_11768c848001JTOD2YquG5792Y\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The prior analysis is fully verified:\\n\\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true.\\n- `70f6236` (\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\", 2026-08-25) changed exactly the auth cards from `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` → `bg-c-bg-surface`, plus `TimePicker` → `bg-c-bg-modal`.\\n- All nine auth card blocks now use `bg-c-bg-surface`; no `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains anywhere.\\n- `git diff main...HEAD` contains only this job's docs — the branch adds no product code.\\n- Nord defines all `--color-c-*` tokens to dark values (`--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252`), so with current code the login page and card are correctly dark.\\n\\nSo TASK-2/TASK-3 are already satisfied by an earlier fix, and there is no product change to make. I'll finalize the job: document this independent pass, commit the pending harness artifacts, and leave the worktree clean.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394119409,\"end\":1791394121781\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394131239,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_11769247d001fKqNN3Peb7ARCx\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176911870010Ehy0M1Rfk4TJc\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Done. Worktree is clean and the job is finalized.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n**Branch check:** `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches `brief.md` (`branch: feature/create_theme-on-login`). ✅\\n\\n**Finding (verified independently):** The white surface on the Nord login page came from literal white utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) on the auth cards. Single-mode themes (`supportsDarkMode: false`, e.g. Nord) never add the `.dark` class, so the themed `dark:` fallback never fired and the card stayed `--color-white` (`#eceff4` under Nord) — a stable near-white card on an otherwise-Nord page. That is exactly the report in `brief.md`.\\n\\n**Why no product code change was needed:** The fix already exists in `main` as commit `70f6236` (\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\", 2026-08-25), which changed precisely these auth cards from `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` (and `TimePicker` to `bg-c-bg-modal`). That commit is an ancestor of this branch (arrived via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`), and `git diff main...HEAD` shows **only this job's docs** — the branch adds no product code.\\n\\nVerification performed this pass:\\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD` → docs only.\\n- All nine auth card blocks use `bg-c-bg-surface`; no `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains anywhere.\\n- Remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative only (logo plates, toggle knob, score/progress bars), none on auth routes.\\n- Nord maps `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252` / `--color-c-neutral: #323a49`, so the current login page renders correctly dark.\\n\\n**Changes committed:** updated `implementation.md` with a final verification pass, and committed the pending harness artifacts (`session.log`, `tokens.json`). Commit `f0a61ab`.\\n\\n**Known limitations / follow-ups:** The prod-browser facts TASK-1 asked for (other-origin LocalStorage, deployed version) can't be read by an unattended agent; `node_modules` is absent, so no build/preview/`shot` render was possible and no packages were installed (project hard rule). The most likely production cause is simply an older deployed frontend build predating `70f6236`; deploying current `main` (which this branch already contains) resolves the white card. No `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT` condition.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394129021,\"end\":1791394131235\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394144076,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_117695d02001gfXmmxIGwKLM2L\",\"messageID\":\"msg_11769541b001bxlTd2OFDXDbv9\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Branch matches the brief. Let me read the task files and existing progress.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394143490,\"end\":1791394144068\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394148977,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_11769705c001qlkrWQUiruxaQH\",\"messageID\":\"msg_11769601d001G59q3oG2yQ6V44\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"This job has prior work. Let me independently verify the state before deciding what remains.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394148444,\"end\":1791394148967\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394172359,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_11769cb7a001WPAATqMnqKv5ko\",\"messageID\":\"msg_11769ada3001I7spFhQzP2HSRc\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The core card fix predates this job, but TASK-2 also asks for label/border token changes that are still present. Let me investigate whether those are real remaining bugs under single-mode themes.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394171770,\"end\":1791394172355\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394257754,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176b1a61001jlJU5aPB9F1uUi\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176b0ba2001dEKwxIKO4aO2b5\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me look at the actual reported screenshot to be certain about the bug.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394257505,\"end\":1791394257748\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394298329,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176bb198001QhiwJmYCYSHxhw\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176b85a9001rggdnkZWSTUZw8\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I can now objectively decode the screenshot without vision. Let me get precise color statistics.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394296216,\"end\":1791394298327\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394309245,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176bce36001WEOEKgFa5X9cHE\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176bc226001NMutt9jHRaKy6D\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Definitive evidence: the screenshot is 89.9% dark `#353d4a` (Nord page) with a central card of `#ebeef4` — exactly Nord's `--color-white` (`#eceff4`). This confirms the bug is the auth card, already fixed by `bg-c-bg-surface`. Let me finalize the job documentation.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394303542,\"end\":1791394309226\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394321299,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176c097f001Ng62GmOeDAS6L1\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176bf7300019JWLC83XrISh2s\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Worktree is clean and the job is finalized. Here's the summary.\\n\\n## Result\\n\\n**Branch:** `feature/create_theme-on-login` — matches `brief.md` (`branch: feature/create_theme-on-login`). ✅\\n\\n**Root cause (confirmed):** The white surface on the Nord login page is the auth **card**, not the page body. The cards used literal `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`; the `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `.dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` removes it for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false`). So under Nord the fallback never applied and the card stayed at Nord's `--color-white: #eceff4` — a stable near-white card on an otherwise dark page.\\n\\n**Objective screenshot evidence (no vision needed):** I downloaded the report image from `brief.md` and decoded the PNG pixels directly:\\n- 89.9% of pixels are dark `#353d4a` (Nord polar-night page).\\n- The only light region is one central rectangle, `#ebeef4`, at x 38–71% / y 34–62% — the auth card, and `#ebeef4` is exactly Nord's `--color-white: #eceff4`.\\n- No other white surface exists, so the page background and inputs were never the problem.\\n\\n**Why no product code change was needed:** That exact fix already landed on `main` as commit `70f6236` (Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) and reached this branch through the `main` merge `8c0ad30`. All nine auth card blocks now use the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token (Nord: `#3b4252`). `git diff main...HEAD` contains only this job's docs; the fix is an ancestor of `HEAD`.\\n\\n**Deliberately not applied** (TASK-2 secondary items): the `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 …` swap (labels already inherit a correct themed colour from `auth/+layout.svelte`, and the swap changes default light rendering, violating the task's “pixel-identical” constraint) and the unspecified `border-white/5` token swap (no target token, `/setup` uses the same pattern, decorative). The team's own fix and its approved review left these untouched.\\n\\n**TASK-3:** already resolved — `TimePicker.svelte:63` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\\n\\n**TASK-4:** static verification only; `node_modules` is not installed and packages must not be installed without approval, so `check`/`lint`/`test`/build could not run — but the branch adds no product code, so there is no rendering change to verify.\\n\\n**Likely production remedy:** prod is running a build older than `70f6236`; deploying current `main` (already contained in this branch) removes the white card. That is an operational deploy step, not a code change.\\n\\nCommitted as `2105e1c`; worktree is clean. Updated `implementation.md` with the condensed summary, the new screenshot-derived evidence, and the follow-ups. No product source was modified.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394318719,\"end\":1791394321287\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394416040,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176d848b001r094Jtgu5SvlPl\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176d718a001t1JqfneInDZYQA\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I've independently confirmed the prior analysis. Let me record the re-verification in the implementation summary.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394415755,\"end\":1791394416029\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394433056,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176dbedf001EnzuI8hOH82HGO\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176db16d001H5Yn2WSbY57nnz\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I've completed the job. Here's the summary.\\n\\n## Outcome\\n\\n**No product code change was required.** The white surface reported on the login page is the auth **card**, and that exact defect was already fixed in the repository before this job's branch.\\n\\n## What I verified independently (not just taken on trust)\\n\\n- **Branch check** — worktree is on `feature/create_theme_on_login`... precisely `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`. No checkout needed.\\n- **Fix is present in the branch** — `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true. Commit `70f6236` (*\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\"*) changed the six auth cards from `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\\n- **No literal white left on auth routes** — `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none. Remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative (icon plate, toggle knob, score bar, progress bar).\\n- **Screenshot decoded objectively** — re-downloaded `iili.io/CZZtpwX.png` (973×989) and decoded the PNG by hand: 89.9% of pixels are the dark Nord page `#353d4a`, and the only light region is one central card `#ebeef4` = Nord's `--color-white`. So the report is the card, not the page body.\\n- **Token mapping is render-safe** — `src/styles/tokens.css:24` sets `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff` (light default) and `src/styles/default.css:19` maps it to `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `.dark`, so the swap is pixel-identical in default light/dark and resolves to `#3b4252` under Nord.\\n\\n**Root cause:** literal `bg-white` + a `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback that never fires under single-mode themes (`ThemeState.apply()` removes the `dark` class for `supportsDarkMode: false`), leaving Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white`. The production symptom is therefore a **stale deploy older than `70f6236`**, not a defect in this branch — an operational step, not code.\\n\\n## Changes committed\\n\\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md` — added an \\\"Independent re-verification\\\" section recording the checks above.\\n- Committed as `712975e [create] implementation: add summary`, plus a session-log commit.\\n\\n## Limitation\\n\\n`node_modules` is not installed, so `npm run check/lint/test` and a build+preview render pass could not be run — and per the project hard rule I did not install packages. Since the branch adds no product code relative to `main`, there is no rendering change from this job to verify. The worktree is clean.\\n\\nThe open item from `tasks.md` (TASK-3, TimePicker) is also already resolved: `TimePicker.svelte` now uses `bg-c-bg-modal` via the same commit.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394430687,\"end\":1791394433053\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394562710,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176fc0e8001Z7ZEGi79UoEC9V\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176fb3a10014i0HaYjNQEux07\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I've independently verified the situation. Let me summarize my findings before finalizing.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394562280,\"end\":1791394562708\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394566660,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176fcb80001r5m63R0X1ZqzO7\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176fc2ed001QochHQnnG8BvvR\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The situation is now fully clear. Let me record the final verification and finish cleanly.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394564992,\"end\":1791394566658\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394582239,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1177004310013Kwas1YOVzD3dO\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176ff921001G61juMixF26mxB\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Done. Here's what I found and did.\\n\\n## Result: no product-code change was required — the fix is already in this branch\\n\\n**Branch check:** on `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`. ✅\\n\\n### Root cause\\nThe white surface in the screenshot is the **auth card**, not the page. The cards used literal utilities `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`) removes that class for every single-mode theme (Nord, Skyrim, Catppuccin ×2, Gruvbox, Dracula, Terminal, Paper, Atari). So under Nord the `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback never applied, and `bg-white` resolved to Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`.\\n\\n### Why nothing needed changing\\nThat exact fix already landed on `main` in commit **`70f6236`** (\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\", 2026-08-25) and reached this branch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`. `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true, and `git show 22c5a68:src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte` already shows `bg-c-bg-surface` — i.e. the fix is inherited, not introduced here. All six auth cards now use the semantic token `bg-c-bg-surface`, which is pixel-identical in default light/dark and resolves to Nord `#3b4252`. The production white card is therefore a **stale deploy**, not a code defect.\\n\\n### Independent verification\\n- Decoded the brief screenshot (`iili.io/CZZtpwX.png`, 973×989) with a standalone PNG reader (no vision model): 89.9% `#353d4a` page; light pixels only 6.15%, bbox x 38.4–71.2% / y 34.3–62.5%, colour `#ebeef4` (Nord's `--color-white`); inputs already themed `#454d5e`. The card is the only unthemed surface — and it's fixed.\\n- `grep` confirms no `bg-white` remains on auth routes and no `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair exists anywhere under `src/`.\\n- TASK-3 (`TimePicker.svelte`) was fixed by the same commit (`bg-c-bg-modal`).\\n- I deliberately did **not** apply TASK-2's two secondary substitutions (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9…`, `border-white/5` → token border): the team's own reviewed fix left both in place (they're decorative/inherited), and changing them would alter default-light rendering, violating TASK-2's pixel-identity constraint.\\n\\n### Commits\\n- `0a60b6e` — finalization notes in `implementation.md` + worktree cleanup. Working tree is clean.\\n\\n### Follow-ups (not in scope)\\nDeploy current `main` to production (operational). Inherited open items: pre-paint theme script (FOUC hardening), `html` background rule, account-synced theme, and `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`. Rendered `shot` verification was not possible — `node_modules` is absent and installing packages is against the project's hard rule.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394579505,\"end\":1791394582236\n","metadata":{"output":"\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394067121,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee8992534ffeRsL1e6F5QzjEOp\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_117682a0c0010uQEhnANzI5siq\",\"messageID\":\"msg_117681ac0001sv26NZjgEf0UvZ\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee8992534ffeRsL1e6F5QzjEOp\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Work complete. Here's the summary of this session.\\n\\n## Outcome\\n\\nThe job's product fix was **already present on `main`** (commit `70f6236`, \\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\") and reached this branch via the `main` merge (`8c0ad30`). This branch's diff against `main` is docs-only — no additional product code change is required.\\n\\n**Root cause (confirmed):** auth cards used literal white utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`). Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false`, so `ThemeState.apply()` never adds `.dark` and the themed fallback never fires — leaving the card at `--color-white`, which Nord deliberately keeps near-white (`#eceff4`) so `text-white` stays legible. That's the white surface in the production screenshot.\\n\\n**Fix (already in tree):** all nine auth card blocks now use the semantic token `bg-c-bg-surface` (→ `#fff` light default, `s-dark-2` dark default, `#3b4252` Nord), and `TimePicker` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\\n\\n## What I did this pass\\n\\n- Independently re-verified the committed tree: `70f6236` is an ancestor of `HEAD`; `git diff main...HEAD` is docs-only; all auth cards use `bg-c-bg-surface`; `grep bg-white src/` leaves only six decorative, non-auth hits (IconPlate ×3, ScoreBar ×3); Nord token values confirmed.\\n- The two secondary `tasks.md` swaps were deliberately not applied — labels already inherit a themed color (`text-c-neutral-8`/Nord `#d8dee9`) and adding `text-c-neutral-9` would change default light rendering, violating the \\\"pixel-identical\\\" requirement.\\n- Recorded a re-verification section in `implementation.md` and committed the leftover harness artifacts (`session.log`, `tokens.json`) so the worktree is clean.\\n\\n## Verification limits\\n\\nNo `node_modules`, dev server, or `build/` exists in this environment, and installing packages is against project rules, so `npm run check/lint/test`, build/preview, and `shot` rendering were not possible. Verification was static (grep/git/token inspection). Nothing in the branch changes rendering relative to `main`.\\n\\nAll changes are committed (`1b6777e`); worktree is clean. No `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT` required.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394064908,\"end\":1791394067113\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394076744,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_117685659001bsQmzOQjeeM3hO\",\"messageID\":\"msg_117684fab0015OTV4ARXCg9ZFc\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The branch matches. There's prior work — let me review it before doing anything.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394076249,\"end\":1791394076740\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394081907,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_11768691d001Q1I6qQZelmcZGK\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176858b0001HvbmkWM6KhOAvc\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me independently verify the prior findings rather than trust them.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394081053,\"end\":1791394081902\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394085948,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_117687af0001hEmQZXEPo7QsvF\",\"messageID\":\"msg_117686cb5001i0rlN2Q83kubrk\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Prior findings verified. Let me look at the actual auth layout/pages to check for any remaining white-surface mechanism the prior analysis may have missed.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394085616,\"end\":1791394085945\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394099468,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_11768ade0001fDRVpeGHuNpnnn\",\"messageID\":\"msg_11768947b001VeWN4L4Vdtkh30\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me check the theme token definitions — the brief says \\\"white background\\\" which could be the page, not just the card.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394098657,\"end\":1791394099464\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394105350,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_11768c5d7001SEHA0ttW5tHuJA\",\"messageID\":\"msg_11768b14a001QcxmHP7Mka9hdx\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me confirm the earlier fix actually touched the auth cards (not something incidental).\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394104792,\"end\":1791394105346\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394121785,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_11768fef1001u6iBYbDB7CB71T\",\"messageID\":\"msg_11768c848001JTOD2YquG5792Y\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The prior analysis is fully verified:\\n\\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true.\\n- `70f6236` (\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\", 2026-08-25) changed exactly the auth cards from `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` → `bg-c-bg-surface`, plus `TimePicker` → `bg-c-bg-modal`.\\n- All nine auth card blocks now use `bg-c-bg-surface`; no `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains anywhere.\\n- `git diff main...HEAD` contains only this job's docs — the branch adds no product code.\\n- Nord defines all `--color-c-*` tokens to dark values (`--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252`), so with current code the login page and card are correctly dark.\\n\\nSo TASK-2/TASK-3 are already satisfied by an earlier fix, and there is no product change to make. I'll finalize the job: document this independent pass, commit the pending harness artifacts, and leave the worktree clean.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394119409,\"end\":1791394121781\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394131239,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_11769247d001fKqNN3Peb7ARCx\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176911870010Ehy0M1Rfk4TJc\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Done. Worktree is clean and the job is finalized.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n**Branch check:** `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches `brief.md` (`branch: feature/create_theme-on-login`). ✅\\n\\n**Finding (verified independently):** The white surface on the Nord login page came from literal white utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) on the auth cards. Single-mode themes (`supportsDarkMode: false`, e.g. Nord) never add the `.dark` class, so the themed `dark:` fallback never fired and the card stayed `--color-white` (`#eceff4` under Nord) — a stable near-white card on an otherwise-Nord page. That is exactly the report in `brief.md`.\\n\\n**Why no product code change was needed:** The fix already exists in `main` as commit `70f6236` (\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\", 2026-08-25), which changed precisely these auth cards from `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` (and `TimePicker` to `bg-c-bg-modal`). That commit is an ancestor of this branch (arrived via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`), and `git diff main...HEAD` shows **only this job's docs** — the branch adds no product code.\\n\\nVerification performed this pass:\\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD` → docs only.\\n- All nine auth card blocks use `bg-c-bg-surface`; no `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains anywhere.\\n- Remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative only (logo plates, toggle knob, score/progress bars), none on auth routes.\\n- Nord maps `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252` / `--color-c-neutral: #323a49`, so the current login page renders correctly dark.\\n\\n**Changes committed:** updated `implementation.md` with a final verification pass, and committed the pending harness artifacts (`session.log`, `tokens.json`). Commit `f0a61ab`.\\n\\n**Known limitations / follow-ups:** The prod-browser facts TASK-1 asked for (other-origin LocalStorage, deployed version) can't be read by an unattended agent; `node_modules` is absent, so no build/preview/`shot` render was possible and no packages were installed (project hard rule). The most likely production cause is simply an older deployed frontend build predating `70f6236`; deploying current `main` (which this branch already contains) resolves the white card. No `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT` condition.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394129021,\"end\":1791394131235\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394144076,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_117695d02001gfXmmxIGwKLM2L\",\"messageID\":\"msg_11769541b001bxlTd2OFDXDbv9\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Branch matches the brief. Let me read the task files and existing progress.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394143490,\"end\":1791394144068\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394148977,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_11769705c001qlkrWQUiruxaQH\",\"messageID\":\"msg_11769601d001G59q3oG2yQ6V44\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"This job has prior work. Let me independently verify the state before deciding what remains.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394148444,\"end\":1791394148967\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394172359,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_11769cb7a001WPAATqMnqKv5ko\",\"messageID\":\"msg_11769ada3001I7spFhQzP2HSRc\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The core card fix predates this job, but TASK-2 also asks for label/border token changes that are still present. Let me investigate whether those are real remaining bugs under single-mode themes.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394171770,\"end\":1791394172355\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394257754,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176b1a61001jlJU5aPB9F1uUi\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176b0ba2001dEKwxIKO4aO2b5\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me look at the actual reported screenshot to be certain about the bug.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394257505,\"end\":1791394257748\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394298329,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176bb198001QhiwJmYCYSHxhw\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176b85a9001rggdnkZWSTUZw8\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I can now objectively decode the screenshot without vision. Let me get precise color statistics.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394296216,\"end\":1791394298327\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394309245,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176bce36001WEOEKgFa5X9cHE\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176bc226001NMutt9jHRaKy6D\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Definitive evidence: the screenshot is 89.9% dark `#353d4a` (Nord page) with a central card of `#ebeef4` — exactly Nord's `--color-white` (`#eceff4`). This confirms the bug is the auth card, already fixed by `bg-c-bg-surface`. Let me finalize the job documentation.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394303542,\"end\":1791394309226\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394321299,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176c097f001Ng62GmOeDAS6L1\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176bf7300019JWLC83XrISh2s\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Worktree is clean and the job is finalized. Here's the summary.\\n\\n## Result\\n\\n**Branch:** `feature/create_theme-on-login` — matches `brief.md` (`branch: feature/create_theme-on-login`). ✅\\n\\n**Root cause (confirmed):** The white surface on the Nord login page is the auth **card**, not the page body. The cards used literal `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`; the `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `.dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` removes it for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false`). So under Nord the fallback never applied and the card stayed at Nord's `--color-white: #eceff4` — a stable near-white card on an otherwise dark page.\\n\\n**Objective screenshot evidence (no vision needed):** I downloaded the report image from `brief.md` and decoded the PNG pixels directly:\\n- 89.9% of pixels are dark `#353d4a` (Nord polar-night page).\\n- The only light region is one central rectangle, `#ebeef4`, at x 38–71% / y 34–62% — the auth card, and `#ebeef4` is exactly Nord's `--color-white: #eceff4`.\\n- No other white surface exists, so the page background and inputs were never the problem.\\n\\n**Why no product code change was needed:** That exact fix already landed on `main` as commit `70f6236` (Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) and reached this branch through the `main` merge `8c0ad30`. All nine auth card blocks now use the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token (Nord: `#3b4252`). `git diff main...HEAD` contains only this job's docs; the fix is an ancestor of `HEAD`.\\n\\n**Deliberately not applied** (TASK-2 secondary items): the `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 …` swap (labels already inherit a correct themed colour from `auth/+layout.svelte`, and the swap changes default light rendering, violating the task's “pixel-identical” constraint) and the unspecified `border-white/5` token swap (no target token, `/setup` uses the same pattern, decorative). The team's own fix and its approved review left these untouched.\\n\\n**TASK-3:** already resolved — `TimePicker.svelte:63` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\\n\\n**TASK-4:** static verification only; `node_modules` is not installed and packages must not be installed without approval, so `check`/`lint`/`test`/build could not run — but the branch adds no product code, so there is no rendering change to verify.\\n\\n**Likely production remedy:** prod is running a build older than `70f6236`; deploying current `main` (already contained in this branch) removes the white card. That is an operational deploy step, not a code change.\\n\\nCommitted as `2105e1c`; worktree is clean. Updated `implementation.md` with the condensed summary, the new screenshot-derived evidence, and the follow-ups. No product source was modified.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394318719,\"end\":1791394321287\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394416040,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176d848b001r094Jtgu5SvlPl\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176d718a001t1JqfneInDZYQA\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I've independently confirmed the prior analysis. Let me record the re-verification in the implementation summary.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394415755,\"end\":1791394416029\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394433056,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176dbedf001EnzuI8hOH82HGO\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176db16d001H5Yn2WSbY57nnz\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I've completed the job. Here's the summary.\\n\\n## Outcome\\n\\n**No product code change was required.** The white surface reported on the login page is the auth **card**, and that exact defect was already fixed in the repository before this job's branch.\\n\\n## What I verified independently (not just taken on trust)\\n\\n- **Branch check** — worktree is on `feature/create_theme_on_login`... precisely `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`. No checkout needed.\\n- **Fix is present in the branch** — `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true. Commit `70f6236` (*\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\"*) changed the six auth cards from `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\\n- **No literal white left on auth routes** — `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none. Remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative (icon plate, toggle knob, score bar, progress bar).\\n- **Screenshot decoded objectively** — re-downloaded `iili.io/CZZtpwX.png` (973×989) and decoded the PNG by hand: 89.9% of pixels are the dark Nord page `#353d4a`, and the only light region is one central card `#ebeef4` = Nord's `--color-white`. So the report is the card, not the page body.\\n- **Token mapping is render-safe** — `src/styles/tokens.css:24` sets `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff` (light default) and `src/styles/default.css:19` maps it to `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `.dark`, so the swap is pixel-identical in default light/dark and resolves to `#3b4252` under Nord.\\n\\n**Root cause:** literal `bg-white` + a `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback that never fires under single-mode themes (`ThemeState.apply()` removes the `dark` class for `supportsDarkMode: false`), leaving Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white`. The production symptom is therefore a **stale deploy older than `70f6236`**, not a defect in this branch — an operational step, not code.\\n\\n## Changes committed\\n\\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md` — added an \\\"Independent re-verification\\\" section recording the checks above.\\n- Committed as `712975e [create] implementation: add summary`, plus a session-log commit.\\n\\n## Limitation\\n\\n`node_modules` is not installed, so `npm run check/lint/test` and a build+preview render pass could not be run — and per the project hard rule I did not install packages. Since the branch adds no product code relative to `main`, there is no rendering change from this job to verify. The worktree is clean.\\n\\nThe open item from `tasks.md` (TASK-3, TimePicker) is also already resolved: `TimePicker.svelte` now uses `bg-c-bg-modal` via the same commit.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394430687,\"end\":1791394433053\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394562710,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176fc0e8001Z7ZEGi79UoEC9V\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176fb3a10014i0HaYjNQEux07\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I've independently verified the situation. Let me summarize my findings before finalizing.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394562280,\"end\":1791394562708\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394566660,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1176fcb80001r5m63R0X1ZqzO7\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176fc2ed001QochHQnnG8BvvR\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The situation is now fully clear. Let me record the final verification and finish cleanly.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394564992,\"end\":1791394566658\n\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791394582239,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1177004310013Kwas1YOVzD3dO\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1176ff921001G61juMixF26mxB\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Done. Here's what I found and did.\\n\\n## Result: no product-code change was required — the fix is already in this branch\\n\\n**Branch check:** on `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`. ✅\\n\\n### Root cause\\nThe white surface in the screenshot is the **auth card**, not the page. The cards used literal utilities `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`) removes that class for every single-mode theme (Nord, Skyrim, Catppuccin ×2, Gruvbox, Dracula, Terminal, Paper, Atari). So under Nord the `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback never applied, and `bg-white` resolved to Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`.\\n\\n### Why nothing needed changing\\nThat exact fix already landed on `main` in commit **`70f6236`** (\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\", 2026-08-25) and reached this branch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`. `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true, and `git show 22c5a68:src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte` already shows `bg-c-bg-surface` — i.e. the fix is inherited, not introduced here. All six auth cards now use the semantic token `bg-c-bg-surface`, which is pixel-identical in default light/dark and resolves to Nord `#3b4252`. The production white card is therefore a **stale deploy**, not a code defect.\\n\\n### Independent verification\\n- Decoded the brief screenshot (`iili.io/CZZtpwX.png`, 973×989) with a standalone PNG reader (no vision model): 89.9% `#353d4a` page; light pixels only 6.15%, bbox x 38.4–71.2% / y 34.3–62.5%, colour `#ebeef4` (Nord's `--color-white`); inputs already themed `#454d5e`. The card is the only unthemed surface — and it's fixed.\\n- `grep` confirms no `bg-white` remains on auth routes and no `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair exists anywhere under `src/`.\\n- TASK-3 (`TimePicker.svelte`) was fixed by the same commit (`bg-c-bg-modal`).\\n- I deliberately did **not** apply TASK-2's two secondary substitutions (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9…`, `border-white/5` → token border): the team's own reviewed fix left both in place (they're decorative/inherited), and changing them would alter default-light rendering, violating TASK-2's pixel-identity constraint.\\n\\n### Commits\\n- `0a60b6e` — finalization notes in `implementation.md` + worktree cleanup. Working tree is clean.\\n\\n### Follow-ups (not in scope)\\nDeploy current `main` to production (operational). Inherited open items: pre-paint theme script (FOUC hardening), `html` background rule, account-synced theme, and `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`. Rendered `shot` verification was not possible — `node_modules` is absent and installing packages is against the project's hard rule.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394579505,\"end\":1791394582236\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -o '\"type\":\"text\"[^}]*' /workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log | tail -20","time":{"start":1791394615268,"end":1791394615301}},"id":"prt_117708f590015AFff5MgYQpVFe","sessionID":"ses_ee88fe25bffe2xhvlL8jpyAcF9","messageID":"msg_1177082490010jVgqC7d9CAN6v"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791394615819,"sessionID":"ses_ee88fe25bffe2xhvlL8jpyAcF9","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_fZwAwKjXbOHE0lmLvJMy7265","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"wc -l /workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log; grep -n -i 'reject\\|verdict\\|NEEDS-HUMAN\\|reviewer\\|duplicate' /workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log | tail -30"},"output":"...output truncated...\n\nFull output saved to: /home/claude/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_1177091f10010SoJWyqEEMqhxz\n\n738:{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1791394615356,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee88fe25bffe2xhvlL8jpyAcF9\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"bash\",\"callID\":\"call_00_y7ibzcoHXUpq6MDWrrAb2266\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"grep -o '\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\"[^}]*' /workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log | tail -20\"},\"output\":\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394067121,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee8992534ffeRsL1e6F5QzjEOp\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_117682a0c0010uQEhnANzI5siq\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_117681ac0001sv26NZjgEf0UvZ\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee8992534ffeRsL1e6F5QzjEOp\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Work complete. Here's the summary of this session.\\\\n\\\\n## Outcome\\\\n\\\\nThe job's product fix was **already present on `main`** (commit `70f6236`, \\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\") and reached this branch via the `main` merge (`8c0ad30`). This branch's diff against `main` is docs-only — no additional product code change is required.\\\\n\\\\n**Root cause (confirmed):** auth cards used literal white utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`). Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false`, so `ThemeState.apply()` never adds `.dark` and the themed fallback never fires — leaving the card at `--color-white`, which Nord deliberately keeps near-white (`#eceff4`) so `text-white` stays legible. That's the white surface in the production screenshot.\\\\n\\\\n**Fix (already in tree):** all nine auth card blocks now use the semantic token `bg-c-bg-surface` (→ `#fff` light default, `s-dark-2` dark default, `#3b4252` Nord), and `TimePicker` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\\\\n\\\\n## What I did this pass\\\\n\\\\n- Independently re-verified the committed tree: `70f6236` is an ancestor of `HEAD`; `git diff main...HEAD` is docs-only; all auth cards use `bg-c-bg-surface`; `grep bg-white src/` leaves only six decorative, non-auth hits (IconPlate ×3, ScoreBar ×3); Nord token values confirmed.\\\\n- The two secondary `tasks.md` swaps were deliberately not applied — labels already inherit a themed color (`text-c-neutral-8`/Nord `#d8dee9`) and adding `text-c-neutral-9` would change default light rendering, violating the \\\\\\\"pixel-identical\\\\\\\" requirement.\\\\n- Recorded a re-verification section in `implementation.md` and committed the leftover harness artifacts (`session.log`, `tokens.json`) so the worktree is clean.\\\\n\\\\n## Verification limits\\\\n\\\\nNo `node_modules`, dev server, or `build/` exists in this environment, and installing packages is against project rules, so `npm run check/lint/test`, build/preview, and `shot` rendering were not possible. Verification was static (grep/git/token inspection). Nothing in the branch changes rendering relative to `main`.\\\\n\\\\nAll changes are committed (`1b6777e`); worktree is clean. No `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT` required.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394064908,\\\"end\\\":1791394067113\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394076744,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_117685659001bsQmzOQjeeM3hO\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_117684fab0015OTV4ARXCg9ZFc\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The branch matches. There's prior work — let me review it before doing anything.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394076249,\\\"end\\\":1791394076740\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394081907,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11768691d001Q1I6qQZelmcZGK\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176858b0001HvbmkWM6KhOAvc\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let me independently verify the prior findings rather than trust them.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394081053,\\\"end\\\":1791394081902\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394085948,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_117687af0001hEmQZXEPo7QsvF\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_117686cb5001i0rlN2Q83kubrk\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Prior findings verified. Let me look at the actual auth layout/pages to check for any remaining white-surface mechanism the prior analysis may have missed.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394085616,\\\"end\\\":1791394085945\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394099468,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11768ade0001fDRVpeGHuNpnnn\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11768947b001VeWN4L4Vdtkh30\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let me check the theme token definitions — the brief says \\\\\\\"white background\\\\\\\" which could be the page, not just the card.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394098657,\\\"end\\\":1791394099464\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394105350,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11768c5d7001SEHA0ttW5tHuJA\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11768b14a001QcxmHP7Mka9hdx\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let me confirm the earlier fix actually touched the auth cards (not something incidental).\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394104792,\\\"end\\\":1791394105346\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394121785,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11768fef1001u6iBYbDB7CB71T\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11768c848001JTOD2YquG5792Y\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The prior analysis is fully verified:\\\\n\\\\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true.\\\\n- `70f6236` (\\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\", 2026-08-25) changed exactly the auth cards from `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` → `bg-c-bg-surface`, plus `TimePicker` → `bg-c-bg-modal`.\\\\n- All nine auth card blocks now use `bg-c-bg-surface`; no `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains anywhere.\\\\n- `git diff main...HEAD` contains only this job's docs — the branch adds no product code.\\\\n- Nord defines all `--color-c-*` tokens to dark values (`--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252`), so with current code the login page and card are correctly dark.\\\\n\\\\nSo TASK-2/TASK-3 are already satisfied by an earlier fix, and there is no product change to make. I'll finalize the job: document this independent pass, commit the pending harness artifacts, and leave the worktree clean.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394119409,\\\"end\\\":1791394121781\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394131239,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11769247d001fKqNN3Peb7ARCx\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176911870010Ehy0M1Rfk4TJc\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Done. Worktree is clean and the job is finalized.\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n**Branch check:** `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches `brief.md` (`branch: feature/create_theme-on-login`). ✅\\\\n\\\\n**Finding (verified independently):** The white surface on the Nord login page came from literal white utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) on the auth cards. Single-mode themes (`supportsDarkMode: false`, e.g. Nord) never add the `.dark` class, so the themed `dark:` fallback never fired and the card stayed `--color-white` (`#eceff4` under Nord) — a stable near-white card on an otherwise-Nord page. That is exactly the report in `brief.md`.\\\\n\\\\n**Why no product code change was needed:** The fix already exists in `main` as commit `70f6236` (\\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\", 2026-08-25), which changed precisely these auth cards from `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` (and `TimePicker` to `bg-c-bg-modal`). That commit is an ancestor of this branch (arrived via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`), and `git diff main...HEAD` shows **only this job's docs** — the branch adds no product code.\\\\n\\\\nVerification performed this pass:\\\\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD` → docs only.\\\\n- All nine auth card blocks use `bg-c-bg-surface`; no `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains anywhere.\\\\n- Remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative only (logo plates, toggle knob, score/progress bars), none on auth routes.\\\\n- Nord maps `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252` / `--color-c-neutral: #323a49`, so the current login page renders correctly dark.\\\\n\\\\n**Changes committed:** updated `implementation.md` with a final verification pass, and committed the pending harness artifacts (`session.log`, `tokens.json`). Commit `f0a61ab`.\\\\n\\\\n**Known limitations / follow-ups:** The prod-browser facts TASK-1 asked for (other-origin LocalStorage, deployed version) can't be read by an unattended agent; `node_modules` is absent, so no build/preview/`shot` render was possible and no packages were installed (project hard rule). The most likely production cause is simply an older deployed frontend build predating `70f6236`; deploying current `main` (which this branch already contains) resolves the white card. No `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT` condition.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394129021,\\\"end\\\":1791394131235\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394144076,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_117695d02001gfXmmxIGwKLM2L\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11769541b001bxlTd2OFDXDbv9\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Branch matches the brief. Let me read the task files and existing progress.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394143490,\\\"end\\\":1791394144068\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394148977,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11769705c001qlkrWQUiruxaQH\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11769601d001G59q3oG2yQ6V44\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"This job has prior work. Let me independently verify the state before deciding what remains.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394148444,\\\"end\\\":1791394148967\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394172359,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11769cb7a001WPAATqMnqKv5ko\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11769ada3001I7spFhQzP2HSRc\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The core card fix predates this job, but TASK-2 also asks for label/border token changes that are still present. Let me investigate whether those are real remaining bugs under single-mode themes.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394171770,\\\"end\\\":1791394172355\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394257754,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176b1a61001jlJU5aPB9F1uUi\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176b0ba2001dEKwxIKO4aO2b5\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let me look at the actual reported screenshot to be certain about the bug.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394257505,\\\"end\\\":1791394257748\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394298329,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176bb198001QhiwJmYCYSHxhw\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176b85a9001rggdnkZWSTUZw8\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I can now objectively decode the screenshot without vision. Let me get precise color statistics.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394296216,\\\"end\\\":1791394298327\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394309245,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176bce36001WEOEKgFa5X9cHE\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176bc226001NMutt9jHRaKy6D\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Definitive evidence: the screenshot is 89.9% dark `#353d4a` (Nord page) with a central card of `#ebeef4` — exactly Nord's `--color-white` (`#eceff4`). This confirms the bug is the auth card, already fixed by `bg-c-bg-surface`. Let me finalize the job documentation.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394303542,\\\"end\\\":1791394309226\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394321299,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176c097f001Ng62GmOeDAS6L1\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176bf7300019JWLC83XrISh2s\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Worktree is clean and the job is finalized. Here's the summary.\\\\n\\\\n## Result\\\\n\\\\n**Branch:** `feature/create_theme-on-login` — matches `brief.md` (`branch: feature/create_theme-on-login`). ✅\\\\n\\\\n**Root cause (confirmed):** The white surface on the Nord login page is the auth **card**, not the page body. The cards used literal `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`; the `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `.dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` removes it for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false`). So under Nord the fallback never applied and the card stayed at Nord's `--color-white: #eceff4` — a stable near-white card on an otherwise dark page.\\\\n\\\\n**Objective screenshot evidence (no vision needed):** I downloaded the report image from `brief.md` and decoded the PNG pixels directly:\\\\n- 89.9% of pixels are dark `#353d4a` (Nord polar-night page).\\\\n- The only light region is one central rectangle, `#ebeef4`, at x 38–71% / y 34–62% — the auth card, and `#ebeef4` is exactly Nord's `--color-white: #eceff4`.\\\\n- No other white surface exists, so the page background and inputs were never the problem.\\\\n\\\\n**Why no product code change was needed:** That exact fix already landed on `main` as commit `70f6236` (Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) and reached this branch through the `main` merge `8c0ad30`. All nine auth card blocks now use the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token (Nord: `#3b4252`). `git diff main...HEAD` contains only this job's docs; the fix is an ancestor of `HEAD`.\\\\n\\\\n**Deliberately not applied** (TASK-2 secondary items): the `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 …` swap (labels already inherit a correct themed colour from `auth/+layout.svelte`, and the swap changes default light rendering, violating the task's “pixel-identical” constraint) and the unspecified `border-white/5` token swap (no target token, `/setup` uses the same pattern, decorative). The team's own fix and its approved review left these untouched.\\\\n\\\\n**TASK-3:** already resolved — `TimePicker.svelte:63` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\\\\n\\\\n**TASK-4:** static verification only; `node_modules` is not installed and packages must not be installed without approval, so `check`/`lint`/`test`/build could not run — but the branch adds no product code, so there is no rendering change to verify.\\\\n\\\\n**Likely production remedy:** prod is running a build older than `70f6236`; deploying current `main` (already contained in this branch) removes the white card. That is an operational deploy step, not a code change.\\\\n\\\\nCommitted as `2105e1c`; worktree is clean. Updated `implementation.md` with the condensed summary, the new screenshot-derived evidence, and the follow-ups. No product source was modified.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394318719,\\\"end\\\":1791394321287\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394416040,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176d848b001r094Jtgu5SvlPl\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176d718a001t1JqfneInDZYQA\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I've independently confirmed the prior analysis. Let me record the re-verification in the implementation summary.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394415755,\\\"end\\\":1791394416029\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394433056,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176dbedf001EnzuI8hOH82HGO\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176db16d001H5Yn2WSbY57nnz\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I've completed the job. Here's the summary.\\\\n\\\\n## Outcome\\\\n\\\\n**No product code change was required.** The white surface reported on the login page is the auth **card**, and that exact defect was already fixed in the repository before this job's branch.\\\\n\\\\n## What I verified independently (not just taken on trust)\\\\n\\\\n- **Branch check** — worktree is on `feature/create_theme_on_login`... precisely `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`. No checkout needed.\\\\n- **Fix is present in the branch** — `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true. Commit `70f6236` (*\\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\"*) changed the six auth cards from `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\\\\n- **No literal white left on auth routes** — `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none. Remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative (icon plate, toggle knob, score bar, progress bar).\\\\n- **Screenshot decoded objectively** — re-downloaded `iili.io/CZZtpwX.png` (973×989) and decoded the PNG by hand: 89.9% of pixels are the dark Nord page `#353d4a`, and the only light region is one central card `#ebeef4` = Nord's `--color-white`. So the report is the card, not the page body.\\\\n- **Token mapping is render-safe** — `src/styles/tokens.css:24` sets `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff` (light default) and `src/styles/default.css:19` maps it to `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `.dark`, so the swap is pixel-identical in default light/dark and resolves to `#3b4252` under Nord.\\\\n\\\\n**Root cause:** literal `bg-white` + a `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback that never fires under single-mode themes (`ThemeState.apply()` removes the `dark` class for `supportsDarkMode: false`), leaving Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white`. The production symptom is therefore a **stale deploy older than `70f6236`**, not a defect in this branch — an operational step, not code.\\\\n\\\\n## Changes committed\\\\n\\\\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md` — added an \\\\\\\"Independent re-verification\\\\\\\" section recording the checks above.\\\\n- Committed as `712975e [create] implementation: add summary`, plus a session-log commit.\\\\n\\\\n## Limitation\\\\n\\\\n`node_modules` is not installed, so `npm run check/lint/test` and a build+preview render pass could not be run — and per the project hard rule I did not install packages. Since the branch adds no product code relative to `main`, there is no rendering change from this job to verify. The worktree is clean.\\\\n\\\\nThe open item from `tasks.md` (TASK-3, TimePicker) is also already resolved: `TimePicker.svelte` now uses `bg-c-bg-modal` via the same commit.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394430687,\\\"end\\\":1791394433053\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394562710,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176fc0e8001Z7ZEGi79UoEC9V\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176fb3a10014i0HaYjNQEux07\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I've independently verified the situation. Let me summarize my findings before finalizing.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394562280,\\\"end\\\":1791394562708\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394566660,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176fcb80001r5m63R0X1ZqzO7\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176fc2ed001QochHQnnG8BvvR\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The situation is now fully clear. Let me record the final verification and finish cleanly.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394564992,\\\"end\\\":1791394566658\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394582239,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1177004310013Kwas1YOVzD3dO\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176ff921001G61juMixF26mxB\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Done. Here's what I found and did.\\\\n\\\\n## Result: no product-code change was required — the fix is already in this branch\\\\n\\\\n**Branch check:** on `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`. ✅\\\\n\\\\n### Root cause\\\\nThe white surface in the screenshot is the **auth card**, not the page. The cards used literal utilities `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`) removes that class for every single-mode theme (Nord, Skyrim, Catppuccin ×2, Gruvbox, Dracula, Terminal, Paper, Atari). So under Nord the `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback never applied, and `bg-white` resolved to Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`.\\\\n\\\\n### Why nothing needed changing\\\\nThat exact fix already landed on `main` in commit **`70f6236`** (\\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\", 2026-08-25) and reached this branch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`. `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true, and `git show 22c5a68:src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte` already shows `bg-c-bg-surface` — i.e. the fix is inherited, not introduced here. All six auth cards now use the semantic token `bg-c-bg-surface`, which is pixel-identical in default light/dark and resolves to Nord `#3b4252`. The production white card is therefore a **stale deploy**, not a code defect.\\\\n\\\\n### Independent verification\\\\n- Decoded the brief screenshot (`iili.io/CZZtpwX.png`, 973×989) with a standalone PNG reader (no vision model): 89.9% `#353d4a` page; light pixels only 6.15%, bbox x 38.4–71.2% / y 34.3–62.5%, colour `#ebeef4` (Nord's `--color-white`); inputs already themed `#454d5e`. The card is the only unthemed surface — and it's fixed.\\\\n- `grep` confirms no `bg-white` remains on auth routes and no `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair exists anywhere under `src/`.\\\\n- TASK-3 (`TimePicker.svelte`) was fixed by the same commit (`bg-c-bg-modal`).\\\\n- I deliberately did **not** apply TASK-2's two secondary substitutions (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9…`, `border-white/5` → token border): the team's own reviewed fix left both in place (they're decorative/inherited), and changing them would alter default-light rendering, violating TASK-2's pixel-identity constraint.\\\\n\\\\n### Commits\\\\n- `0a60b6e` — finalization notes in `implementation.md` + worktree cleanup. Working tree is clean.\\\\n\\\\n### Follow-ups (not in scope)\\\\nDeploy current `main` to production (operational). Inherited open items: pre-paint theme script (FOUC hardening), `html` background rule, account-synced theme, and `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`. Rendered `shot` verification was not possible — `node_modules` is absent and installing packages is against the project's hard rule.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394579505,\\\"end\\\":1791394582236\\n\",\"metadata\":{\"output\":\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394067121,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee8992534ffeRsL1e6F5QzjEOp\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_117682a0c0010uQEhnANzI5siq\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_117681ac0001sv26NZjgEf0UvZ\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee8992534ffeRsL1e6F5QzjEOp\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Work complete. Here's the summary of this session.\\\\n\\\\n## Outcome\\\\n\\\\nThe job's product fix was **already present on `main`** (commit `70f6236`, \\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\") and reached this branch via the `main` merge (`8c0ad30`). This branch's diff against `main` is docs-only — no additional product code change is required.\\\\n\\\\n**Root cause (confirmed):** auth cards used literal white utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`). Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false`, so `ThemeState.apply()` never adds `.dark` and the themed fallback never fires — leaving the card at `--color-white`, which Nord deliberately keeps near-white (`#eceff4`) so `text-white` stays legible. That's the white surface in the production screenshot.\\\\n\\\\n**Fix (already in tree):** all nine auth card blocks now use the semantic token `bg-c-bg-surface` (→ `#fff` light default, `s-dark-2` dark default, `#3b4252` Nord), and `TimePicker` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\\\\n\\\\n## What I did this pass\\\\n\\\\n- Independently re-verified the committed tree: `70f6236` is an ancestor of `HEAD`; `git diff main...HEAD` is docs-only; all auth cards use `bg-c-bg-surface`; `grep bg-white src/` leaves only six decorative, non-auth hits (IconPlate ×3, ScoreBar ×3); Nord token values confirmed.\\\\n- The two secondary `tasks.md` swaps were deliberately not applied — labels already inherit a themed color (`text-c-neutral-8`/Nord `#d8dee9`) and adding `text-c-neutral-9` would change default light rendering, violating the \\\\\\\"pixel-identical\\\\\\\" requirement.\\\\n- Recorded a re-verification section in `implementation.md` and committed the leftover harness artifacts (`session.log`, `tokens.json`) so the worktree is clean.\\\\n\\\\n## Verification limits\\\\n\\\\nNo `node_modules`, dev server, or `build/` exists in this environment, and installing packages is against project rules, so `npm run check/lint/test`, build/preview, and `shot` rendering were not possible. Verification was static (grep/git/token inspection). Nothing in the branch changes rendering relative to `main`.\\\\n\\\\nAll changes are committed (`1b6777e`); worktree is clean. No `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT` required.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394064908,\\\"end\\\":1791394067113\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394076744,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_117685659001bsQmzOQjeeM3hO\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_117684fab0015OTV4ARXCg9ZFc\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The branch matches. There's prior work — let me review it before doing anything.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394076249,\\\"end\\\":1791394076740\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394081907,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11768691d001Q1I6qQZelmcZGK\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176858b0001HvbmkWM6KhOAvc\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let me independently verify the prior findings rather than trust them.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394081053,\\\"end\\\":1791394081902\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394085948,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_117687af0001hEmQZXEPo7QsvF\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_117686cb5001i0rlN2Q83kubrk\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Prior findings verified. Let me look at the actual auth layout/pages to check for any remaining white-surface mechanism the prior analysis may have missed.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394085616,\\\"end\\\":1791394085945\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394099468,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11768ade0001fDRVpeGHuNpnnn\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11768947b001VeWN4L4Vdtkh30\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let me check the theme token definitions — the brief says \\\\\\\"white background\\\\\\\" which could be the page, not just the card.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394098657,\\\"end\\\":1791394099464\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394105350,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11768c5d7001SEHA0ttW5tHuJA\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11768b14a001QcxmHP7Mka9hdx\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let me confirm the earlier fix actually touched the auth cards (not something incidental).\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394104792,\\\"end\\\":1791394105346\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394121785,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11768fef1001u6iBYbDB7CB71T\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11768c848001JTOD2YquG5792Y\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The prior analysis is fully verified:\\\\n\\\\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true.\\\\n- `70f6236` (\\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\", 2026-08-25) changed exactly the auth cards from `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` → `bg-c-bg-surface`, plus `TimePicker` → `bg-c-bg-modal`.\\\\n- All nine auth card blocks now use `bg-c-bg-surface`; no `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains anywhere.\\\\n- `git diff main...HEAD` contains only this job's docs — the branch adds no product code.\\\\n- Nord defines all `--color-c-*` tokens to dark values (`--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252`), so with current code the login page and card are correctly dark.\\\\n\\\\nSo TASK-2/TASK-3 are already satisfied by an earlier fix, and there is no product change to make. I'll finalize the job: document this independent pass, commit the pending harness artifacts, and leave the worktree clean.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394119409,\\\"end\\\":1791394121781\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394131239,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11769247d001fKqNN3Peb7ARCx\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176911870010Ehy0M1Rfk4TJc\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Done. Worktree is clean and the job is finalized.\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n**Branch check:** `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches `brief.md` (`branch: feature/create_theme-on-login`). ✅\\\\n\\\\n**Finding (verified independently):** The white surface on the Nord login page came from literal white utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) on the auth cards. Single-mode themes (`supportsDarkMode: false`, e.g. Nord) never add the `.dark` class, so the themed `dark:` fallback never fired and the card stayed `--color-white` (`#eceff4` under Nord) — a stable near-white card on an otherwise-Nord page. That is exactly the report in `brief.md`.\\\\n\\\\n**Why no product code change was needed:** The fix already exists in `main` as commit `70f6236` (\\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\", 2026-08-25), which changed precisely these auth cards from `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` (and `TimePicker` to `bg-c-bg-modal`). That commit is an ancestor of this branch (arrived via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`), and `git diff main...HEAD` shows **only this job's docs** — the branch adds no product code.\\\\n\\\\nVerification performed this pass:\\\\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD` → docs only.\\\\n- All nine auth card blocks use `bg-c-bg-surface`; no `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains anywhere.\\\\n- Remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative only (logo plates, toggle knob, score/progress bars), none on auth routes.\\\\n- Nord maps `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252` / `--color-c-neutral: #323a49`, so the current login page renders correctly dark.\\\\n\\\\n**Changes committed:** updated `implementation.md` with a final verification pass, and committed the pending harness artifacts (`session.log`, `tokens.json`). Commit `f0a61ab`.\\\\n\\\\n**Known limitations / follow-ups:** The prod-browser facts TASK-1 asked for (other-origin LocalStorage, deployed version) can't be read by an unattended agent; `node_modules` is absent, so no build/preview/`shot` render was possible and no packages were installed (project hard rule). The most likely production cause is simply an older deployed frontend build predating `70f6236`; deploying current `main` (which this branch already contains) resolves the white card. No `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT` condition.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394129021,\\\"end\\\":1791394131235\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394144076,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_117695d02001gfXmmxIGwKLM2L\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11769541b001bxlTd2OFDXDbv9\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Branch matches the brief. Let me read the task files and existing progress.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394143490,\\\"end\\\":1791394144068\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394148977,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11769705c001qlkrWQUiruxaQH\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11769601d001G59q3oG2yQ6V44\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"This job has prior work. Let me independently verify the state before deciding what remains.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394148444,\\\"end\\\":1791394148967\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394172359,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11769cb7a001WPAATqMnqKv5ko\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11769ada3001I7spFhQzP2HSRc\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The core card fix predates this job, but TASK-2 also asks for label/border token changes that are still present. Let me investigate whether those are real remaining bugs under single-mode themes.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394171770,\\\"end\\\":1791394172355\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394257754,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176b1a61001jlJU5aPB9F1uUi\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176b0ba2001dEKwxIKO4aO2b5\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let me look at the actual reported screenshot to be certain about the bug.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394257505,\\\"end\\\":1791394257748\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394298329,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176bb198001QhiwJmYCYSHxhw\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176b85a9001rggdnkZWSTUZw8\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I can now objectively decode the screenshot without vision. Let me get precise color statistics.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394296216,\\\"end\\\":1791394298327\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394309245,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176bce36001WEOEKgFa5X9cHE\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176bc226001NMutt9jHRaKy6D\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Definitive evidence: the screenshot is 89.9% dark `#353d4a` (Nord page) with a central card of `#ebeef4` — exactly Nord's `--color-white` (`#eceff4`). This confirms the bug is the auth card, already fixed by `bg-c-bg-surface`. Let me finalize the job documentation.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394303542,\\\"end\\\":1791394309226\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394321299,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176c097f001Ng62GmOeDAS6L1\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176bf7300019JWLC83XrISh2s\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Worktree is clean and the job is finalized. Here's the summary.\\\\n\\\\n## Result\\\\n\\\\n**Branch:** `feature/create_theme-on-login` — matches `brief.md` (`branch: feature/create_theme-on-login`). ✅\\\\n\\\\n**Root cause (confirmed):** The white surface on the Nord login page is the auth **card**, not the page body. The cards used literal `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`; the `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `.dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` removes it for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false`). So under Nord the fallback never applied and the card stayed at Nord's `--color-white: #eceff4` — a stable near-white card on an otherwise dark page.\\\\n\\\\n**Objective screenshot evidence (no vision needed):** I downloaded the report image from `brief.md` and decoded the PNG pixels directly:\\\\n- 89.9% of pixels are dark `#353d4a` (Nord polar-night page).\\\\n- The only light region is one central rectangle, `#ebeef4`, at x 38–71% / y 34–62% — the auth card, and `#ebeef4` is exactly Nord's `--color-white: #eceff4`.\\\\n- No other white surface exists, so the page background and inputs were never the problem.\\\\n\\\\n**Why no product code change was needed:** That exact fix already landed on `main` as commit `70f6236` (Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) and reached this branch through the `main` merge `8c0ad30`. All nine auth card blocks now use the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token (Nord: `#3b4252`). `git diff main...HEAD` contains only this job's docs; the fix is an ancestor of `HEAD`.\\\\n\\\\n**Deliberately not applied** (TASK-2 secondary items): the `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 …` swap (labels already inherit a correct themed colour from `auth/+layout.svelte`, and the swap changes default light rendering, violating the task's “pixel-identical” constraint) and the unspecified `border-white/5` token swap (no target token, `/setup` uses the same pattern, decorative). The team's own fix and its approved review left these untouched.\\\\n\\\\n**TASK-3:** already resolved — `TimePicker.svelte:63` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\\\\n\\\\n**TASK-4:** static verification only; `node_modules` is not installed and packages must not be installed without approval, so `check`/`lint`/`test`/build could not run — but the branch adds no product code, so there is no rendering change to verify.\\\\n\\\\n**Likely production remedy:** prod is running a build older than `70f6236`; deploying current `main` (already contained in this branch) removes the white card. That is an operational deploy step, not a code change.\\\\n\\\\nCommitted as `2105e1c`; worktree is clean. Updated `implementation.md` with the condensed summary, the new screenshot-derived evidence, and the follow-ups. No product source was modified.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394318719,\\\"end\\\":1791394321287\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394416040,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176d848b001r094Jtgu5SvlPl\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176d718a001t1JqfneInDZYQA\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I've independently confirmed the prior analysis. Let me record the re-verification in the implementation summary.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394415755,\\\"end\\\":1791394416029\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394433056,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176dbedf001EnzuI8hOH82HGO\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176db16d001H5Yn2WSbY57nnz\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I've completed the job. Here's the summary.\\\\n\\\\n## Outcome\\\\n\\\\n**No product code change was required.** The white surface reported on the login page is the auth **card**, and that exact defect was already fixed in the repository before this job's branch.\\\\n\\\\n## What I verified independently (not just taken on trust)\\\\n\\\\n- **Branch check** — worktree is on `feature/create_theme_on_login`... precisely `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`. No checkout needed.\\\\n- **Fix is present in the branch** — `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true. Commit `70f6236` (*\\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\"*) changed the six auth cards from `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\\\\n- **No literal white left on auth routes** — `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none. Remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative (icon plate, toggle knob, score bar, progress bar).\\\\n- **Screenshot decoded objectively** — re-downloaded `iili.io/CZZtpwX.png` (973×989) and decoded the PNG by hand: 89.9% of pixels are the dark Nord page `#353d4a`, and the only light region is one central card `#ebeef4` = Nord's `--color-white`. So the report is the card, not the page body.\\\\n- **Token mapping is render-safe** — `src/styles/tokens.css:24` sets `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff` (light default) and `src/styles/default.css:19` maps it to `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `.dark`, so the swap is pixel-identical in default light/dark and resolves to `#3b4252` under Nord.\\\\n\\\\n**Root cause:** literal `bg-white` + a `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback that never fires under single-mode themes (`ThemeState.apply()` removes the `dark` class for `supportsDarkMode: false`), leaving Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white`. The production symptom is therefore a **stale deploy older than `70f6236`**, not a defect in this branch — an operational step, not code.\\\\n\\\\n## Changes committed\\\\n\\\\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md` — added an \\\\\\\"Independent re-verification\\\\\\\" section recording the checks above.\\\\n- Committed as `712975e [create] implementation: add summary`, plus a session-log commit.\\\\n\\\\n## Limitation\\\\n\\\\n`node_modules` is not installed, so `npm run check/lint/test` and a build+preview render pass could not be run — and per the project hard rule I did not install packages. Since the branch adds no product code relative to `main`, there is no rendering change from this job to verify. The worktree is clean.\\\\n\\\\nThe open item from `tasks.md` (TASK-3, TimePicker) is also already resolved: `TimePicker.svelte` now uses `bg-c-bg-modal` via the same commit.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394430687,\\\"end\\\":1791394433053\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394562710,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176fc0e8001Z7ZEGi79UoEC9V\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176fb3a10014i0HaYjNQEux07\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I've independently verified the situation. Let me summarize my findings before finalizing.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394562280,\\\"end\\\":1791394562708\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394566660,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176fcb80001r5m63R0X1ZqzO7\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176fc2ed001QochHQnnG8BvvR\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The situation is now fully clear. Let me record the final verification and finish cleanly.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394564992,\\\"end\\\":1791394566658\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394582239,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1177004310013Kwas1YOVzD3dO\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176ff921001G61juMixF26mxB\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Done. Here's what I found and did.\\\\n\\\\n## Result: no product-code change was required — the fix is already in this branch\\\\n\\\\n**Branch check:** on `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`. ✅\\\\n\\\\n### Root cause\\\\nThe white surface in the screenshot is the **auth card**, not the page. The cards used literal utilities `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`) removes that class for every single-mode theme (Nord, Skyrim, Catppuccin ×2, Gruvbox, Dracula, Terminal, Paper, Atari). So under Nord the `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback never applied, and `bg-white` resolved to Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`.\\\\n\\\\n### Why nothing needed changing\\\\nThat exact fix already landed on `main` in commit **`70f6236`** (\\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\", 2026-08-25) and reached this branch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`. `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true, and `git show 22c5a68:src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte` already shows `bg-c-bg-surface` — i.e. the fix is inherited, not introduced here. All six auth cards now use the semantic token `bg-c-bg-surface`, which is pixel-identical in default light/dark and resolves to Nord `#3b4252`. The production white card is therefore a **stale deploy**, not a code defect.\\\\n\\\\n### Independent verification\\\\n- Decoded the brief screenshot (`iili.io/CZZtpwX.png`, 973×989) with a standalone PNG reader (no vision model): 89.9% `#353d4a` page; light pixels only 6.15%, bbox x 38.4–71.2% / y 34.3–62.5%, colour `#ebeef4` (Nord's `--color-white`); inputs already themed `#454d5e`. The card is the only unthemed surface — and it's fixed.\\\\n- `grep` confirms no `bg-white` remains on auth routes and no `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair exists anywhere under `src/`.\\\\n- TASK-3 (`TimePicker.svelte`) was fixed by the same commit (`bg-c-bg-modal`).\\\\n- I deliberately did **not** apply TASK-2's two secondary substitutions (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9…`, `border-white/5` → token border): the team's own reviewed fix left both in place (they're decorative/inherited), and changing them would alter default-light rendering, violating TASK-2's pixel-identity constraint.\\\\n\\\\n### Commits\\\\n- `0a60b6e` — finalization notes in `implementation.md` + worktree cleanup. Working tree is clean.\\\\n\\\\n### Follow-ups (not in scope)\\\\nDeploy current `main` to production (operational). Inherited open items: pre-paint theme script (FOUC hardening), `html` background rule, account-synced theme, and `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`. Rendered `shot` verification was not possible — `node_modules` is absent and installing packages is against the project's hard rule.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394579505,\\\"end\\\":1791394582236\\n\",\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"grep -o '\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\"[^}]*' /workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log | tail -20\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394615268,\"end\":1791394615301}},\"id\":\"prt_117708f590015AFff5MgYQpVFe\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee88fe25bffe2xhvlL8jpyAcF9\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1177082490010jVgqC7d9CAN6v\"}}\n","metadata":{"output":"...\n\n`/`lint`/`test`/build could not run — but the branch adds no product code, so there is no rendering change to verify.\\\\n\\\\n**Likely production remedy:** prod is running a build older than `70f6236`; deploying current `main` (already contained in this branch) removes the white card. That is an operational deploy step, not a code change.\\\\n\\\\nCommitted as `2105e1c`; worktree is clean. Updated `implementation.md` with the condensed summary, the new screenshot-derived evidence, and the follow-ups. No product source was modified.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394318719,\\\"end\\\":1791394321287\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394416040,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176d848b001r094Jtgu5SvlPl\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176d718a001t1JqfneInDZYQA\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I've independently confirmed the prior analysis. Let me record the re-verification in the implementation summary.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394415755,\\\"end\\\":1791394416029\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394433056,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176dbedf001EnzuI8hOH82HGO\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176db16d001H5Yn2WSbY57nnz\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I've completed the job. Here's the summary.\\\\n\\\\n## Outcome\\\\n\\\\n**No product code change was required.** The white surface reported on the login page is the auth **card**, and that exact defect was already fixed in the repository before this job's branch.\\\\n\\\\n## What I verified independently (not just taken on trust)\\\\n\\\\n- **Branch check** — worktree is on `feature/create_theme_on_login`... precisely `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`. No checkout needed.\\\\n- **Fix is present in the branch** — `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true. Commit `70f6236` (*\\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\"*) changed the six auth cards from `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\\\\n- **No literal white left on auth routes** — `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none. Remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative (icon plate, toggle knob, score bar, progress bar).\\\\n- **Screenshot decoded objectively** — re-downloaded `iili.io/CZZtpwX.png` (973×989) and decoded the PNG by hand: 89.9% of pixels are the dark Nord page `#353d4a`, and the only light region is one central card `#ebeef4` = Nord's `--color-white`. So the report is the card, not the page body.\\\\n- **Token mapping is render-safe** — `src/styles/tokens.css:24` sets `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff` (light default) and `src/styles/default.css:19` maps it to `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `.dark`, so the swap is pixel-identical in default light/dark and resolves to `#3b4252` under Nord.\\\\n\\\\n**Root cause:** literal `bg-white` + a `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback that never fires under single-mode themes (`ThemeState.apply()` removes the `dark` class for `supportsDarkMode: false`), leaving Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white`. The production symptom is therefore a **stale deploy older than `70f6236`**, not a defect in this branch — an operational step, not code.\\\\n\\\\n## Changes committed\\\\n\\\\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md` — added an \\\\\\\"Independent re-verification\\\\\\\" section recording the checks above.\\\\n- Committed as `712975e [create] implementation: add summary`, plus a session-log commit.\\\\n\\\\n## Limitation\\\\n\\\\n`node_modules` is not installed, so `npm run check/lint/test` and a build+preview render pass could not be run — and per the project hard rule I did not install packages. Since the branch adds no product code relative to `main`, there is no rendering change from this job to verify. The worktree is clean.\\\\n\\\\nThe open item from `tasks.md` (TASK-3, TimePicker) is also already resolved: `TimePicker.svelte` now uses `bg-c-bg-modal` via the same commit.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394430687,\\\"end\\\":1791394433053\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394562710,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176fc0e8001Z7ZEGi79UoEC9V\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176fb3a10014i0HaYjNQEux07\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I've independently verified the situation. Let me summarize my findings before finalizing.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394562280,\\\"end\\\":1791394562708\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394566660,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176fcb80001r5m63R0X1ZqzO7\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176fc2ed001QochHQnnG8BvvR\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The situation is now fully clear. Let me record the final verification and finish cleanly.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394564992,\\\"end\\\":1791394566658\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394582239,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1177004310013Kwas1YOVzD3dO\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176ff921001G61juMixF26mxB\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Done. Here's what I found and did.\\\\n\\\\n## Result: no product-code change was required — the fix is already in this branch\\\\n\\\\n**Branch check:** on `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`. ✅\\\\n\\\\n### Root cause\\\\nThe white surface in the screenshot is the **auth card**, not the page. The cards used literal utilities `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`) removes that class for every single-mode theme (Nord, Skyrim, Catppuccin ×2, Gruvbox, Dracula, Terminal, Paper, Atari). So under Nord the `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback never applied, and `bg-white` resolved to Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`.\\\\n\\\\n### Why nothing needed changing\\\\nThat exact fix already landed on `main` in commit **`70f6236`** (\\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\", 2026-08-25) and reached this branch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`. `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true, and `git show 22c5a68:src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte` already shows `bg-c-bg-surface` — i.e. the fix is inherited, not introduced here. All six auth cards now use the semantic token `bg-c-bg-surface`, which is pixel-identical in default light/dark and resolves to Nord `#3b4252`. The production white card is therefore a **stale deploy**, not a code defect.\\\\n\\\\n### Independent verification\\\\n- Decoded the brief screenshot (`iili.io/CZZtpwX.png`, 973×989) with a standalone PNG reader (no vision model): 89.9% `#353d4a` page; light pixels only 6.15%, bbox x 38.4–71.2% / y 34.3–62.5%, colour `#ebeef4` (Nord's `--color-white`); inputs already themed `#454d5e`. The card is the only unthemed surface — and it's fixed.\\\\n- `grep` confirms no `bg-white` remains on auth routes and no `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair exists anywhere under `src/`.\\\\n- TASK-3 (`TimePicker.svelte`) was fixed by the same commit (`bg-c-bg-modal`).\\\\n- I deliberately did **not** apply TASK-2's two secondary substitutions (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9…`, `border-white/5` → token border): the team's own reviewed fix left both in place (they're decorative/inherited), and changing them would alter default-light rendering, violating TASK-2's pixel-identity constraint.\\\\n\\\\n### Commits\\\\n- `0a60b6e` — finalization notes in `implementation.md` + worktree cleanup. Working tree is clean.\\\\n\\\\n### Follow-ups (not in scope)\\\\nDeploy current `main` to production (operational). Inherited open items: pre-paint theme script (FOUC hardening), `html` background rule, account-synced theme, and `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`. Rendered `shot` verification was not possible — `node_modules` is absent and installing packages is against the project's hard rule.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394579505,\\\"end\\\":1791394582236\\n\",\"metadata\":{\"output\":\"\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394067121,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee8992534ffeRsL1e6F5QzjEOp\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_117682a0c0010uQEhnANzI5siq\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_117681ac0001sv26NZjgEf0UvZ\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee8992534ffeRsL1e6F5QzjEOp\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Work complete. Here's the summary of this session.\\\\n\\\\n## Outcome\\\\n\\\\nThe job's product fix was **already present on `main`** (commit `70f6236`, \\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\") and reached this branch via the `main` merge (`8c0ad30`). This branch's diff against `main` is docs-only — no additional product code change is required.\\\\n\\\\n**Root cause (confirmed):** auth cards used literal white utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`). Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false`, so `ThemeState.apply()` never adds `.dark` and the themed fallback never fires — leaving the card at `--color-white`, which Nord deliberately keeps near-white (`#eceff4`) so `text-white` stays legible. That's the white surface in the production screenshot.\\\\n\\\\n**Fix (already in tree):** all nine auth card blocks now use the semantic token `bg-c-bg-surface` (→ `#fff` light default, `s-dark-2` dark default, `#3b4252` Nord), and `TimePicker` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\\\\n\\\\n## What I did this pass\\\\n\\\\n- Independently re-verified the committed tree: `70f6236` is an ancestor of `HEAD`; `git diff main...HEAD` is docs-only; all auth cards use `bg-c-bg-surface`; `grep bg-white src/` leaves only six decorative, non-auth hits (IconPlate ×3, ScoreBar ×3); Nord token values confirmed.\\\\n- The two secondary `tasks.md` swaps were deliberately not applied — labels already inherit a themed color (`text-c-neutral-8`/Nord `#d8dee9`) and adding `text-c-neutral-9` would change default light rendering, violating the \\\\\\\"pixel-identical\\\\\\\" requirement.\\\\n- Recorded a re-verification section in `implementation.md` and committed the leftover harness artifacts (`session.log`, `tokens.json`) so the worktree is clean.\\\\n\\\\n## Verification limits\\\\n\\\\nNo `node_modules`, dev server, or `build/` exists in this environment, and installing packages is against project rules, so `npm run check/lint/test`, build/preview, and `shot` rendering were not possible. Verification was static (grep/git/token inspection). Nothing in the branch changes rendering relative to `main`.\\\\n\\\\nAll changes are committed (`1b6777e`); worktree is clean. No `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT` required.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394064908,\\\"end\\\":1791394067113\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394076744,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_117685659001bsQmzOQjeeM3hO\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_117684fab0015OTV4ARXCg9ZFc\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The branch matches. There's prior work — let me review it before doing anything.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394076249,\\\"end\\\":1791394076740\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394081907,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11768691d001Q1I6qQZelmcZGK\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176858b0001HvbmkWM6KhOAvc\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let me independently verify the prior findings rather than trust them.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394081053,\\\"end\\\":1791394081902\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394085948,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_117687af0001hEmQZXEPo7QsvF\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_117686cb5001i0rlN2Q83kubrk\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Prior findings verified. Let me look at the actual auth layout/pages to check for any remaining white-surface mechanism the prior analysis may have missed.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394085616,\\\"end\\\":1791394085945\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394099468,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11768ade0001fDRVpeGHuNpnnn\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11768947b001VeWN4L4Vdtkh30\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let me check the theme token definitions — the brief says \\\\\\\"white background\\\\\\\" which could be the page, not just the card.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394098657,\\\"end\\\":1791394099464\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394105350,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11768c5d7001SEHA0ttW5tHuJA\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11768b14a001QcxmHP7Mka9hdx\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let me confirm the earlier fix actually touched the auth cards (not something incidental).\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394104792,\\\"end\\\":1791394105346\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394121785,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11768fef1001u6iBYbDB7CB71T\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11768c848001JTOD2YquG5792Y\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The prior analysis is fully verified:\\\\n\\\\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true.\\\\n- `70f6236` (\\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\", 2026-08-25) changed exactly the auth cards from `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` → `bg-c-bg-surface`, plus `TimePicker` → `bg-c-bg-modal`.\\\\n- All nine auth card blocks now use `bg-c-bg-surface`; no `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains anywhere.\\\\n- `git diff main...HEAD` contains only this job's docs — the branch adds no product code.\\\\n- Nord defines all `--color-c-*` tokens to dark values (`--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252`), so with current code the login page and card are correctly dark.\\\\n\\\\nSo TASK-2/TASK-3 are already satisfied by an earlier fix, and there is no product change to make. I'll finalize the job: document this independent pass, commit the pending harness artifacts, and leave the worktree clean.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394119409,\\\"end\\\":1791394121781\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394131239,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11769247d001fKqNN3Peb7ARCx\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176911870010Ehy0M1Rfk4TJc\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee897c0b7ffeO7xIHVgA1TSFt6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Done. Worktree is clean and the job is finalized.\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n**Branch check:** `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches `brief.md` (`branch: feature/create_theme-on-login`). ✅\\\\n\\\\n**Finding (verified independently):** The white surface on the Nord login page came from literal white utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) on the auth cards. Single-mode themes (`supportsDarkMode: false`, e.g. Nord) never add the `.dark` class, so the themed `dark:` fallback never fired and the card stayed `--color-white` (`#eceff4` under Nord) — a stable near-white card on an otherwise-Nord page. That is exactly the report in `brief.md`.\\\\n\\\\n**Why no product code change was needed:** The fix already exists in `main` as commit `70f6236` (\\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\", 2026-08-25), which changed precisely these auth cards from `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` (and `TimePicker` to `bg-c-bg-modal`). That commit is an ancestor of this branch (arrived via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`), and `git diff main...HEAD` shows **only this job's docs** — the branch adds no product code.\\\\n\\\\nVerification performed this pass:\\\\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD` → docs only.\\\\n- All nine auth card blocks use `bg-c-bg-surface`; no `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains anywhere.\\\\n- Remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative only (logo plates, toggle knob, score/progress bars), none on auth routes.\\\\n- Nord maps `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252` / `--color-c-neutral: #323a49`, so the current login page renders correctly dark.\\\\n\\\\n**Changes committed:** updated `implementation.md` with a final verification pass, and committed the pending harness artifacts (`session.log`, `tokens.json`). Commit `f0a61ab`.\\\\n\\\\n**Known limitations / follow-ups:** The prod-browser facts TASK-1 asked for (other-origin LocalStorage, deployed version) can't be read by an unattended agent; `node_modules` is absent, so no build/preview/`shot` render was possible and no packages were installed (project hard rule). The most likely production cause is simply an older deployed frontend build predating `70f6236`; deploying current `main` (which this branch already contains) resolves the white card. No `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT` condition.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394129021,\\\"end\\\":1791394131235\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394144076,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_117695d02001gfXmmxIGwKLM2L\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11769541b001bxlTd2OFDXDbv9\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Branch matches the brief. Let me read the task files and existing progress.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394143490,\\\"end\\\":1791394144068\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394148977,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11769705c001qlkrWQUiruxaQH\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11769601d001G59q3oG2yQ6V44\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"This job has prior work. Let me independently verify the state before deciding what remains.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394148444,\\\"end\\\":1791394148967\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394172359,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_11769cb7a001WPAATqMnqKv5ko\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_11769ada3001I7spFhQzP2HSRc\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The core card fix predates this job, but TASK-2 also asks for label/border token changes that are still present. Let me investigate whether those are real remaining bugs under single-mode themes.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394171770,\\\"end\\\":1791394172355\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394257754,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176b1a61001jlJU5aPB9F1uUi\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176b0ba2001dEKwxIKO4aO2b5\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Let me look at the actual reported screenshot to be certain about the bug.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394257505,\\\"end\\\":1791394257748\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394298329,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176bb198001QhiwJmYCYSHxhw\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176b85a9001rggdnkZWSTUZw8\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I can now objectively decode the screenshot without vision. Let me get precise color statistics.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394296216,\\\"end\\\":1791394298327\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394309245,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176bce36001WEOEKgFa5X9cHE\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176bc226001NMutt9jHRaKy6D\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Definitive evidence: the screenshot is 89.9% dark `#353d4a` (Nord page) with a central card of `#ebeef4` — exactly Nord's `--color-white` (`#eceff4`). This confirms the bug is the auth card, already fixed by `bg-c-bg-surface`. Let me finalize the job documentation.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394303542,\\\"end\\\":1791394309226\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394321299,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176c097f001Ng62GmOeDAS6L1\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176bf7300019JWLC83XrISh2s\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee896c4f0ffeVPTzeEEyhcpWIi\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Worktree is clean and the job is finalized. Here's the summary.\\\\n\\\\n## Result\\\\n\\\\n**Branch:** `feature/create_theme-on-login` — matches `brief.md` (`branch: feature/create_theme-on-login`). ✅\\\\n\\\\n**Root cause (confirmed):** The white surface on the Nord login page is the auth **card**, not the page body. The cards used literal `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`; the `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `.dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` removes it for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false`). So under Nord the fallback never applied and the card stayed at Nord's `--color-white: #eceff4` — a stable near-white card on an otherwise dark page.\\\\n\\\\n**Objective screenshot evidence (no vision needed):** I downloaded the report image from `brief.md` and decoded the PNG pixels directly:\\\\n- 89.9% of pixels are dark `#353d4a` (Nord polar-night page).\\\\n- The only light region is one central rectangle, `#ebeef4`, at x 38–71% / y 34–62% — the auth card, and `#ebeef4` is exactly Nord's `--color-white: #eceff4`.\\\\n- No other white surface exists, so the page background and inputs were never the problem.\\\\n\\\\n**Why no product code change was needed:** That exact fix already landed on `main` as commit `70f6236` (Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) and reached this branch through the `main` merge `8c0ad30`. All nine auth card blocks now use the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token (Nord: `#3b4252`). `git diff main...HEAD` contains only this job's docs; the fix is an ancestor of `HEAD`.\\\\n\\\\n**Deliberately not applied** (TASK-2 secondary items): the `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 …` swap (labels already inherit a correct themed colour from `auth/+layout.svelte`, and the swap changes default light rendering, violating the task's “pixel-identical” constraint) and the unspecified `border-white/5` token swap (no target token, `/setup` uses the same pattern, decorative). The team's own fix and its approved review left these untouched.\\\\n\\\\n**TASK-3:** already resolved — `TimePicker.svelte:63` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\\\\n\\\\n**TASK-4:** static verification only; `node_modules` is not installed and packages must not be installed without approval, so `check`/`lint`/`test`/build could not run — but the branch adds no product code, so there is no rendering change to verify.\\\\n\\\\n**Likely production remedy:** prod is running a build older than `70f6236`; deploying current `main` (already contained in this branch) removes the white card. That is an operational deploy step, not a code change.\\\\n\\\\nCommitted as `2105e1c`; worktree is clean. Updated `implementation.md` with the condensed summary, the new screenshot-derived evidence, and the follow-ups. No product source was modified.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394318719,\\\"end\\\":1791394321287\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394416040,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176d848b001r094Jtgu5SvlPl\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176d718a001t1JqfneInDZYQA\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I've independently confirmed the prior analysis. Let me record the re-verification in the implementation summary.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394415755,\\\"end\\\":1791394416029\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394433056,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176dbedf001EnzuI8hOH82HGO\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176db16d001H5Yn2WSbY57nnz\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee893df15ffeq9Fnscoi4bvYur\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I've completed the job. Here's the summary.\\\\n\\\\n## Outcome\\\\n\\\\n**No product code change was required.** The white surface reported on the login page is the auth **card**, and that exact defect was already fixed in the repository before this job's branch.\\\\n\\\\n## What I verified independently (not just taken on trust)\\\\n\\\\n- **Branch check** — worktree is on `feature/create_theme_on_login`... precisely `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`. No checkout needed.\\\\n- **Fix is present in the branch** — `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true. Commit `70f6236` (*\\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\"*) changed the six auth cards from `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\\\\n- **No literal white left on auth routes** — `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none. Remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative (icon plate, toggle knob, score bar, progress bar).\\\\n- **Screenshot decoded objectively** — re-downloaded `iili.io/CZZtpwX.png` (973×989) and decoded the PNG by hand: 89.9% of pixels are the dark Nord page `#353d4a`, and the only light region is one central card `#ebeef4` = Nord's `--color-white`. So the report is the card, not the page body.\\\\n- **Token mapping is render-safe** — `src/styles/tokens.css:24` sets `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff` (light default) and `src/styles/default.css:19` maps it to `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `.dark`, so the swap is pixel-identical in default light/dark and resolves to `#3b4252` under Nord.\\\\n\\\\n**Root cause:** literal `bg-white` + a `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback that never fires under single-mode themes (`ThemeState.apply()` removes the `dark` class for `supportsDarkMode: false`), leaving Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white`. The production symptom is therefore a **stale deploy older than `70f6236`**, not a defect in this branch — an operational step, not code.\\\\n\\\\n## Changes committed\\\\n\\\\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md` — added an \\\\\\\"Independent re-verification\\\\\\\" section recording the checks above.\\\\n- Committed as `712975e [create] implementation: add summary`, plus a session-log commit.\\\\n\\\\n## Limitation\\\\n\\\\n`node_modules` is not installed, so `npm run check/lint/test` and a build+preview render pass could not be run — and per the project hard rule I did not install packages. Since the branch adds no product code relative to `main`, there is no rendering change from this job to verify. The worktree is clean.\\\\n\\\\nThe open item from `tasks.md` (TASK-3, TimePicker) is also already resolved: `TimePicker.svelte` now uses `bg-c-bg-modal` via the same commit.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394430687,\\\"end\\\":1791394433053\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394562710,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176fc0e8001Z7ZEGi79UoEC9V\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176fb3a10014i0HaYjNQEux07\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I've independently verified the situation. Let me summarize my findings before finalizing.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394562280,\\\"end\\\":1791394562708\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394566660,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1176fcb80001r5m63R0X1ZqzO7\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176fc2ed001QochHQnnG8BvvR\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The situation is now fully clear. Let me record the final verification and finish cleanly.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394564992,\\\"end\\\":1791394566658\\n\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1791394582239,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_1177004310013Kwas1YOVzD3dO\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_1176ff921001G61juMixF26mxB\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_ee89228fcffeNbSVRYIVCuZekH\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Done. Here's what I found and did.\\\\n\\\\n## Result: no product-code change was required — the fix is already in this branch\\\\n\\\\n**Branch check:** on `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`. ✅\\\\n\\\\n### Root cause\\\\nThe white surface in the screenshot is the **auth card**, not the page. The cards used literal utilities `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`) removes that class for every single-mode theme (Nord, Skyrim, Catppuccin ×2, Gruvbox, Dracula, Terminal, Paper, Atari). So under Nord the `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback never applied, and `bg-white` resolved to Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`.\\\\n\\\\n### Why nothing needed changing\\\\nThat exact fix already landed on `main` in commit **`70f6236`** (\\\\\\\"nord theme bug with todos\\\\\\\", 2026-08-25) and reached this branch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`. `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true, and `git show 22c5a68:src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte` already shows `bg-c-bg-surface` — i.e. the fix is inherited, not introduced here. All six auth cards now use the semantic token `bg-c-bg-surface`, which is pixel-identical in default light/dark and resolves to Nord `#3b4252`. The production white card is therefore a **stale deploy**, not a code defect.\\\\n\\\\n### Independent verification\\\\n- Decoded the brief screenshot (`iili.io/CZZtpwX.png`, 973×989) with a standalone PNG reader (no vision model): 89.9% `#353d4a` page; light pixels only 6.15%, bbox x 38.4–71.2% / y 34.3–62.5%, colour `#ebeef4` (Nord's `--color-white`); inputs already themed `#454d5e`. The card is the only unthemed surface — and it's fixed.\\\\n- `grep` confirms no `bg-white` remains on auth routes and no `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair exists anywhere under `src/`.\\\\n- TASK-3 (`TimePicker.svelte`) was fixed by the same commit (`bg-c-bg-modal`).\\\\n- I deliberately did **not** apply TASK-2's two secondary substitutions (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9…`, `border-white/5` → token border): the team's own reviewed fix left both in place (they're decorative/inherited), and changing them would alter default-light rendering, violating TASK-2's pixel-identity constraint.\\\\n\\\\n### Commits\\\\n- `0a60b6e` — finalization notes in `implementation.md` + worktree cleanup. Working tree is clean.\\\\n\\\\n### Follow-ups (not in scope)\\\\nDeploy current `main` to production (operational). Inherited open items: pre-paint theme script (FOUC hardening), `html` background rule, account-synced theme, and `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`. Rendered `shot` verification was not possible — `node_modules` is absent and installing packages is against the project's hard rule.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1791394579505,\\\"end\\\":1791394582236\\n\",\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"grep -o '\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\"[^}]*' /workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log | tail -20\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791394615268,\"end\":1791394615301}},\"id\":\"prt_117708f590015AFff5MgYQpVFe\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee88fe25bffe2xhvlL8jpyAcF9\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1177082490010jVgqC7d9CAN6v\"}}\n","exit":0,"truncated":true,"outputPath":"/home/claude/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_1177091f10010SoJWyqEEMqhxz"},"title":"wc -l /workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log; grep -n -i 'reject\\|verdict\\|NEEDS-HUMAN\\|reviewer\\|duplicate' /workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log | tail -30","time":{"start":1791394615628,"end":1791394615806}},"id":"prt_11770901b001R69Pfo8n7SGyJw","sessionID":"ses_ee88fe25bffe2xhvlL8jpyAcF9","messageID":"msg_1177082490010jVgqC7d9CAN6v"}}
