{"type":"text","timestamp":1791394946572,"sessionID":"ses_ee88fe25bffe2xhvlL8jpyAcF9","part":{"id":"prt_1177593ec001rQhySkDrqrMl9z","messageID":"msg_1177587b4001YV1dQ1nQZEXT2N","sessionID":"ses_ee88fe25bffe2xhvlL8jpyAcF9","type":"text","text":"Work complete. Here's the summary.\n\n## Result\n\n**Branch check:** on `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md` (`branch: feature/create_theme-on-login`). ✅\n\n**Root cause (confirmed):** The white surface is the auth **card**, not the page body. The cards used `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`; the `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`) removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false`). Under Nord the fallback never applied, leaving the card at Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`. The report screenshot decodes to 89.9% `#353d4a` page + one `#ebeef4` card — exactly that.\n\n**Why no product code change was needed:** that fix already landed in `main` as `70f6236` (\"nord theme bug with todos\", 2026-08-25) and is an ancestor of this branch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`. All nine auth cards already use `bg-c-bg-surface`; `TimePicker.svelte` already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`; no `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains under `src/`.\n\n## New evidence this pass (the previous 6 passes were static-only)\n\n`node_modules` is genuinely absent (can't build without installing, which is forbidden), so I verified the real deployed app with the globally available Playwright (the engine `shot` uses — `shot` itself can't seed `localStorage`):\n\n- Production app is `https://my.solyto.app` (`solyto.app` is the landing page and 404s).\n- With `theme=nord`: `documentElement.className = \"\"`, card class `… bg-c-bg-surface …`, computed card background **`rgb(59,66,82)` = `#3b4252`**, no white pixels anywhere on the page.\n- Full sweep of default light/dark + all nine single-mode themes: card is dark under every single-mode dark theme; light only under the by-design light themes (`catppuccin-latte`, `paper`, default-light).\n- **This disproves the earlier \"production is a stale deploy\" hypothesis** — prod already serves the fix and renders Nord correctly.\n\n## Deliverables (committed)\n\n- `implementation.md` — rewritten in the requested Summary / Changes / Known-issues format, per-TASK.\n- `notes.md` — added the captured production environment facts (TASK-1) and the hypothesis resolution.\n- `screenshots/` — `prod-login-{nord,default-light,default-dark}.png` + `render-report.md` (sweep table, method, pixel histogram).\n\nWorktree is clean. No `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT` required.\n\n**Follow-up for a human/orchestrator:** this job is a duplicate — it was fixed by `70f6236` before this branch merged `main`, so the branch is docs-only. It should be closed against the existing fix rather than re-run. Inherited out-of-scope items (pre-paint theme script/FOUC, `html` background rule, account-synced theme, `y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`) are listed in `implementation.md`.","time":{"start":1791394943980,"end":1791394946556}}}
