{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791395027561,"sessionID":"ses_ee8897c9dffeMfM78ZrXbxKvA1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_HRf8p1UhyMumH6UZZlpl2905","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/screenshots/render-report.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/screenshots/render-report.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Render report — production `/auth/login` theme sweep\n2: \n3: Produced by the developer during TASK-1/TASK-4 verification (2026-10-07).\n4: \n5: ## Why this is not a `shot` report\n6: \n7: `shot` opens a URL with a fresh browser profile and cannot inject\n8: `localStorage`. The reported defect only appears when `localStorage.theme` is\n9: set to a single-mode theme (`nord`), so `shot` alone cannot reproduce it. The\n10: sweep below was captured with the globally available Playwright\n11: (the same engine `shot` uses) via `context.addInitScript()` so the stored\n12: theme is present before the app boots. The rendered PNGs are byte-identical\n13: to what `shot` would capture for the same theme.\n14: \n15: ## Target\n16: \n17: - Production app: `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login`\n18:   (the app host from `src/lib/config/platform.ts`; `solyto.app` is the\n19:   marketing landing page and 404s on `/auth/login`).\n20: - Viewport 1280x900, Chromium (headless), captured after `networkidle`.\n21: \n22: ## TASK-1 environment facts (production)\n23: \n24: At `theme=nord`, on the deployed login page:\n25: \n26: | fact | value |\n27: | --- | --- |\n28: | `localStorage.getItem('theme')` | `\"nord\"` |\n29: | `document.documentElement.className` | `\"\"` (empty — no `dark` class, as designed for single-mode themes) |\n30: | login card class | `... border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface ...` |\n31: | computed card `background-color` | `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252` |\n32: | computed card `color` | `rgb(216, 222, 233)` = Nord `#d8dee9` |\n33: | `--color-c-bg-surface` | `#3b4252` |\n34: | `--color-white` | `#eceff4` |\n35: | `--color-c-bg` | `#2e3440` |\n36: | `--color-c-neutral` | `#323a49` |\n37: | Nord stylesheet link present | yes (`/themes/nord/nord.css`) |\n38: \n39: **Conclusion:** production already serves the fixed auth-card markup\n40: (`bg-c-bg-surface`) and renders the login page fully Nord-themed. The white\n41: card from `brief.md` is no longer reproducible on production.\n42: \n43: ## Full theme sweep (login card on production)\n44: \n45: | theme | `html.class` | card `background-color` | card luminance | large light surfaces (>3000px², α≥0.5) |\n46: | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n47: | default (light) | *(none)* | `rgb(255,255,255)` | 1.000 | page + card + inputs — expected for a light theme |\n48: | default (dark, `prefers-color-scheme: dark`) | `dark` | `rgb(34,34,34)` | 0.016 | none |\n49: | nord | *(none)* | `rgb(59,66,82)` | 0.054 | none |\n50: | skyrim | *(none)* | `rgba(0,0,0,0)` | n/a | none (theme uses transparent surfaces over its own backdrop) |\n51: | catppuccin-mocha | *(none)* | `rgb(49,50,68)` | 0.034 | none |\n52: | catppuccin-latte | *(none)* | `rgb(230,233,239)` | 0.813 | page + card + inputs — expected for a light theme |\n53: | gruvbox | *(none)* | `rgb(60,56,54)` | 0.041 | none |\n54: | dracula | *(none)* | `rgb(54,55,71)` | 0.040 | none |\n55: | terminal | *(none)* | `rgb(10,26,10)` | 0.008 | none |\n56: | paper | *(none)* | `rgb(243,240,235)` | 0.874 | page + card + inputs — expected for a light theme |\n57: | atari | *(none)* | `rgb(13,0,32)` | 0.002 | none |\n58: \n59: No single-mode dark theme leaves a white/light login card. The three light\n60: themes (`catppuccin-latte`, `paper`, and default-light) are light by design.\n61: \n62: ## Pixel check of the captured artifacts\n63: \n64: `prod-login-nord.png` (1280x900):\n65: \n66: - `#323a49` — 90.64% (page background, Nord `--color-c-neutral`)\n67: - `#3b4252` — 4.84% (login card, Nord `--color-c-bg-surface`)\n68: - `#434c5e` — 1.63% (inputs, Nord `--color-c-bg-elevated`)\n69: - `#4c566a` — 0.85% (button, Nord `--color-c-btn`)\n70: - **no white/near-white pixels**\n71: \n72: ## Files\n73: \n74: - `prod-login-nord.png` — reported case, now correct\n75: - `prod-login-default-light.png` — light-theme regression reference\n76: - `prod-login-default-dark.png` — dark-theme regression reference\n\n(End of file - total 76 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Render report — production `/auth/login` theme sweep\n\nProduced by the developer during TASK-1/TASK-4 verification (2026-10-07).\n\n## Why this is not a `shot` report\n\n`shot` opens a URL with a fresh browser profile and cannot inject\n`localStorage`. The reported defect only appears when `localStorage.theme` is\nset to a single-mode theme (`nord`), so `shot` alone cannot reproduce it. The\nsweep below was captured with the globally available Playwright\n(the same engine `shot` uses) via `context.addInitScript()` so the stored\ntheme is present before the app boots. The rendered PNGs are byte-identical\nto what `shot` would capture for the same theme.\n\n## Target\n\n- Production app: `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login`\n  (the app host from `src/lib/config/platform.ts`; `solyto.app` is the\n  marketing landing page and 404s on `/auth/login`).\n- Viewport 1280x900, Chromium (headless), captured after `networkidle`.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/screenshots/render-report.md","text":"# Render report — production `/auth/login` theme sweep\n\nProduced by the developer during TASK-1/TASK-4 verification (2026-10-07).\n\n## Why this is not a `shot` report\n\n`shot` opens a URL with a fresh browser profile and cannot inject\n`localStorage`. The reported defect only appears when `localStorage.theme` is\nset to a single-mode theme (`nord`), so `shot` alone cannot reproduce it. The\nsweep below was captured with the globally available Playwright\n(the same engine `shot` uses) via `context.addInitScript()` so the stored\ntheme is present before the app boots. The rendered PNGs are byte-identical\nto what `shot` would capture for the same theme.\n\n## Target\n\n- Production app: `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login`\n  (the app host from `src/lib/config/platform.ts`; `solyto.app` is the\n  marketing landing page and 404s on `/auth/login`).\n- Viewport 1280x900, Chromium (headless), captured after `networkidle`.\n\n## TASK-1 environment facts (production)\n\nAt `theme=nord`, on the deployed login page:\n\n| fact | value |\n| --- | --- |\n| `localStorage.getItem('theme')` | `\"nord\"` |\n| `document.documentElement.className` | `\"\"` (empty — no `dark` class, as designed for single-mode themes) |\n| login card class | `... border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface ...` |\n| computed card `background-color` | `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252` |\n| computed card `color` | `rgb(216, 222, 233)` = Nord `#d8dee9` |\n| `--color-c-bg-surface` | `#3b4252` |\n| `--color-white` | `#eceff4` |\n| `--color-c-bg` | `#2e3440` |\n| `--color-c-neutral` | `#323a49` |\n| Nord stylesheet link present | yes (`/themes/nord/nord.css`) |\n\n**Conclusion:** production already serves the fixed auth-card markup\n(`bg-c-bg-surface`) and renders the login page fully Nord-themed. The white\ncard from `brief.md` is no longer reproducible on production.\n\n## Full theme sweep (login card on production)\n\n| theme | `html.class` | card `background-color` | card luminance | large light surfaces (>3000px², α≥0.5) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| default (light) | *(none)* | `rgb(255,255,255)` | 1.000 | page + card + inputs — expected for a light theme |\n| default (dark, `prefers-color-scheme: dark`) | `dark` | `rgb(34,34,34)` | 0.016 | none |\n| nord | *(none)* | `rgb(59,66,82)` | 0.054 | none |\n| skyrim | *(none)* | `rgba(0,0,0,0)` | n/a | none (theme uses transparent surfaces over its own backdrop) |\n| catppuccin-mocha | *(none)* | `rgb(49,50,68)` | 0.034 | none |\n| catppuccin-latte | *(none)* | `rgb(230,233,239)` | 0.813 | page + card + inputs — expected for a light theme |\n| gruvbox | *(none)* | `rgb(60,56,54)` | 0.041 | none |\n| dracula | *(none)* | `rgb(54,55,71)` | 0.040 | none |\n| terminal | *(none)* | `rgb(10,26,10)` | 0.008 | none |\n| paper | *(none)* | `rgb(243,240,235)` | 0.874 | page + card + inputs — expected for a light theme |\n| atari | *(none)* | `rgb(13,0,32)` | 0.002 | none |\n\nNo single-mode dark theme leaves a white/light login card. The three light\nthemes (`catppuccin-latte`, `paper`, and default-light) are light by design.\n\n## Pixel check of the captured artifacts\n\n`prod-login-nord.png` (1280x900):\n\n- `#323a49` — 90.64% (page background, Nord `--color-c-neutral`)\n- `#3b4252` — 4.84% (login card, Nord `--color-c-bg-surface`)\n- `#434c5e` — 1.63% (inputs, Nord `--color-c-bg-elevated`)\n- `#4c566a` — 0.85% (button, Nord `--color-c-btn`)\n- **no white/near-white pixels**\n\n## Files\n\n- `prod-login-nord.png` — reported case, now correct\n- `prod-login-default-light.png` — light-theme regression reference\n- `prod-login-default-dark.png` — dark-theme regression reference","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":76,"totalLines":76,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/screenshots/render-report.md","time":{"start":1791395027467,"end":1791395027551}},"id":"prt_11776d9c4001PMT4PFp3E7XFqZ","sessionID":"ses_ee8897c9dffeMfM78ZrXbxKvA1","messageID":"msg_11776c111001su7F2Or04jPAcU"}}
