{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791395057831,"sessionID":"ses_ee8897c9dffeMfM78ZrXbxKvA1","part":{"id":"prt_1177750a4001P6Tdd20nknBthb","messageID":"msg_117774c28001ndt2OJeXKGUgyM","sessionID":"ses_ee8897c9dffeMfM78ZrXbxKvA1","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1791395063755,"sessionID":"ses_ee8897c9dffeMfM78ZrXbxKvA1","part":{"id":"prt_117775e7b00124EwQ59wclRWMB","messageID":"msg_117774c28001ndt2OJeXKGUgyM","sessionID":"ses_ee8897c9dffeMfM78ZrXbxKvA1","type":"text","text":"The job is complete and was already resolved before this session. Here's what I found and did.\n\n## What the issue was\n\nThe white surface in the report screenshot was the **auth card**, not the page body and not a late/failed theme load. The cards used the literal utilities `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`) explicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). Under Nord the themed fallback `dark:bg-s-dark-2` never applied, so the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`.\n\n## Current state — already fixed upstream\n\nCommit `70f6236` (\"nord theme bug with todos\", 2026-08-25) swept the literal-white surfaces to semantic tokens. Verified independently this session:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 main` → yes; the fix is in `main`.\n- `git diff main...HEAD -- src/` → **empty**: this branch adds no product source change.\n- All nine auth card blocks already carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44); `grep bg-white src/routes/auth/` → none.\n- `TimePicker.svelte` already uses `bg-c-bg-modal` (TASK-3 also resolved).\n\nThe analyst's `tasks.md` (rev 4) predates that fix and is stale; the prior developer captured production facts with Playwright against `https://my.solyto.app` (theme sweep in `screenshots/render-report.md`). Under `theme=nord`, production renders the login card as `rgb(59,66,82)` = Nord `#3b4252` with no white pixels, which also disproves the \"version skew / stale deploy\" hypothesis. `implementation.md` and `notes.md` already document all of this.\n\n## Action taken this session\n\nNo product code change was needed (any change to the already-correct auth classes would be unnecessary churn). I confirmed the tree state and committed the only remaining dirty files (the harness-owned `session.log` / `tokens.json`) so the worktree is clean:\n\n- `1fef8cb [create] chore: sync session artifacts`\n\n`implementation.md` is already present, accurate, and committed, so no redundant summary commit was made.\n\n## Limitation (unchanged, not blocking)\n\n`npm run check` / `lint` / `test` / `build` / `preview` could not be run: `node_modules` is not installed, and the project hard rule forbids installing packages without asking. With no product source diff, there is nothing new for those commands to check.","time":{"start":1791395061371,"end":1791395063746}}}
