{"type":"text","timestamp":1791395240511,"sessionID":"ses_ee8866beeffeo6mxUr2u0AoCTl","part":{"id":"prt_1177a1071001SIt6lfJnBaltXE","messageID":"msg_1177a08050014Vwznh1yj8AKVI","sessionID":"ses_ee8866beeffeo6mxUr2u0AoCTl","type":"text","text":"The job at `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login` is already fully resolved. I verified the state independently rather than re-doing work that prior passes completed.\n\n## What I found\n\n**Branch check:** `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches the `branch:` field in `brief.md`. ✅\n\n**Root cause (from `brief.md`):** the white surface on the login page is the auth **card**, whose markup used literal `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. `ThemeState.apply()` strips the `dark` class for single-mode themes (`supportsDarkMode: false` — nord, skyrim, catppuccin, gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari), so the `dark:` fallback never fires and the card stays at Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`.\n\n**Already fixed, not by this branch:** commit `70f6236` (job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`) swept those literals to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token. It is an ancestor of this branch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`.\n\n## Independent verification\n\n- `git diff main...HEAD --stat -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` → **empty** (branch contributes docs only).\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true.\n- All nine auth card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72/100, reset-password:72/85/105, logout:27, verify:44).\n- `grep 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → no matches. Remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative (IconPlate dots, Toggle knob, ScoreBar highlight), as noted in `implementation.md`.\n- Production was measured directly in a prior pass (`screenshots/render-report.md`): under `theme=nord` the card renders `rgb(59,66,82)` = Nord `#3b4252`, no white pixels. The stale-deploy hypothesis is disproven.\n\n`npm run check/lint/test` cannot run here because `node_modules` is absent and the project forbids installing packages without approval; with no product diff there is nothing new for them to check (documented in `implementation.md`).\n\n## Action taken\n\nNo product code change was warranted. I committed the two leftover session artifacts (`session.log`, `tokens.json`) to leave the worktree clean. The existing `implementation.md` already documents the resolution and re-verification, so I did not duplicate it.\n\nWorking tree is clean; no push/merge performed.","time":{"start":1791395238001,"end":1791395240503}}}
