{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791395433855,"sessionID":"ses_ee88329d0ffeLjdpCf63m0P8Mc","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_EgLKsNuW6ZInRZlhs19A8342","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ## Summary\n2: \n3: The white surface reported in `brief.md` was the auth **card**, not the page\n4: body and not a late/failed theme load. The cards used the literal utilities\n5: `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has\n6: the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\n7: explicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme\n8: (`supportsDarkMode: false`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox,\n9: dracula, terminal, paper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2`\n10: fallback therefore never applied and the card stayed at Nord's deliberately\n11: near-white `--color-white: #eceff4` — exactly the `#ebeef4` card in the report\n12: screenshot, on an otherwise-Nord `#353d4a` page (both values are the screenshot's\n13: slightly colour-managed renditions of Nord `#eceff4` / `#323a49`).\n14: \n15: That defect is **already fixed in this branch and in `main`**. Commit `70f6236`\n16: (\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\n17: swept the literal-white surfaces to semantic tokens; the auth cards became\n18: `bg-c-bg-surface` and `TimePicker.svelte` became `bg-c-bg-modal`. It reached this\n19: branch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`, so `git diff main...HEAD` is docs-only and\n20: no product source change was required.\n21: \n22: This pass adds the missing objective evidence: production was measured directly\n23: and **already runs the fixed markup** — a browser probe of\n24: `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` with `theme=nord` renders the card as\n25: `rgb(59,66,82)` (`#3b4252`), with no white pixels on the page. The earlier\n26: \"production is a stale deploy older than `70f6236`\" hypothesis is disproven.\n27: \n28: ## Changes\n29: \n30: TASK-1: Captured the previously-missing environment facts against the real\n31:   production app (`my.solyto.app`) with Playwright (the engine `shot` uses,\n32:   used because `shot` cannot seed `localStorage`). Under `theme=nord`:\n33:   `localStorage.theme = \"nord\"`, `documentElement.className = \"\"`,\n34:   card class includes `bg-c-bg-surface`, computed card background\n35:   `rgb(59,66,82)`. A full theme sweep and three reference screenshots are in\n36:   `screenshots/` (`render-report.md`). Recorded in `notes.md`.\n37:   No product code changed.\n38: \n39: TASK-2: No change needed. All nine auth card blocks already carry the requested\n40:   `bg-c-bg-surface` (`login:110`, `register:92`, `forgot-password:72,100`,\n41:   `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`, `verify/...:44`), and\n42:   `--color-c-bg-surface` maps to `#ffffff` in default light,\n43:   `var(--color-s-dark-2)` in default dark (pixel-identical to the old\n44:   `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`), and `#3b4252` under Nord. The two secondary\n45:   substitutions in the task were deliberately **not** applied:\n46:   - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: the labels already\n47:     inherit a correctly themed colour from `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte`\n48:     (`text-c-neutral-8` = Nord `#d8dee9`, ≈7:1 contrast on `#3b4252`). Adding an\n49:     explicit light-mode token would change default-light rendering\n50:     (`c-neutral-8` → `c-neutral-9`), which TASK-2 says must stay pixel-identical.\n51:   - `border-white/5` → token border: no target token was specified, and the\n52:     available `--color-c-border` is transparent / not overridden by Nord, so a\n53:     blind swap would remove the card outline. The accepted upstream fix\n54:     (`70f6236`) left this decorative border untouched.\n55: \n56: TASK-3: Resolved (no change). `src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte`\n57:   already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`, fixed by the same `70f6236` sweep. No\n58:   `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains anywhere under `src/`; the eight\n59:   remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative (IconPlate, Toggle knob, ScoreBar,\n60:   Progress).\n61: \n62: TASK-4: Rendered verification completed against production (which is\n63:   byte-for-byte the auth-card markup this branch contains, since the branch has\n64:   no product diff). Swept default light, default dark and all nine single-mode\n65:   themes; the login card is dark under every single-mode dark theme and no\n66:   unexpected light surface (>3000px²) appears. `npm run check` / `lint` / `test`\n67:   could not be run because `node_modules` is not installed and the project hard\n68:   rule forbids installing packages without asking; with no product diff there is\n69:   nothing new for them to check. Full table in\n70:   `screenshots/render-report.md`.\n71: \n72: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n73: \n74: - The job is a duplicate: the defect was already fixed by `70f6236` before this\n75:   branch's `main` merge. Product behaviour needs no change; the resolution is to\n76:   close this job against the existing fix.\n77: - `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale: it was written before the\n78:   `70f6236` merge and describes the pre-fix auth-card classes. Left as the\n79:   analyst's artifact; the corrected picture is here and in `notes.md`.\n80: - Inherited open items (out of scope): pre-paint theme script / FOUC hardening\n81:   (there is still a brief flash of the light default on first paint for\n82:   single-mode themes, because `theme.load()` runs in `onMount`), an `html`\n83:   background-color rule, account-synced theme setting, and\n84:   `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` existing on disk but missing from `themes.ts`.\n85: - Cosmetic consistency (not applied): auth labels use bare `dark:text-white`\n86:   while the rest of the app mostly uses `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`.\n87: - Same bug class, out of this job's auth scope: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Progress.svelte`\n88:   still uses `not-dark:bg-white`, which renders white under single-mode dark\n89:   themes (`.dark` is absent) — candidate for a follow-up identical to TASK-3.\n90: \n91: ## Independent re-verification (final developer pass, 2026-10-07)\n92: \n93: Re-confirmed the resolution from a clean checkout of this branch:\n94: \n95: - `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true (the fix is in this branch).\n96: - `git diff main...HEAD --stat -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` → empty, so\n97:   this branch contributes no product source change relative to `main`.\n98: - `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → no matches; all six auth\n99:   cards carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (`login:110`, `register:92`,\n100:   `forgot-password:72,100`, `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`,\n101:   `verify/...:44`).\n102: - `npm run check` / `lint` / `test` still cannot run because `node_modules` is\n103:   not installed and the project forbids installing packages without approval.\n104: \n105: No code was changed; this pass only records the re-verification.\n106: \n107: Additional text-legibility check (2026-10-07): because `dark:text-white` never\n108: fires under single-mode themes, the auth labels inherit `text-c-neutral-8` from\n109: `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte`. Confirmed this stays readable everywhere:\n110: Nord/dracula/gruvbox/skyrim/catppuccin-mocha override `--color-c-neutral-7/8/9`\n111: explicitly, `atari` and `terminal` override the whole `--color-gray-*` palette\n112: (e.g. atari `gray-800: #cc88ee`, terminal `gray-800: #00dd00`), and the light\n113: themes (`paper`, `catppuccin-latte`) fall back to the base dark\n114: `--color-gray-800`. No low-contrast label case found.\n\n(End of file - total 114 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"## Summary\n\nThe white surface reported in `brief.md` was the auth **card**, not the page\nbody and not a late/failed theme load. The cards used the literal utilities\n`bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has\nthe `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\nexplicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme\n(`supportsDarkMode: false`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox,\ndracula, terminal, paper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2`\nfallback therefore never applied and the card stayed at Nord's deliberately\nnear-white `--color-white: #eceff4` — exactly the `#ebeef4` card in the report\nscreenshot, on an otherwise-Nord `#353d4a` page (both values are the screenshot's\nslightly colour-managed renditions of Nord `#eceff4` / `#323a49`).\n\nThat defect is **already fixed in this branch and in `main`**. Commit `70f6236`\n(\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\nswept the literal-white surfaces to semantic tokens; the auth cards became\n`bg-c-bg-surface` and `TimePicker.svelte` became `bg-c-bg-modal`. It reached this\nbranch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`, so `git diff main...HEAD` is docs-only and\nno product source change was required.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","text":"## Summary\n\nThe white surface reported in `brief.md` was the auth **card**, not the page\nbody and not a late/failed theme load. The cards used the literal utilities\n`bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has\nthe `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\nexplicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme\n(`supportsDarkMode: false`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox,\ndracula, terminal, paper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2`\nfallback therefore never applied and the card stayed at Nord's deliberately\nnear-white `--color-white: #eceff4` — exactly the `#ebeef4` card in the report\nscreenshot, on an otherwise-Nord `#353d4a` page (both values are the screenshot's\nslightly colour-managed renditions of Nord `#eceff4` / `#323a49`).\n\nThat defect is **already fixed in this branch and in `main`**. Commit `70f6236`\n(\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\nswept the literal-white surfaces to semantic tokens; the auth cards became\n`bg-c-bg-surface` and `TimePicker.svelte` became `bg-c-bg-modal`. It reached this\nbranch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`, so `git diff main...HEAD` is docs-only and\nno product source change was required.\n\nThis pass adds the missing objective evidence: production was measured directly\nand **already runs the fixed markup** — a browser probe of\n`https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` with `theme=nord` renders the card as\n`rgb(59,66,82)` (`#3b4252`), with no white pixels on the page. The earlier\n\"production is a stale deploy older than `70f6236`\" hypothesis is disproven.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: Captured the previously-missing environment facts against the real\n  production app (`my.solyto.app`) with Playwright (the engine `shot` uses,\n  used because `shot` cannot seed `localStorage`). Under `theme=nord`:\n  `localStorage.theme = \"nord\"`, `documentElement.className = \"\"`,\n  card class includes `bg-c-bg-surface`, computed card background\n  `rgb(59,66,82)`. A full theme sweep and three reference screenshots are in\n  `screenshots/` (`render-report.md`). Recorded in `notes.md`.\n  No product code changed.\n\nTASK-2: No change needed. All nine auth card blocks already carry the requested\n  `bg-c-bg-surface` (`login:110`, `register:92`, `forgot-password:72,100`,\n  `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`, `verify/...:44`), and\n  `--color-c-bg-surface` maps to `#ffffff` in default light,\n  `var(--color-s-dark-2)` in default dark (pixel-identical to the old\n  `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`), and `#3b4252` under Nord. The two secondary\n  substitutions in the task were deliberately **not** applied:\n  - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: the labels already\n    inherit a correctly themed colour from `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte`\n    (`text-c-neutral-8` = Nord `#d8dee9`, ≈7:1 contrast on `#3b4252`). Adding an\n    explicit light-mode token would change default-light rendering\n    (`c-neutral-8` → `c-neutral-9`), which TASK-2 says must stay pixel-identical.\n  - `border-white/5` → token border: no target token was specified, and the\n    available `--color-c-border` is transparent / not overridden by Nord, so a\n    blind swap would remove the card outline. The accepted upstream fix\n    (`70f6236`) left this decorative border untouched.\n\nTASK-3: Resolved (no change). `src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte`\n  already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`, fixed by the same `70f6236` sweep. No\n  `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains anywhere under `src/`; the eight\n  remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative (IconPlate, Toggle knob, ScoreBar,\n  Progress).\n\nTASK-4: Rendered verification completed against production (which is\n  byte-for-byte the auth-card markup this branch contains, since the branch has\n  no product diff). Swept default light, default dark and all nine single-mode\n  themes; the login card is dark under every single-mode dark theme and no\n  unexpected light surface (>3000px²) appears. `npm run check` / `lint` / `test`\n  could not be run because `node_modules` is not installed and the project hard\n  rule forbids installing packages without asking; with no product diff there is\n  nothing new for them to check. Full table in\n  `screenshots/render-report.md`.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- The job is a duplicate: the defect was already fixed by `70f6236` before this\n  branch's `main` merge. Product behaviour needs no change; the resolution is to\n  close this job against the existing fix.\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale: it was written before the\n  `70f6236` merge and describes the pre-fix auth-card classes. Left as the\n  analyst's artifact; the corrected picture is here and in `notes.md`.\n- Inherited open items (out of scope): pre-paint theme script / FOUC hardening\n  (there is still a brief flash of the light default on first paint for\n  single-mode themes, because `theme.load()` runs in `onMount`), an `html`\n  background-color rule, account-synced theme setting, and\n  `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` existing on disk but missing from `themes.ts`.\n- Cosmetic consistency (not applied): auth labels use bare `dark:text-white`\n  while the rest of the app mostly uses `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`.\n- Same bug class, out of this job's auth scope: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Progress.svelte`\n  still uses `not-dark:bg-white`, which renders white under single-mode dark\n  themes (`.dark` is absent) — candidate for a follow-up identical to TASK-3.\n\n## Independent re-verification (final developer pass, 2026-10-07)\n\nRe-confirmed the resolution from a clean checkout of this branch:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true (the fix is in this branch).\n- `git diff main...HEAD --stat -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` → empty, so\n  this branch contributes no product source change relative to `main`.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → no matches; all six auth\n  cards carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (`login:110`, `register:92`,\n  `forgot-password:72,100`, `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`,\n  `verify/...:44`).\n- `npm run check` / `lint` / `test` still cannot run because `node_modules` is\n  not installed and the project forbids installing packages without approval.\n\nNo code was changed; this pass only records the re-verification.\n\nAdditional text-legibility check (2026-10-07): because `dark:text-white` never\nfires under single-mode themes, the auth labels inherit `text-c-neutral-8` from\n`src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte`. Confirmed this stays readable everywhere:\nNord/dracula/gruvbox/skyrim/catppuccin-mocha override `--color-c-neutral-7/8/9`\nexplicitly, `atari` and `terminal` override the whole `--color-gray-*` palette\n(e.g. atari `gray-800: #cc88ee`, terminal `gray-800: #00dd00`), and the light\nthemes (`paper`, `catppuccin-latte`) fall back to the base dark\n`--color-gray-800`. No low-contrast label case found.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":114,"totalLines":114,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791395433826,"end":1791395433848}},"id":"prt_1177d0d1d001S35qu14Lznhyy1","sessionID":"ses_ee88329d0ffeLjdpCf63m0P8Mc","messageID":"msg_1177d04aa001lCDJnU03xgUmwE"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791395433961,"sessionID":"ses_ee88329d0ffeLjdpCf63m0P8Mc","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_aXKSz6zeOMoHO9BoErH66886","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/verdict.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/verdict.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Verdict: theme on login\n2: \n3: id: create\n4: status: open\n5: reviewer:\n6: date:\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n9: \n10: ## Review\n11: \n12: <!-- TASK-1: PASS / FAIL / PARTIAL\n13:      notes: ...\n14: \n15: TASK-2: ...\n16: -->\n17: \n18: ## Security\n19: \n20: <!-- Any security findings from @security, or \"none\" if not run. -->\n21: \n22: ## Overall\n23: \n24: <!-- APPROVED / REJECTED / NEEDS WORK -->\n25: <!-- Summary of what needs to change before this can be approved, if anything. -->\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Verdict: theme on login\n\nid: create\nstatus: open\nreviewer:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\n<!-- TASK-1: PASS / FAIL / PARTIAL\n     notes: ...\n\nTASK-2: ...\n-->\n\n## Security\n\n<!-- Any security findings from @security, or \"none\" if not run. -->","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/verdict.md","text":"# Verdict: theme on login\n\nid: create\nstatus: open\nreviewer:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\n<!-- TASK-1: PASS / FAIL / PARTIAL\n     notes: ...\n\nTASK-2: ...\n-->\n\n## Security\n\n<!-- Any security findings from @security, or \"none\" if not run. -->\n\n## Overall\n\n<!-- APPROVED / REJECTED / NEEDS WORK -->\n<!-- Summary of what needs to change before this can be approved, if anything. -->","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":25,"totalLines":25,"truncated":false}},"title":"do