{"type":"text","timestamp":1791395488491,"sessionID":"ses_ee88329d0ffeLjdpCf63m0P8Mc","part":{"id":"prt_1177dd905001ME3yziYLEd9x7T","messageID":"msg_1177dd19b001yaopMXoNV95d6o","sessionID":"ses_ee88329d0ffeLjdpCf63m0P8Mc","type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI worked the job `create_theme-on-login` on branch `feature/create_theme-on-login` (matches `brief.md`). The result is a **confirmed no-op**: the defect described in the brief was already fixed before this job's work.\n\n### What I found\n\n- **Root cause (matches the analyst):** auth cards used the literal `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. Single-mode themes (`supportsDarkMode: false`, incl. Nord) cause `ThemeState.apply()` to remove the `dark` class, so the `dark:` escape hatch never fires and the card stays at Nord's near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`.\n- **The fix is already present:** commit `70f6236` (\"nord theme bug with todos\", 2026-08-25) swept the literal-white surfaces to semantic tokens. I verified `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true.\n- `git diff main...HEAD` is **docs-only** — this branch contributes no product source change relative to `main`.\n- No `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains anywhere under `src/`; all nine auth card blocks (`login:110`, `register:92`, `forgot-password:72,100`, `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`, `verify/...:44`) carry `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n- `TimePicker.svelte` (TASK-3) already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\n- `--color-c-bg-surface` maps to `#ffffff` (default light), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` (default dark, pixel-identical to the old classes), and `#3b4252` (Nord) — exactly what TASK-2 asked for.\n\n### What I changed\n\nNo product code. I re-confirmed the resolution and committed the harness session artifacts so the worktree is clean. `implementation.md`, `notes.md`, and `screenshots/render-report.md` (production probe showing the Nord card as `rgb(59,66,82)` with no white pixels) already documented this; I did not duplicate them.\n\n### Notes\n\n- The two secondary TASK-2 substitutions (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`, `border-white/5` → token border) were deliberately not applied by the prior pass: adding `text-c-neutral-9` would change default-light text from `gray-800` to `gray-900`, violating TASK-2's own \"keep default light/dark pixel-identical\" constraint, and no safe token was specified for the decorative border. I agree with that call.\n- TASK-3 was flagged optional / needs owner go-ahead; in an unattended session I did not undertake it, and it is already fixed regardless.\n- `npm run check/lint/test/build/preview` cannot run here: `node_modules` is absent and the project forbids installing packages without asking. With no product diff there is nothing new for them to check.\n- Resolution: close this job as a duplicate of the existing `70f6236` fix.\n\nWorktree left clean (branch tip `db245a9`).","time":{"start":1791395485957,"end":1791395488486}}}
