{"type":"text","timestamp":1791395579875,"sessionID":"ses_ee8820ea8ffeQqZi1ggiqgN3qb","part":{"id":"prt_1177f3bf1001NvP1NDkyHcA6P8","messageID":"msg_1177f1d7f001xuQw36bIPztWVO","sessionID":"ses_ee8820ea8ffeQqZi1ggiqgN3qb","type":"text","text":"Worktree is clean and the resolution is committed. Here's the outcome.\n\n## Summary\n\nI read `brief.md`, `tasks.md`, and the branch state, then independently verified the prior passes' conclusion.\n\n**Finding: the reported bug is already fixed in this branch — no product code change is required or appropriate.**\n\nThe brief's white login surface was the auth **card**, which used the literal utilities `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` Tailwind variant only fires when `<html>` carries the `dark` class, but single-mode themes (`supportsDarkMode: false` — nord, skyrim, catppuccin-*, gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari) make `ThemeState.apply()` explicitly remove that class (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts`). So under Nord the card fell back to Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`.\n\nThat exact defect was fixed in `main` by commit `70f6236` (\"nord theme bug with todos\", job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`), which I confirmed changed `src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte` and `register/+page.svelte` from `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`, and `TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`. It reached this branch via the `main` merge.\n\n### Evidence I re-verified this session\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true (fix is in the branch).\n- `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` → empty (no product diff).\n- All nine auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`: login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify/…:44.\n- No `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark*` pair remains anywhere under `src/`.\n- `nord.css` overrides `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252` and the page wrapper's `--color-c-neutral: #323a49`, so the whole login page is themed under Nord.\n\nI deliberately **did not** apply TASK-2's two secondary substitutions (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`, and `border-white/5` → token border): the labels already inherit a correctly themed, readable `text-c-neutral-8`, and adding an explicit light-mode token would change default-light rendering, violating the task's own \"pixel-identical\" constraint. No suitable border token exists (`--color-c-border` is transparent), so a blind swap would drop the card outline.\n\n### Changes\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md` — appended a \"Final confirmation pass\" recording the re-verification.\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log`, `tokens.json` — committed remaining agent artifacts to leave the worktree clean.\n\nNo commits touch product source, because the fix is already present.\n\n### Known issues / follow-ups (out of scope, already tracked)\n- TASK-4's `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` could not be run: `node_modules` is absent and the project forbids installing packages without asking. With no product diff there is nothing new for them to check.\n- Inherited items noted by earlier passes: pre-paint theme script (FOUC), `html` background rule, account-synced theme, `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`, and `Progress.svelte`'s `not-dark:bg-white` as the same bug class outside auth scope.\n\nBranch: `feature/create_theme-on-login` (matches `brief.md`). Working tree clean. Not pushed/merged, per hard rules.","time":{"start":1791395576817,"end":1791395579869}}}
