{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791395596598,"sessionID":"ses_ee880a7b0ffeIqckXNvh7zeCm7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_m4IZnrPmIAXJJE2NTcTH3041","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ## Summary\n2: \n3: The white surface reported in `brief.md` was the auth **card**, not the page\n4: body and not a late/failed theme load. The cards used the literal utilities\n5: `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has\n6: the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\n7: explicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme\n8: (`supportsDarkMode: false`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox,\n9: dracula, terminal, paper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2`\n10: fallback therefore never applied and the card stayed at Nord's deliberately\n11: near-white `--color-white: #eceff4` — exactly the `#ebeef4` card in the report\n12: screenshot, on an otherwise-Nord `#353d4a` page (both values are the screenshot's\n13: slightly colour-managed renditions of Nord `#eceff4` / `#323a49`).\n14: \n15: That defect is **already fixed in this branch and in `main`**. Commit `70f6236`\n16: (\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\n17: swept the literal-white surfaces to semantic tokens; the auth cards became\n18: `bg-c-bg-surface` and `TimePicker.svelte` became `bg-c-bg-modal`. It reached this\n19: branch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`, so `git diff main...HEAD` is docs-only and\n20: no product source change was required.\n21: \n22: This pass adds the missing objective evidence: production was measured directly\n23: and **already runs the fixed markup** — a browser probe of\n24: `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` with `theme=nord` renders the card as\n25: `rgb(59,66,82)` (`#3b4252`), with no white pixels on the page. The earlier\n26: \"production is a stale deploy older than `70f6236`\" hypothesis is disproven.\n27: \n28: ## Changes\n29: \n30: TASK-1: Captured the previously-missing environment facts against the real\n31:   production app (`my.solyto.app`) with Playwright (the engine `shot` uses,\n32:   used because `shot` cannot seed `localStorage`). Under `theme=nord`:\n33:   `localStorage.theme = \"nord\"`, `documentElement.className = \"\"`,\n34:   card class includes `bg-c-bg-surface`, computed card background\n35:   `rgb(59,66,82)`. A full theme sweep and three reference screenshots are in\n36:   `screenshots/` (`render-report.md`). Recorded in `notes.md`.\n37:   No product code changed.\n38: \n39: TASK-2: No change needed. All nine auth card blocks already carry the requested\n40:   `bg-c-bg-surface` (`login:110`, `register:92`, `forgot-password:72,100`,\n41:   `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`, `verify/...:44`), and\n42:   `--color-c-bg-surface` maps to `#ffffff` in default light,\n43:   `var(--color-s-dark-2)` in default dark (pixel-identical to the old\n44:   `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`), and `#3b4252` under Nord. The two secondary\n45:   substitutions in the task were deliberately **not** applied:\n46:   - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: the labels already\n47:     inherit a correctly themed colour from `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte`\n48:     (`text-c-neutral-8` = Nord `#d8dee9`, ≈7:1 contrast on `#3b4252`). Adding an\n49:     explicit light-mode token would change default-light rendering\n50:     (`c-neutral-8` → `c-neutral-9`), which TASK-2 says must stay pixel-identical.\n51:   - `border-white/5` → token border: no target token was specified, and the\n52:     available `--color-c-border` is transparent / not overridden by Nord, so a\n53:     blind swap would remove the card outline. The accepted upstream fix\n54:     (`70f6236`) left this decorative border untouched.\n55: \n56: TASK-3: Resolved (no change). `src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte`\n57:   already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`, fixed by the same `70f6236` sweep. No\n58:   `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains anywhere under `src/`; the eight\n59:   remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative (IconPlate, Toggle knob, ScoreBar,\n60:   Progress).\n61: \n62: TASK-4: Rendered verification completed against production (which is\n63:   byte-for-byte the auth-card markup this branch contains, since the branch has\n64:   no product diff). Swept default light, default dark and all nine single-mode\n65:   themes; the login card is dark under every single-mode dark theme and no\n66:   unexpected light surface (>3000px²) appears. `npm run check` / `lint` / `test`\n67:   could not be run because `node_modules` is not installed and the project hard\n68:   rule forbids installing packages without asking; with no product diff there is\n69:   nothing new for them to check. Full table in\n70:   `screenshots/render-report.md`.\n71: \n72: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n73: \n74: - The job is a duplicate: the defect was already fixed by `70f6236` before this\n75:   branch's `main` merge. Product behaviour needs no change; the resolution is to\n76:   close this job against the existing fix.\n77: - `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale: it was written before the\n78:   `70f6236` merge and describes the pre-fix auth-card classes. Left as the\n79:   analyst's artifact; the corrected picture is here and in `notes.md`.\n80: - Inherited open items (out of scope): pre-paint theme script / FOUC hardening\n81:   (there is still a brief flash of the light default on first paint for\n82:   single-mode themes, because `theme.load()` runs in `onMount`), an `html`\n83:   background-color rule, account-synced theme setting, and\n84:   `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` existing on disk but missing from `themes.ts`.\n85: - Cosmetic consistency (not applied): auth labels use bare `dark:text-white`\n86:   while the rest of the app mostly uses `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`.\n87: - Same bug class, out of this job's auth scope: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Progress.svelte`\n88:   still uses `not-dark:bg-white`, which renders white under single-mode dark\n89:   themes (`.dark` is absent) — candidate for a follow-up identical to TASK-3.\n90: \n91: ## Independent re-verification (final developer pass, 2026-10-07)\n92: \n93: Re-confirmed the resolution from a clean checkout of this branch:\n94: \n95: - `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true (the fix is in this branch).\n96: - `git diff main...HEAD --stat -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` → empty, so\n97:   this branch contributes no product source change relative to `main`.\n98: - `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → no matches; all six auth\n99:   cards carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (`login:110`, `register:92`,\n100:   `forgot-password:72,100`, `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`,\n101:   `verify/...:44`).\n102: - `npm run check` / `lint` / `test` still cannot run because `node_modules` is\n103:   not installed and the project forbids installing packages without approval.\n104: \n105: No code was changed; this pass only records the re-verification.\n106: \n107: Additional text-legibility check (2026-10-07): because `dark:text-white` never\n108: fires under single-mode themes, the auth labels inherit `text-c-neutral-8` from\n109: `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte`. Confirmed this stays readable everywhere:\n110: Nord/dracula/gruvbox/skyrim/catppuccin-mocha override `--color-c-neutral-7/8/9`\n111: explicitly, `atari` and `terminal` override the whole `--color-gray-*` palette\n112: (e.g. atari `gray-800: #cc88ee`, terminal `gray-800: #00dd00`), and the light\n113: themes (`paper`, `catppuccin-latte`) fall back to the base dark\n114: `--color-gray-800`. No low-contrast label case found.\n115: \n116: ## Final confirmation pass (2026-10-07, developer)\n117: \n118: Re-verified from this checkout, no product change:\n119: `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true;\n120: `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` → empty; all nine\n121: auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (`login:110`, `register:92`,\n122: `forgot-password:72,100`, `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`,\n123: `verify/...:44`); and `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/` yields no `… dark:bg-s-dark*`\n124: pair. The white login/login-card surface reported in `brief.md` is therefore\n125: already fixed by the existing `main` fix (`70f6236`); no code change is required\n126: for this job.\n\n(End of file - total 126 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"## Summary\n\nThe white surface reported in `brief.md` was the auth **card**, not the page\nbody and not a late/failed theme load. The cards used the literal utilities\n`bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has\nthe `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\nexplicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme\n(`supportsDarkMode: false`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox,\ndracula, terminal, paper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2`\nfallback therefore never applied and the card stayed at Nord's deliberately\nnear-white `--color-white: #eceff4` — exactly the `#ebeef4` card in the report\nscreenshot, on an otherwise-Nord `#353d4a` page (both values are the screenshot's\nslightly colour-managed renditions of Nord `#eceff4` / `#323a49`).\n\nThat defect is **already fixed in this branch and in `main`**. Commit `70f6236`\n(\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\nswept the literal-white surfaces to semantic tokens; the auth cards became\n`bg-c-bg-surface` and `TimePicker.svelte` became `bg-c-bg-modal`. It reached this\nbranch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`, so `git diff main...HEAD` is docs-only and\nno product source change was required.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","text":"## Summary\n\nThe white surface reported in `brief.md` was the auth **card**, not the page\nbody and not a late/failed theme load. The cards used the literal utilities\n`bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has\nthe `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\nexplicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme\n(`supportsDarkMode: false`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox,\ndracula, terminal, paper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2`\nfallback therefore never applied and the card stayed at Nord's deliberately\nnear-white `--color-white: #eceff4` — exactly the `#ebeef4` card in the report\nscreenshot, on an otherwise-Nord `#353d4a` page (both values are the screenshot's\nslightly colour-managed renditions of Nord `#eceff4` / `#323a49`).\n\nThat defect is **already fixed in this branch and in `main`**. Commit `70f6236`\n(\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\nswept the literal-white surfaces to semantic tokens; the auth cards became\n`bg-c-bg-surface` and `TimePicker.svelte` became `bg-c-bg-modal`. It reached this\nbranch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`, so `git diff main...HEAD` is docs-only and\nno product source change was required.\n\nThis pass adds the missing objective evidence: production was measured directly\nand **already runs the fixed markup** — a browser probe of\n`https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` with `theme=nord` renders the card as\n`rgb(59,66,82)` (`#3b4252`), with no white pixels on the page. The earlier\n\"production is a stale deploy older than `70f6236`\" hypothesis is disproven.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: Captured the previously-missing environment facts against the real\n  production app (`my.solyto.app`) with Playwright (the engine `shot` uses,\n  used because `shot` cannot seed `localStorage`). Under `theme=nord`:\n  `localStorage.theme = \"nord\"`, `documentElement.className = \"\"`,\n  card class includes `bg-c-bg-surface`, computed card background\n  `rgb(59,66,82)`. A full theme sweep and three reference screenshots are in\n  `screenshots/` (`render-report.md`). Recorded in `notes.md`.\n  No product code changed.\n\nTASK-2: No change needed. All nine auth card blocks already carry the requested\n  `bg-c-bg-surface` (`login:110`, `register:92`, `forgot-password:72,100`,\n  `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`, `verify/...:44`), and\n  `--color-c-bg-surface` maps to `#ffffff` in default light,\n  `var(--color-s-dark-2)` in default dark (pixel-identical to the old\n  `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`), and `#3b4252` under Nord. The two secondary\n  substitutions in the task were deliberately **not** applied:\n  - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: the labels already\n    inherit a correctly themed colour from `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte`\n    (`text-c-neutral-8` = Nord `#d8dee9`, ≈7:1 contrast on `#3b4252`). Adding an\n    explicit light-mode token would change default-light rendering\n    (`c-neutral-8` → `c-neutral-9`), which TASK-2 says must stay pixel-identical.\n  - `border-white/5` → token border: no target token was specified, and the\n    available `--color-c-border` is transparent / not overridden by Nord, so a\n    blind swap would remove the card outline. The accepted upstream fix\n    (`70f6236`) left this decorative border untouched.\n\nTASK-3: Resolved (no change). `src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte`\n  already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`, fixed by the same `70f6236` sweep. No\n  `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-*` pair remains anywhere under `src/`; the eight\n  remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative (IconPlate, Toggle knob, ScoreBar,\n  Progress).\n\nTASK-4: Rendered verification completed against production (which is\n  byte-for-byte the auth-card markup this branch contains, since the branch has\n  no product diff). Swept default light, default dark and all nine single-mode\n  themes; the login card is dark under every single-mode dark theme and no\n  unexpected light surface (>3000px²) appears. `npm run check` / `lint` / `test`\n  could not be run because `node_modules` is not installed and the project hard\n  rule forbids installing packages without asking; with no product diff there is\n  nothing new for them to check. Full table in\n  `screenshots/render-report.md`.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- The job is a duplicate: the defect was already fixed by `70f6236` before this\n  branch's `main` merge. Product behaviour needs no change; the resolution is to\n  close this job against the existing fix.\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale: it was written before the\n  `70f6236` merge and describes the pre-fix auth-card classes. Left as the\n  analyst's artifact; the corrected picture is here and in `notes.md`.\n- Inherited open items (out of scope): pre-paint theme script / FOUC hardening\n  (there is still a brief flash of the light default on first paint for\n  single-mode themes, because `theme.load()` runs in `onMount`), an `html`\n  background-color rule, account-synced theme setting, and\n  `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` existing on disk but missing from `themes.ts`.\n- Cosmetic consistency (not applied): auth labels use bare `dark:text-white`\n  while the rest of the app mostly uses `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`.\n- Same bug class, out of this job's auth scope: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Progress.svelte`\n  still uses `not-dark:bg-white`, which renders white under single-mode dark\n  themes (`.dark` is absent) — candidate for a follow-up identical to TASK-3.\n\n## Independent re-verification (final developer pass, 2026-10-07)\n\nRe-confirmed the resolution from a clean checkout of this branch:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true (the fix is in this branch).\n- `git diff main...HEAD --stat -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` → empty, so\n  this branch contributes no product source change relative to `main`.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → no matches; all six auth\n  cards carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (`login:110`, `register:92`,\n  `forgot-password:72,100`, `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`,\n  `verify/...:44`).\n- `npm run check` / `lint` / `test` still cannot run because `node_modules` is\n  not installed and the project forbids installing packages without approval.\n\nNo code was changed; this pass only records the re-verification.\n\nAdditional text-legibility check (2026-10-07): because `dark:text-white` never\nfires under single-mode themes, the auth labels inherit `text-c-neutral-8` from\n`src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte`. Confirmed this stays readable everywhere:\nNord/dracula/gruvbox/skyrim/catppuccin-mocha override `--color-c-neutral-7/8/9`\nexplicitly, `atari` and `terminal` override the whole `--color-gray-*` palette\n(e.g. atari `gray-800: #cc88ee`, terminal `gray-800: #00dd00`), and the light\nthemes (`paper`, `catppuccin-latte`) fall back to the base dark\n`--color-gray-800`. No low-contrast label case found.\n\n## Final confirmation pass (2026-10-07, developer)\n\nRe-verified from this checkout, no product change:\n`git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true;\n`git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` → empty; all nine\nauth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (`login:110`, `register:92`,\n`forgot-password:72,100`, `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`,\n`verify/...:44`); and `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/` yields no `… dark:bg-s-dark*`\npair. The white login/login-card surface reported in `brief.md` is therefore\nalready fixed by the existing `main` fix (`70f6236`); no code change is required\nfor this job.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":126,"totalLines":126,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791395595966,"end":1791395596594}},"id":"prt_1177f86710018wsiWbR0TcEJ7y","sessionID":"ses_ee880a7b0ffeIqckXNvh7zeCm7","messageID":"msg_1177f7c8e0010H8lsWGvkdymL0"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791395596623,"sessionID":"ses_ee880a7b0ffeIqckXNvh7zeCm7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_02_a8RdQVpQdGVyPf9bLRUS8908","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git log --oneline -20 && echo \"=== STATUS ===\" && git status && echo \"=== DIFF STAT ===\" && git diff --stat"},"output":"01822aa [create] chore: commit all\n8166bf5 [create] chore: sync session artifacts\nf099721 [create] implementation: confirm theme-on-login fix already present in main\n2e985a7 [create] chore: commit all\ndb245a9 [create] chore: final session artifact sync\ncd224a8 [create] chore: sync session artifacts (final pass, no product change)\nd1f20dd [create] chore: commit all\na0e38aa [create] chore: final session log sync\n35b7617 [create] implementation: confirm auth-card theme fix already in main\n6068eb5 [create] chore: commit all\n57179c5 [create] chore: final session artifact sync\nfc66e8d [create] chore: commit session artifacts\n1b25ded [create] chore: commit all\n2c6d0be [create] chore: sync session artifacts\nbd96228 [create] chore: commit all\n1e3005d [create] chore: sync session artifacts\n0ad6782 [create] implementation: final re-verification of theme-on-login resolution\nd485364 [create] chore: commit all\nd29655b [create] chore: sync session artifacts\nc6ca1ba [create] chore: commit all\n=== STATUS ===\nOn branch feature/create_theme-on-login\nChanges not staged for commit:\n  (use \"git add <file>...\" to update what will be committed)\n  (use \"git restore <file>...\" to discard changes in working directory)\n\tmodified:   docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log\n\tmodified:   docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tokens.json\n\nno changes added to commit (use \"git add\" and/or \"git commit -a\")\n=== DIFF STAT ===\n docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log | 13 +++++++++++++\n docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tokens.json | 10 ++++++++++\n 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+)\n","metadata":{"output":"01822aa [create] chore: commit all\n8166bf5 [create] chore: sync session artifacts\nf099721 [create] implementation: confirm theme-on-login fix already present in main\n2e985a7 [create] chore: commit all\ndb245a9 [create] chore: final session artifact sync\ncd224a8 [create] chore: sync session artifacts (final pass, no product change)\nd1f20dd [create] chore: commit all\na0e38aa [create] chore: final session log sync\n35b7617 [create] implementation: confirm auth-card theme fix already in main\n6068eb5 [create] chore: commit all\n57179c5 [create] chore: final session artifact sync\nfc66e8d [create] chore: commit session artifacts\n1b25ded [create] chore: commit all\n2c6d0be [create] chore: sync session artifacts\nbd96228 [create] chore: commit all\n1e3005d [create] chore: sync session artifacts\n0ad6782 [create] implementation: final re-verification of theme-on-login resolution\nd485364 [create] chore: commit all\nd29655b [create] chore: sync session artifacts\nc6ca1ba [create] chore: commit all\n=== STATUS ===\nOn branch feature/create_theme-on-login\nChanges not staged for commit:\n  (use \"git add <file>...\" to update what will be committed)\n  (use \"git restore <file>...\" to discard changes in working directory)\n\tmodified:   docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log\n\tmodified:   docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tokens.json\n\nno changes added to commit (use \"git add\" and/or \"git commit -a\")\n=== DIFF STAT ===\n docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log | 13 +++++++++++++\n docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tokens.json | 10 ++++++++++\n 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git log --oneline -20 && echo \"=== STATUS ===\" && git status && echo \"=== DIFF STAT ===\" && git diff --stat","time":{"start":1791395596380,"end":1791395596602}},"id":"prt_1177f882f001m6Gj142TTl9aV2","sessionID":"ses_ee880a7b0ffeIqckXNvh7zeCm7","messageID":"msg_1177f7c8e0010H8lsWGvkdymL0"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791395596623,"sessionID":"ses_ee880a7b0ffeIqckXNvh7zeCm7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_oLeu083qf9SzekfsHxYU1850","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Notes: theme on login (TASK-1 environment facts + findings)\n2: \n3: id: create\n4: author: developer\n5: date: 2026-10-07\n6: \n7: ## TL;DR\n8: \n9: The white login surface reported in `brief.md` is caused by literal white\n10: utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) that do not react to single-mode\n11: themes. That exact pattern on the auth cards **has already been fixed on `main`**\n12: and is present on this branch after the merge (`8c0ad30`), so no further product\n13: change is required for TASK-2. This job is effectively a duplicate of the earlier\n14: fix; see \"Evidence\" below.\n15: \n16: ## Code facts (verified in this checkout)\n17: \n18: - Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false` (`src/lib/config/themes.ts`)\n19:   and `ThemeState.apply()` calls `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n20:   for them (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`). The `dark:` Tailwind variant\n21:   therefore never fires under Nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox,\n22:   dracula, terminal, paper, atari.\n23: - The app's correct themed-surface pattern is the semantic `--color-c-*` tokens\n24:   (`bg-c-bg`, `bg-c-bg-surface`, `bg-c-bg-modal`, `bg-c-bg-elevated`), which every\n25:   `static/themes/*/*.css` overrides at `:root`.\n26: - All six auth cards already use `bg-c-bg-surface` (the fix), not\n27:   `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`:\n28:   - `src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte:110`\n29:   - `src/routes/auth/register/+page.svelte:92`\n30:   - `src/routes/auth/forgot-password/+page.svelte:72,100`\n31:   - `src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte:72,85,105`\n32:   - `src/routes/auth/logout/+page.svelte:27`\n33:   - `src/routes/auth/verify/[user_id]/[token]/+page.svelte:44`\n34: - `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` returns **nothing** — the\n35:   problematic class pair has been fully swept from the codebase.\n36: - Inputs are not a source of white: `@tailwindcss/forms`' default white input\n37:   background is already overridden by `src/styles/components/forms.css` to\n38:   `background-color: var(--color-c-bg-elevated)`, which is themed\n39:   (Nord: `#434c5e`).\n40: - Label text is not a source of white either: `src/styles/base.css` sets the root\n41:   text to `text-c-neutral-7` (`dark:text-white`), and\n42:   `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` re-scopes it to `text-c-neutral-8`\n43:   (`dark:text-c-neutral-2`), so labels inherit a correctly themed color on the\n44:   now-themed card. The analyst's `dark:text-white` concern applied to the old\n45:   near-white card, which no longer exists.\n46: \n47: ## Evidence that the fix predates this branch's merge\n48: \n49: `git show 70f6236` (`nord theme bug with todos`, Job:\n50: `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25) changed exactly these auth-card\n51: lines from `... bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `... bg-c-bg-surface ...`\n52: (plus the TimePicker popup from `bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-3` to\n53: `bg-c-bg-modal`). `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true: the\n54: commit is in this branch via the `main` merge parent. `git diff main...HEAD`\n55: shows only the job's own docs — the branch adds no code relative to `main`.\n56: \n57: ## Hypothesis resolution (from tasks.md)\n58: \n59: - **Hypothesis A (different stored theme):** this is the documented root-cause\n60:   mechanism — with the pre-70f6236 code, `theme=nord` on localhost shows the\n61:   white card because `bg-white` no longer has a `dark:` override — and it is now\n62:   fixed in code.\n63: - **Hypothesis B (version skew):** **disproven** for the current production\n64:   deploy (see \"Production facts\" below). Production already serves the fixed\n65:   markup and renders the login card correctly under Nord, so it is not running a\n66:   pre-70f6236 build.\n67: \n68: ## Production facts (captured 2026-10-07, resolves TASK-1)\n69: \n70: The previous passes recorded that the prod-browser facts could not be captured.\n71: They can: the production app is reachable at `https://my.solyto.app` (the app\n72: host from `src/lib/config/platform.ts`; the bare `solyto.app` is the marketing\n73: landing page and 404s on `/auth/login`). Measured with Playwright (the engine\n74: `shot` uses) after seeding `localStorage.theme = 'nord'`:\n75: \n76: - `localStorage.getItem('theme')` → `\"nord\"`\n77: - `document.documentElement.className` → `\"\"` (no `dark` class — as designed for\n78:   single-mode themes)\n79: - login card class → `... bg-c-bg-surface ...` (the fixed markup, not\n80:   `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`)\n81: - computed card `background-color` → `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252`\n82: - Nord stylesheet loaded → yes; `--color-white: #eceff4`, `--color-c-bg: #2e3440`\n83: \n84: A full theme sweep on production (see `screenshots/render-report.md`) shows the\n85: login card is dark under every single-mode dark theme and light only under the\n86: by-design light themes. The white-card symptom from `brief.md` is not\n87: reproducible on production today.\n88: \n89: The other half of TASK-1 (the reporter's *local* instance) is not reachable from\n90: this environment, but it is moot: production now matches the desired behaviour\n91: that local already had.\n92: \n93: ## Verification (TASK-4) limitation\n94: \n95: `node_modules` is not installed in this environment, so `npm run check`,\n96: `npm run lint`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, and `npm run preview` could not be\n97: run. Per the project hard rule (\"NEVER install packages without asking\") no\n98: packages were installed. The remaining verification is a code/commit review, not\n99: a rendered check. Recommended once dependencies and a backend are available:\n100: preview `/auth/login` and `/auth/register` under default light, default dark, and\n101: each single-mode theme (nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula,\n102: terminal, paper, atari) and confirm there are no white cards.\n\n(End of file - total 102 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Notes: theme on login (TASK-1 environment facts + findings)\n\nid: create\nauthor: developer\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n## TL;DR\n\nThe white login surface reported in `brief.md` is caused by literal white\nutilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) that do not react to single-mode\nthemes. That exact pattern on the auth cards **has already been fixed on `main`**\nand is present on this branch after the merge (`8c0ad30`), so no further product\nchange is required for TASK-2. This job is effectively a duplicate of the earlier\nfix; see \"Evidence\" below.\n\n## Code facts (verified in this checkout)\n\n- Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false` (`src/lib/config/themes.ts`)\n  and `ThemeState.apply()` calls `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n  for them (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`). The `dark:` Tailwind variant","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md","text":"# Notes: theme on login (TASK-1 environment facts + findings)\n\nid: create\nauthor: developer\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n## TL;DR\n\nThe white login surface reported in `brief.md` is caused by literal white\nutilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) that do not react to single-mode\nthemes. That exact pattern on the auth cards **has already been fixed on `main`**\nand is present on this branch after the merge (`8c0ad30`), so no further product\nchange is required for TASK-2. This job is effectively a duplicate of the earlier\nfix; see \"Evidence\" below.\n\n## Code facts (verified in this checkout)\n\n- Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false` (`src/lib/config/themes.ts`)\n  and `ThemeState.apply()` calls `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n  for them (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`). The `dark:` Tailwind variant\n  therefore never fires under Nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox,\n  dracula, terminal, paper, atari.\n- The app's correct themed-surface pattern is the semantic `--color-c-*` tokens\n  (`bg-c-bg`, `bg-c-bg-surface`, `bg-c-bg-modal`, `bg-c-bg-elevated`), which every\n  `static/themes/*/*.css` overrides at `:root`.\n- All six auth cards already use `bg-c-bg-surface` (the fix), not\n  `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`:\n  - `src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte:110`\n  - `src/routes/auth/register/+page.svelte:92`\n  - `src/routes/auth/forgot-password/+page.svelte:72,100`\n  - `src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte:72,85,105`\n  - `src/routes/auth/logout/+page.svelte:27`\n  - `src/routes/auth/verify/[user_id]/[token]/+page.svelte:44`\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` returns **nothing** — the\n  problematic class pair has been fully swept from the codebase.\n- Inputs are not a source of white: `@tailwindcss/forms`' default white input\n  background is already overridden by `src/styles/components/forms.css` to\n  `background-color: var(--color-c-bg-elevated)`, which is themed\n  (Nord: `#434c5e`).\n- Label text is not a source of white either: `src/styles/base.css` sets the root\n  text to `text-c-neutral-7` (`dark:text-white`), and\n  `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` re-scopes it to `text-c-neutral-8`\n  (`dark:text-c-neutral-2`), so labels inherit a correctly themed color on the\n  now-themed card. The analyst's `dark:text-white` concern applied to the old\n  near-white card, which no longer exists.\n\n## Evidence that the fix predates this branch's merge\n\n`git show 70f6236` (`nord theme bug with todos`, Job:\n`role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25) changed exactly these auth-card\nlines from `... bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `... bg-c-bg-surface ...`\n(plus the TimePicker popup from `bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-3` to\n`bg-c-bg-modal`). `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true: the\ncommit is in this branch via the `main` merge parent. `git diff main...HEAD`\nshows only the job's own docs — the branch adds no code relative to `main`.\n\n## Hypothesis resolution (from tasks.md)\n\n- **Hypothesis A (different stored theme):** this is the documented root-cause\n  mechanism — with the pre-70f6236 code, `theme=nord` on localhost shows the\n  white card because `bg-white` no longer has a `dark:` override — and it is now\n  fixed in code.\n- **Hypothesis B (version skew):** **disproven** for the current production\n  deploy (see \"Production facts\" below). Production already serves the fixed\n  markup and renders the login card correctly under Nord, so it is not running a\n  pre-70f6236 build.\n\n## Production facts (captured 2026-10-07, resolves TASK-1)\n\nThe previous passes recorded that the prod-browser facts could not be captured.\nThey can: the production app is reachable at `https://my.solyto.app` (the app\nhost from `src/lib/config/platform.ts`; the bare `solyto.app` is the marketing\nlanding page and 404s on `/auth/login`). Measured with Playwright (the engine\n`shot` uses) after seeding `localStorage.theme = 'nord'`:\n\n- `localStorage.getItem('theme')` → `\"nord\"`\n- `document.documentElement.className` → `\"\"` (no `dark` class — as designed for\n  single-mode themes)\n- login card class → `... bg-c-bg-surface ...` (the fixed markup, not\n  `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`)\n- computed card `background-color` → `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252`\n- Nord stylesheet loaded → yes; `--color-white: #eceff4`, `--color-c-bg: #2e3440`\n\nA full theme sweep on production (see `screenshots/render-report.md`) shows the\nlogin card is dark under every single-mode dark theme and light only under the\nby-design light themes. The white-card symptom from `brief.md` is not\nreproducible on production today.\n\nThe other half of TASK-1 (the reporter's *local* instance) is not reachable from\nthis environment, but it is moot: production now matches the desired behaviour\nthat local already had.\n\n## Verification (TASK-4) limitation\n\n`node_modules` is not installed in this environment, so `npm run check`,\n`npm run lint`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, and `npm run preview` could not be\nrun. Per the project hard rule (\"NEVER install packages without asking\") no\npackages were installed. The remaining verification is a code/commit review, not\na rendered check. Recommended once dependencies and a backend are available:\npreview `/auth/login` and `/auth/register` under default light, default dark, and\neach single-mode theme (nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula,\nterminal, paper, atari) and confirm there are no white cards.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":102,"totalLines":102,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md","time":{"start":1791395596332,"end":1791395596611}},"id":"prt_1177f86f9001SSLxEvD3Vzg97u","sessionID":"ses_ee880a7b0ffeIqckXNvh7zeCm7","messageID":"msg_1177f7c8e0010H8lsWGvkdymL0"}}
