{"type":"text","timestamp":1791395805390,"sessionID":"ses_ee880a7b0ffeIqckXNvh7zeCm7","part":{"id":"prt_11782adbe001DhZ6LxeOqGkKnP","messageID":"msg_11782a4ce001j4lXje7JQKcOY5","sessionID":"ses_ee880a7b0ffeIqckXNvh7zeCm7","type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI worked the job at `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login` on branch `feature/create_theme-on-login` (matches `brief.md`). The outcome is that **the bug is already fixed in this branch — no product code change was required or made.**\n\n### What the bug was\nIndependent evidence (I decoded the `brief.md` screenshot with a pure-Python PNG decoder, since no vision model is available): it is 973×989, ~90% Nord page `#353d4a`, containing one centred 320×280 near-white block `#ebeef4` (= Nord's `--color-white` `#eceff4`) with darker input fields inside. So the white surface is the auth **card**, not the page and not a theme-load flash.\n\nMechanism: auth cards used `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has `.dark`, which `ThemeState.apply()` explicitly removes for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). So under Nord the card stayed literal `bg-white` → Nord's near-white `#eceff4`.\n\n### Why no change is needed\n- The accepted upstream fix `70f6236` (\"nord theme bug with todos\") already swept exactly this pattern to the semantic tokens. It is an ancestor of `HEAD` and reached this branch via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`.\n- All nine auth card blocks now carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44); `TimePicker` uses `bg-c-bg-modal` (TASK-3 moot).\n- `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is **empty** — this branch contributes no product-source change.\n- `localStorage`, `documentElement.className`, and computed card colour were previously captured against production (`my.solyto.app`), which already serves the fixed markup and renders the card `rgb(59,66,82)` (`#3b4252`).\n\nI deliberately did **not** apply the analyst's two secondary TASK-2 substitutions (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`, `border-white/5` → token border): the upstream reference left them in place, no commit anywhere introduced the label swap, and applying them would change default-light rendering (`c-neutral-8` → `c-neutral-9`), contradicting TASK-2's own \"pixel-identical\" constraint. `--color-c-border` is transparent in light mode, so the border swap would remove the card outline.\n\n### Commits\n- `cdd3965 [create] implementation: confirm theme-on-login fix already in branch (no-op)` — added the closing analysis to `implementation.md`.\n- Two `[create] chore: sync session artifacts` commits.\n\n### Note\n`docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log` / `tokens.json` are harness-managed and get a new entry appended every step, so they may appear dirty again after this message — that is inherent to the live session and matches how prior passes ended. The branch's product state already matches the accepted fix; the correct process outcome is to close this job as a duplicate.","time":{"start":1791395802559,"end":1791395805381}}}
