{"type":"text","timestamp":1791395883444,"sessionID":"ses_ee87d37e7ffe5d6D49q0r0KIDS","part":{"id":"prt_11783e01e001rIY97wmd03wPol","messageID":"msg_11783d983001z0qOWrzBs26haJ","sessionID":"ses_ee87d37e7ffe5d6D49q0r0KIDS","type":"text","text":"Done. Here is the outcome of this developer session.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe job `create_theme-on-login` is a **duplicate: the defect it describes is already fixed in the codebase**, so no product change was made.\n\nThe white surface in the `brief.md` screenshot is the auth **card**, produced by the literal utilities `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, but `ThemeState.apply()` strips that class for every single-mode theme (nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). Under Nord the card therefore fell back to Nord's near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`.\n\nThat exact pattern on all auth cards was swept to the semantic token `bg-c-bg-surface` (and `TimePicker` to `bg-c-bg-modal`) by commit `70f6236` (\"nord theme bug with todos\"), which this branch already contains via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`.\n\n## Verification performed\n\n- Branch is `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md` — no checkout needed.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true.\n- `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` → empty (no product diff vs `main`).\n- `git log 70f6236..HEAD -- src/routes/auth/` → empty (no auth-card commit after the fix).\n- All nine auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`; no `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark*` pair remains in `src/`.\n- Confirmed label legibility fallback across light and dark single-mode themes.\n- `npm run check` / `lint` / `test` could not run: `node_modules` is absent and installing packages is forbidden by the project rules. With no product diff there is nothing new for them to check.\n- Production was measured directly in an earlier pass (`my.solyto.app/auth/login`, `theme=nord`) and already renders the card `rgb(59,66,82)` — no white pixels. That evidence is recorded in `notes.md` / `screenshots/render-report.md`.\n\n## Changes\n\n`implementation.md` was updated with a final independent re-verification section; the session artifacts (`session.log`, `tokens.json`) were committed. Worktree is clean, nothing pushed or merged.\n\nNotably, TASK-2's two secondary substitutions (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`, `border-white/5` → token border) were deliberately **not** applied: the accepted upstream fix left them, the label swap would change default-light rendering (contradicting TASK-2's own pixel-identical constraint), and no suitable semantic border token exists (`--color-c-border` is transparent). TASK-3 is moot (`TimePicker` already fixed).","time":{"start":1791395880992,"end":1791395883431}}}
