{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791395988559,"sessionID":"ses_ee87c0694ffeDdtz9WPo07qRkG","part":{"id":"prt_11785844b001F8abT4CBTENxTw","messageID":"msg_117857f06001pbHw3u6rwTHxTh","sessionID":"ses_ee87c0694ffeDdtz9WPo07qRkG","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1791395991918,"sessionID":"ses_ee87c0694ffeDdtz9WPo07qRkG","part":{"id":"prt_1178589c0001kQX8JuNqEYvpoq","messageID":"msg_117857f06001pbHw3u6rwTHxTh","sessionID":"ses_ee87c0694ffeDdtz9WPo07qRkG","type":"text","text":"Done. Here's the outcome of this developer pass.\n\n## What I found\n\nThe `brief.md` symptom — a **white login card under a single-mode theme like Nord** — is caused by literal white utilities (`bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`). The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`) strips that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). So the themed fallback never applied and the card stayed at the literal near-white `--color-white`.\n\n**That defect is already fixed in this branch.** Commit `70f6236` (\"nord theme bug with todos\") swept the auth cards to `bg-c-bg-surface` and `TimePicker` to `bg-c-bg-modal`, and it is an ancestor of this branch's HEAD. `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is empty — the branch carries no product source change.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true\n- All nine auth-card surfaces use `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44)\n- `TimePicker.svelte` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`\n- No `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark*` pair remains under `src/`\n- `bg-c-bg-surface` maps to `#ffffff` (default light), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` (default dark — pixel-identical to the old classes) and `#3b4252` under Nord\n- `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` are unavailable: `node_modules` is not installed and the project rules forbid installing packages without approval. With no product diff there is nothing new for them to validate.\n\n## Result\n\nNo code change was required or made. I made the smallest possible change: a short verification note appended to `implementation.md`, and committed it together with the session artifacts so the worktree is clean (`39f3971`). This job is effectively a duplicate of the earlier upstream fix; the correct resolution is to close it against `70f6236` rather than modify product code.\n\nNotable out-of-scope follow-ups already recorded in `implementation.md`: the pre-paint theme flash (FOUC) for single-mode themes, and `Progress.svelte`'s `not-dark:bg-white`, which is the same bug class but outside the auth scope.","time":{"start":1791395989952,"end":1791395991912}}}
