{"type":"text","timestamp":1791402323192,"sessionID":"ses_ee81aac60ffepvWn8tnjGtr7L1","part":{"id":"prt_117e625ee001NKbIw518gcN6sY","messageID":"msg_117e61cd0001S0hXpdOw58qtuY","sessionID":"ses_ee81aac60ffepvWn8tnjGtr7L1","type":"text","text":"The job is complete. Here's what I found and did.\n\n## Result\n\nI read `brief.md`, `tasks.md`, and the prior job artifacts, then independently verified the conclusion rather than trusting them.\n\n**Root cause of the white surface:** the six auth cards used the literal pair `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` removes that class for every single-mode theme (Nord included). So under Nord the card fell back to Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4` on an otherwise-Nord page — exactly the reported symptom.\n\n**That defect is already fixed upstream.** Commit `70f6236` swept the auth cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token; it reached this branch through the `main` merge. Verified in this checkout:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true\n- `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` → empty (no product source change on this branch)\n- `grep bg-white | grep dark:bg-s-dark` → no matches; all nine auth-card blocks use `bg-c-bg-surface`\n\nI also ran a live production probe (`https://my.solyto.app/auth/login`, Chromium, seeding `theme=nord`): the login card class is `…bg-c-bg-surface…`, computed background `rgb(59,66,82)` = Nord `#3b4252`, text `#d8dee9`, `html` correctly carries no `dark` class. The white-card symptom is not reproducible on production today.\n\n**No product code change is warranted** — this job duplicates the earlier fix. `TASK-3` (the `not-dark:bg-white` in `Progress.svelte`) is explicitly optional and needs owner go-ahead, so with no human available I left it as a documented follow-up.\n\n## Bookkeeping\n- Added a short \"Third verification pass\" to `implementation.md` recording the fresh checks and probe.\n- Committed all artifacts (including the earlier agents' `session.log`/`tokens.json`); worktree is clean.\n- Branch matches `brief.md` (`feature/create_theme-on-login`), nothing pushed/merged.","time":{"start":1791402321390,"end":1791402323181}}}
