{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791402386891,"sessionID":"ses_ee819048dffekwq55dJro1KEkf","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_Y12KaAvMdvj9BDpp7EcJ3025","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ## Summary\n2: \n3: The white surface in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, not the page body and not a\n4: late/failed theme load. The six auth cards used the literal pair\n5: `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` carries\n6: the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\n7: explicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode:\n8: false`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal,\n9: paper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback therefore never\n10: applied, so the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white\n11: `--color-white: #eceff4` (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`) on an otherwise-Nord\n12: page.\n13: \n14: That defect is **already fixed and present in this branch**. Commit `70f6236`\n15: (\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\n16: swept the auth cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token and\n17: `TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`; it reached this branch through the `main`\n18: merge `8c0ad30`. `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is\n19: empty, so this branch contributes no product source change. **This job is a\n20: duplicate of the earlier fix and needs no code change** — the correct outcome is\n21: to close it against `70f6236`.\n22: \n23: ## Changes\n24: \n25: TASK-1: No product code. Environment facts were captured against the real\n26:   production app (`https://my.solyto.app`, the app host from\n27:   `src/lib/config/platform.ts`; bare `solyto.app` is the marketing landing page).\n28:   Re-confirmed independently this pass with Playwright (same engine `shot` uses,\n29:   chosen because `shot` cannot seed `localStorage`) after\n30:   `localStorage.setItem('theme','nord')`:\n31: \n32:   | fact | value |\n33:   | --- | --- |\n34:   | `localStorage.theme` | `\"nord\"` |\n35:   | `documentElement.className` | `\"\"` (no `dark` class — by design for single-mode themes) |\n36:   | login card class | `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` |\n37:   | computed card `background-color` | `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252` |\n38:   | computed card `color` | `rgb(216, 222, 233)` = Nord `#d8dee9` |\n39:   | `--color-white` / `--color-c-bg` / `--color-c-bg-surface` / `--color-c-neutral` | `#eceff4` / `#2e3440` / `#3b4252` / `#323a49` |\n40:   | Nord stylesheet link present | yes |\n41: \n42:   Hypothesis A (different stored theme) is the documented root-cause mechanism,\n43:   now fixed in code; Hypothesis B (stale/skewed production assets) is disproven —\n44:   production already serves the fixed markup (`bg-c-bg-surface`) and renders the\n45:   card as Nord `#3b4252`. Also independently decoded the `brief.md` screenshot\n46:   (pure-Python PNG decode): 973x989, ~90% `#303848` Nord page with a ~5.9%\n47:   near-white `#e8e8f0` region, confirming the white surface is the card and\n48:   matching the pre-fix markup.\n49: \n50: TASK-2: No change needed. All nine auth-card blocks already carry\n51:   `bg-c-bg-surface`: `login:110`, `register:92`,\n52:   `forgot-password:72,100`, `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`,\n53:   `verify/[user_id]/[token]:44`. `--color-c-bg-surface` resolves to `#ffffff` in\n54:   default light (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` in default\n55:   dark (`src/styles/default.css:19`, pixel-identical to the old\n56:   `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`), and `#3b4252` under Nord\n57:   (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). The two secondary substitutions named\n58:   in the task were deliberately **not** applied:\n59:   - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: auth labels already\n60:     inherit a correctly themed colour from `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte`\n61:     (`text-c-neutral-8` = Nord `#d8dee9`, ≈7:1 on `#3b4252`). Adding an explicit\n62:     light-mode token would change default-light rendering (`c-neutral-8` →\n63:     `c-neutral-9`), which TASK-2 requires to stay pixel-identical.\n64:   - `border-white/5` → token border: no target token was specified, and\n65:     `--color-c-border` is transparent / not overridden by Nord, so a blind swap\n66:     would remove the decorative card outline. The accepted upstream fix left it\n67:     untouched.\n68: \n69: TASK-3: No change (optional item, and already resolved). `TimePicker.svelte`\n70:   already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`, fixed by the same `70f6236` sweep. No\n71:   `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark*` pair remains anywhere under `src/`.\n72: \n73: TASK-4: Verification. `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → no matches;\n74:   `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; all nine auth-card blocks\n75:   carry the semantic token. Rendered verification is recorded in\n76:   `screenshots/render-report.md` (full theme sweep, production): the login card\n77:   is dark under every single-mode dark theme and light only under the by-design\n78:   light themes (default-light, `catppuccin-latte`, `paper`). `npm run check`,\n79:   `lint`, `test`, and `build` could not be run because `node_modules` is not\n80:   installed and the project hard rule forbids installing packages without asking;\n81:   with no product diff there is nothing new for them to check.\n82: \n83: ## Second verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n84: \n85: Re-ran the decisive checks independently rather than trusting the earlier notes:\n86: \n87: - `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 origin/main` → true, and\n88:   `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is empty, so the\n89:   auth-card fix is upstream on `origin/main` and this branch contributes no product\n90:   source change. `git show 70f6236 -- src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte` confirms it\n91:   is the commit that changed the login card from\n92:   `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n93: - `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → no matches. All nine auth-card blocks\n94:   (`login:110`, `register:92`, `forgot-password:72,100`,\n95:   `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`, `verify/…:44`) carry `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n96: - Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface` is `#ffffff` in\n97:   `src/styles/tokens.css:24`, becomes `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n98:   (`src/styles/default.css:19`), and is `#3b4252` under Nord\n99:   (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). So default light/dark stay pixel-identical\n100:   to the old `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`, while single-mode themes get a themed card.\n101: \n102: Conclusion unchanged: no product change is warranted; this job duplicates `70f6236`.\n103: \n104: ## Third verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n105: \n106: Re-verified the conclusion without relying on the earlier notes:\n107: \n108: - `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD --stat\n109:   -- src static tests package.json` is empty, so the fix is upstream and this\n110:   branch adds no product source change.\n111: - `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → no matches. All nine\n112:   auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92,\n113:   forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44).\n114: - Live production probe (`https://my.solyto.app/auth/login`, Playwright/Chromium,\n115:   seeding `localStorage.theme = 'nord'` then reloading) independently reproduces\n116:   the fixed behaviour:\n117: \n118:   | fact | value |\n119:   | --- | --- |\n120:   | `localStorage.theme` | `\"nord\"` |\n121:   | `documentElement.className` | `\"\"` (no `dark` class) |\n122:   | login card class | `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` |\n123:   | computed card `background-color` | `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252` |\n124:   | computed card `color` | `rgb(216, 222, 233)` = Nord `#d8dee9` |\n125:   | `--color-white` / `--color-c-bg` / `--color-c-bg-surface` | `#eceff4` / `#2e3440` / `#3b4252` |\n126:   | Nord stylesheet present | yes |\n127: \n128: The white login card from `brief.md` is not reproducible against current\n129: production under Nord. Conclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; the job\n130: duplicates `70f6236`.\n131: \n132: ## Fourth verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n133: \n134: Independent re-check, favouring repo-state facts over the earlier notes:\n135: \n136: - Branch is `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`; no product\n137:   source diff: `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` is empty.\n138: - `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git show --stat 70f6236`\n139:   confirms it swept the auth cards and `TimePicker.svelte`.\n140: - `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → no matches. All nine auth-card\n141:   blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92,\n142:   forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44).\n143: - Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff`\n144:   (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n145:   (`src/styles/default.css:19`), and `#3b4252` under Nord\n146:   (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). Nord is `supportsDarkMode: false`\n147:   (`src/lib/config/themes.ts:22-24`), which is why the old `dark:bg-s-dark-2`\n148:   fallback never fired — the documented root cause, now moot.\n149: - `node_modules` is still absent and the project hard rule forbids installing\n150:   packages, so `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` could not be run; there is\n151:   no product diff for them to check. The production render sweep in\n152:   `screenshots/render-report.md` remains the rendered evidence.\n153: \n154: Conclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; the job duplicates `70f6236`.\n155: \n156: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n157: \n158: - This job is a duplicate: the defect was already fixed by `70f6236` before this\n159:   branch's `main` merge. Product behaviour needs no change; close against the\n160:   existing fix.\n161: - `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale — it was written at rev 4\n162:   before the `70f6236` merge and still describes the pre-fix auth-card classes.\n163:   Left as the analyst's artifact; the corrected picture is in `notes.md` and here.\n164: - Inherited open items (out of scope): pre-paint theme script / FOUC hardening\n165:   (`theme.load()` runs in `onMount`, so there is still a brief light-default flash\n166:   before a single-mode theme applies), an `html`/`body` background-color rule, an\n167:   account-synced theme setting, and `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` existing on disk\n168:   but missing from `src/lib/config/themes.ts`.\n169: - Same bug class, outside this job's auth scope: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Progress.svelte:74`\n170:   still uses `not-dark:bg-white`, which renders white under single-mode dark\n171:   themes (`.dark` absent) — candidate for a follow-up identical to TASK-3.\n172: - Cosmetic consistency (not applied): auth labels use bare `dark:text-white`\n173:   while most of the app uses `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`.\n\n(End of file - total 173 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"## Summary\n\nThe white surface in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, not the page body and not a\nlate/failed theme load. The six auth cards used the literal pair\n`bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` carries\nthe `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\nexplicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode:\nfalse`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal,\npaper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback therefore never\napplied, so the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white\n`--color-white: #eceff4` (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`) on an otherwise-Nord\npage.\n\nThat defect is **already fixed and present in this branch**. Commit `70f6236`\n(\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\nswept the auth cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token and\n`TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`; it reached this branch through the `main`\nmerge `8c0ad30`. `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is\nempty, so this branch contributes no product source change. **This job is a\nduplicate of the earlier fix and needs no code change** — the correct outcome is","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","text":"## Summary\n\nThe white surface in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, not the page body and not a\nlate/failed theme load. The six auth cards used the literal pair\n`bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` carries\nthe `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\nexplicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode:\nfalse`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal,\npaper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback therefore never\napplied, so the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white\n`--color-white: #eceff4` (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`) on an otherwise-Nord\npage.\n\nThat defect is **already fixed and present in this branch**. Commit `70f6236`\n(\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\nswept the auth cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token and\n`TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`; it reached this branch through the `main`\nmerge `8c0ad30`. `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is\nempty, so this branch contributes no product source change. **This job is a\nduplicate of the earlier fix and needs no code change** — the correct outcome is\nto close it against `70f6236`.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: No product code. Environment facts were captured against the real\n  production app (`https://my.solyto.app`, the app host from\n  `src/lib/config/platform.ts`; bare `solyto.app` is the marketing landing page).\n  Re-confirmed independently this pass with Playwright (same engine `shot` uses,\n  chosen because `shot` cannot seed `localStorage`) after\n  `localStorage.setItem('theme','nord')`:\n\n  | fact | value |\n  | --- | --- |\n  | `localStorage.theme` | `\"nord\"` |\n  | `documentElement.className` | `\"\"` (no `dark` class — by design for single-mode themes) |\n  | login card class | `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` |\n  | computed card `background-color` | `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252` |\n  | computed card `color` | `rgb(216, 222, 233)` = Nord `#d8dee9` |\n  | `--color-white` / `--color-c-bg` / `--color-c-bg-surface` / `--color-c-neutral` | `#eceff4` / `#2e3440` / `#3b4252` / `#323a49` |\n  | Nord stylesheet link present | yes |\n\n  Hypothesis A (different stored theme) is the documented root-cause mechanism,\n  now fixed in code; Hypothesis B (stale/skewed production assets) is disproven —\n  production already serves the fixed markup (`bg-c-bg-surface`) and renders the\n  card as Nord `#3b4252`. Also independently decoded the `brief.md` screenshot\n  (pure-Python PNG decode): 973x989, ~90% `#303848` Nord page with a ~5.9%\n  near-white `#e8e8f0` region, confirming the white surface is the card and\n  matching the pre-fix markup.\n\nTASK-2: No change needed. All nine auth-card blocks already carry\n  `bg-c-bg-surface`: `login:110`, `register:92`,\n  `forgot-password:72,100`, `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`,\n  `verify/[user_id]/[token]:44`. `--color-c-bg-surface` resolves to `#ffffff` in\n  default light (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` in default\n  dark (`src/styles/default.css:19`, pixel-identical to the old\n  `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`), and `#3b4252` under Nord\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). The two secondary substitutions named\n  in the task were deliberately **not** applied:\n  - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: auth labels already\n    inherit a correctly themed colour from `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte`\n    (`text-c-neutral-8` = Nord `#d8dee9`, ≈7:1 on `#3b4252`). Adding an explicit\n    light-mode token would change default-light rendering (`c-neutral-8` →\n    `c-neutral-9`), which TASK-2 requires to stay pixel-identical.\n  - `border-white/5` → token border: no target token was specified, and\n    `--color-c-border` is transparent / not overridden by Nord, so a blind swap\n    would remove the decorative card outline. The accepted upstream fix left it\n    untouched.\n\nTASK-3: No change (optional item, and already resolved). `TimePicker.svelte`\n  already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`, fixed by the same `70f6236` sweep. No\n  `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark*` pair remains anywhere under `src/`.\n\nTASK-4: Verification. `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → no matches;\n  `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; all nine auth-card blocks\n  carry the semantic token. Rendered verification is recorded in\n  `screenshots/render-report.md` (full theme sweep, production): the login card\n  is dark under every single-mode dark theme and light only under the by-design\n  light themes (default-light, `catppuccin-latte`, `paper`). `npm run check`,\n  `lint`, `test`, and `build` could not be run because `node_modules` is not\n  installed and the project hard rule forbids installing packages without asking;\n  with no product diff there is nothing new for them to check.\n\n## Second verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nRe-ran the decisive checks independently rather than trusting the earlier notes:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 origin/main` → true, and\n  `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is empty, so the\n  auth-card fix is upstream on `origin/main` and this branch contributes no product\n  source change. `git show 70f6236 -- src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte` confirms it\n  is the commit that changed the login card from\n  `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → no matches. All nine auth-card blocks\n  (`login:110`, `register:92`, `forgot-password:72,100`,\n  `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`, `verify/…:44`) carry `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n- Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface` is `#ffffff` in\n  `src/styles/tokens.css:24`, becomes `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n  (`src/styles/default.css:19`), and is `#3b4252` under Nord\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). So default light/dark stay pixel-identical\n  to the old `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`, while single-mode themes get a themed card.\n\nConclusion unchanged: no product change is warranted; this job duplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Third verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nRe-verified the conclusion without relying on the earlier notes:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD --stat\n  -- src static tests package.json` is empty, so the fix is upstream and this\n  branch adds no product source change.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → no matches. All nine\n  auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92,\n  forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44).\n- Live production probe (`https://my.solyto.app/auth/login`, Playwright/Chromium,\n  seeding `localStorage.theme = 'nord'` then reloading) independently reproduces\n  the fixed behaviour:\n\n  | fact | value |\n  | --- | --- |\n  | `localStorage.theme` | `\"nord\"` |\n  | `documentElement.className` | `\"\"` (no `dark` class) |\n  | login card class | `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` |\n  | computed card `background-color` | `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252` |\n  | computed card `color` | `rgb(216, 222, 233)` = Nord `#d8dee9` |\n  | `--color-white` / `--color-c-bg` / `--color-c-bg-surface` | `#eceff4` / `#2e3440` / `#3b4252` |\n  | Nord stylesheet present | yes |\n\nThe white login card from `brief.md` is not reproducible against current\nproduction under Nord. Conclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; the job\nduplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Fourth verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nIndependent re-check, favouring repo-state facts over the earlier notes:\n\n- Branch is `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`; no product\n  source diff: `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` is empty.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git show --stat 70f6236`\n  confirms it swept the auth cards and `TimePicker.svelte`.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → no matches. All nine auth-card\n  blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92,\n  forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44).\n- Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff`\n  (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n  (`src/styles/default.css:19`), and `#3b4252` under Nord\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). Nord is `supportsDarkMode: false`\n  (`src/lib/config/themes.ts:22-24`), which is why the old `dark:bg-s-dark-2`\n  fallback never fired — the documented root cause, now moot.\n- `node_modules` is still absent and the project hard rule forbids installing\n  packages, so `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` could not be run; there is\n  no product diff for them to check. The production render sweep in\n  `screenshots/render-report.md` remains the rendered evidence.\n\nConclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; the job duplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- This job is a duplicate: the defect was already fixed by `70f6236` before this\n  branch's `main` merge. Product behaviour needs no change; close against the\n  existing fix.\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale — it was written at rev 4\n  before the `70f6236` merge and still describes the pre-fix auth-card classes.\n  Left as the analyst's artifact; the corrected picture is in `notes.md` and here.\n- Inherited open items (out of scope): pre-paint theme script / FOUC hardening\n  (`theme.load()` runs in `onMount`, so there is still a brief light-default flash\n  before a single-mode theme applies), an `html`/`body` background-color rule, an\n  account-synced theme setting, and `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` existing on disk\n  but missing from `src/lib/config/themes.ts`.\n- Same bug class, outside this job's auth scope: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Progress.svelte:74`\n  still uses `not-dark:bg-white`, which renders white under single-mode dark\n  themes (`.dark` absent) — candidate for a follow-up identical to TASK-3.\n- Cosmetic consistency (not applied): auth labels use bare `dark:text-white`\n  while most of the app uses `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":173,"totalLines":173,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791402386667,"end":1791402386886}},"id":"prt_117e724c6001JJrqeWGOkBRycV","sessionID":"ses_ee819048dffekwq55dJro1KEkf","messageID":"msg_117e71de5001sqnFADkcyQiwRh"}}
