{"type":"text","timestamp":1791402494329,"sessionID":"ses_ee819048dffekwq55dJro1KEkf","part":{"id":"prt_117e8be57001DUriQOiUa5LfFN","messageID":"msg_117e8b473001j0gGHNLyIrGuz8","sessionID":"ses_ee819048dffekwq55dJro1KEkf","type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nI worked the job at `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login`. Branch verified first: `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches the `branch:` field in `brief.md`.\n\n**Outcome: no product code change is warranted — this job duplicates an existing upstream fix.**\n\n### What the bug was\nThe screenshot in `brief.md` shows a mostly-Nord page with one near-white surface. I downloaded and pixel-decoded the original PNG (no image input available to me, so I analyzed it directly): 973×989, ~90% Nord page background, with a ~5.9% near-white region (`#ebEEF4`, essentially Nord `--color-white: #eceff4`) at x374–693, y339–618 — a ~320px login card.\n\nCause: the six auth cards used literal `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` fallback only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, which `ThemeState.apply()` explicitly removes for single-mode themes (`supportsDarkMode: false`, e.g. Nord). So under Nord the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white`.\n\n### Verification (independent, this session)\n- `70f6236` (\"nord theme bug with todos\") is an ancestor of `HEAD`; `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` is **empty** — this branch adds only job docs.\n- `grep` → no `bg-white` in `src/routes/auth/`, no `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark` anywhere under `src/`. All nine auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n- Token mapping: `--color-c-bg-surface` is `#ffffff` light, `var(--color-s-dark-2)` dark, `#3b4252` Nord — pixel-identical to the old classes in default light/dark, correctly themed for single-mode.\n- Independent production probe: deployed `my.solyto.app/auth/login` server HTML already contains `bg-c-bg-surface` (no `bg-white`); with `localStorage.theme='nord'` seeded, Chromium/Playwright measured `html.class=\"\"`, card `background-color: rgb(59,66,82)` = Nord `#3b4252`. White card not reproducible on current production.\n- Hypothesis B (stale prod assets) is disproven; Hypothesis A's mechanism is the root cause and is fixed.\n- `node_modules` is absent; per the hard rule I did not install packages, so `npm run check/lint/test/build` could not run — and there is no product diff for them to check.\n\n### Changes\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md` — added a fifth verification pass documenting the independent prod probe and gate limitation.\n- Committed harness artifacts (`session.log`, `tokens.json`); worktree left clean.\n\n### Follow-ups (out of scope, not changed)\n- Pre-paint theme script / FOUC hardening; `html`/`body` background rule; account-synced theme setting; `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`.\n- Same bug class outside auth scope: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Progress.svelte:74` uses `not-dark:bg-white`.\n\nThe correct close-out is to close this job against `70f6236`.","time":{"start":1791402491479,"end":1791402494321}}}
