{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791402593185,"sessionID":"ses_ee815c9b3ffe1ffWjQDgOdBgXm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_GJvs7Jr9r8EUUBStBwrg2412","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/brief.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/brief.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Brief: theme on login\n2: \n3: status: open\n4: type: feature\n5: id: create\n6: branch: feature/create_theme-on-login\n7: date: 2026-08-22\n8: author: Leander Muskalla\n9: \n10: ## What\n11: \n12: It seems to me themes are not fully applied on login? Or it might just be the nord theme.\n13: On the production app, when I log in with my Fedora Desktop that uses Nord theme for everything, I see this: https://iili.io/CZZtpwX.png\n14: On my local instance of solyto, everything looks correct.\n15: Try to find out what the issue is - why do I see a white background?\n16: \n17: ## Why\n18: \n19: <!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n20: \n21: ## Out of scope\n22: \n23: <!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\n24: \n25: ## Notes\n26: \n27: <!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->\n\n(End of file - total 27 lines)\n</content>\n\n<system-reminder>\nInstructions from: /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md\n# solyto frontend\n\n<!--\nThis is your project context, loaded by the agent at the start of every session.\nmanigot is vendor-agnostic: it runs Claude Code or OpenCode against the same\nproject (`mg --profile claude-pro` vs `mg --profile zai`/`--profile\nopencode-go`), and this one file serves both — manigot mounts it read-only\nwherever the selected tool looks for it\n(/workspace/AGENTS.md for OpenCode, /workspace/.claude/CLAUDE.md for Claude\nCode). Those mount paths are read-only: to change this context, edit this\nfile (docs/AGENTS.md), never the mount paths.\nThe same global agents are available under @name either way, and custom\nproject agents in docs/agents/ work under both tools — write them in the\nbuilt-in format (name:, description:, tools: Read, Grep, ...), no per-tool\nformat needed. To make a custom agent read-only under OpenCode, add a\n`permission:` frontmatter block (the built-in format manigot's conversion\npasses through to OpenCode's schema — see the manigot README's agent section);\nthe read-only built-in agents' blocks deny the destructive git commands\n(worktree management, branch -d/-D, reset, checkout, push, ...).\nCustom agents that must commit (like the built-in developer/reviewer/quality)\ndeclare `commit: true` in their frontmatter; agents that never commit declare\n`commit: false` and get a read-only git mount. The default — no agent named,\nfile missing, or marker absent/unknown — is a writable git mount, so a\ncommitting agent is never broken by a missing marker.\nAgent sessions also restrict git to reading history and making commits (the\nsession git shim): worktree management, branch deletes, resets, checkouts,\npushes, and the other destructive subcommands are refused.\nKeep this file tool-neutral — write it for \"the agent\", not for one vendor.\n-->\n\nThe client for [solyto.app](https://solyto.app): a free, private, all-in-one personal management app — todos, notes, calendar, contacts, media libraries, check-in, finances, feeds, time tracking, clipboard, and dev-requests in one place. This repo is the frontend only: a SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 single-page app that runs on the web, as an installable PWA, or as a native desktop/mobile shell. There is no backend or database here — every piece of data comes from the solyto REST API, which lives in a separate repository.\n\n## Stack\n- Backend: none in this repo — pure client-side SPA. Consumes the solyto REST API at `/api/v1` (`api.solyto.app` in prod, `http://localhost:8000` in dev; configurable per hostname in `src/lib/config/platform.ts`).\n- Frontend: SvelteKit 2, Svelte 5 (runes, `$state`), TypeScript (strict), Vite 7, Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`, adapter-node (outputs to `build/`).\n- Database: none — persistence is owned by the backend. The client only stores auth tokens, theme, and preferences in LocalStorage (`src/lib/services/LocalStorageService.ts`).\n- Key packages: `@tiptap/*` (notes rich-text editor), `echarts` (statistics charts), `@simplewebauthn/browser` (passkey login), `marked` + `dompurify` (markdown), `@lucide/svelte` (icons), `svelte-dnd-action` / `svelte-gestures` (drag & drop, swipe), `canvas-confetti`, `@fontsource/*`, `@vvo/tzdb`.\n\n## Architecture\n- `src/routes/` — SvelteKit file-based routes, all client-rendered (no `+page.server.ts`/`+server.ts` anywhere). The root `+layout.svelte` bootstraps every state store via `setContext`, guards unauthenticated access (redirect to `/auth/login` or `/setup`), and renders the navbar/footer shells. Feature routes: `/todos`, `/notes`, `/calendar`, `/contacts`, `/check-in`, `/finances`, `/feeds`, `/time-tracking`, `/clipboard`, `/dev-requests`, `/libraries/{books,movies,music,games,links,quotes,recipes,plants}`, plus `/settings`, `/admin`, `/profile`, `/auth/*`, `/setup`, `/share`.\n- `src/lib/state/` — one Svelte 5 runes class per domain (`Auth`, `Todos`, `Notes`, `Calendars`, `BookLibrary`, ...). Instances are created in `+layout.svelte` and shared through Svelte context (`setContext`/`getContext`); each store fetches via `ApiService` and holds the result in reactive `$state`.\n- `src/lib/services/` — `ApiService` (fetch wrapper over the REST API: Bearer auth, JSON, `%s`/`%d` URL placeholders, FormData uploads) and pure domain services (`TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`, `TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`, `LibraryFilterService`, `WealthStatisticsService`, ...) that are unit-tested.\n- `src/lib/config/` — `apiRoutes.ts` (all endpoints, composed from `getApiUrl()` + `/api/v1`), `platform.ts` (web vs. desktop vs. mobile via `PUBLIC_DESKTOP`/`PUBLIC_MOBILE`, API URL resolution), `themes.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `urls.ts`, `features.ts`.\n- `src/lib/components/` — feature components plus shared `ui/` (buttons, modals, navbar), `forms/` (inputs, pickers, toggles), and `charts/` (echarts wrappers). Several features keep separate desktop/mobile view variants (e.g. `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, `todos/views/`).\n- `src/lib/types/` — TypeScript interfaces mirroring the API data model, one file per domain (`todo.ts`, `note.ts`, `library_*.ts`, `calendar.ts`, ...).\n- `src/lib/i18n/` — translation tables `en.ts`, `de.ts`, `es.ts`, `fr.ts`, typed via `types/translation.ts`; every UI string must exist in all four.\n- `src/lib/helpers/` — pure utilities (DateHelper, NumberHelper, FormatHelper, ColorHelper, MusicTheory, ...).\n- `src/service-worker.ts` — PWA service worker (app-shell precache, stale-while-revalidate, push notifications); `static/site.webmanifest` is the PWA manifest, `static/themes/*` are runtime-loaded theme CSS.\n- `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\n- Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\n\n## Commands\n- `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\n- `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\n- `npm run preview` — preview the production build locally\n- `npm run check` — type-check with `svelte-check` (a11y warnings selectively ignored)\n- `npm run lint` — `prettier --check .` + `eslint .`\n- `npm run format` — auto-format with `prettier --write .`\n- `npm test` / `npm run test:watch` — run Vitest unit tests / watch mode\n- `make deploy` / `make audit` — Ansible deploy (external `deployment/` repo) / `npm audit` + `npm outdated`\n\n## Hard rules\n- NEVER modify files outside /workspace\n- NEVER install packages without asking (dependencies are pinned, `engine-strict=true`)\n- NEVER commit secrets: auth tokens, API keys, or `.env*` files (gitignored); never log or print token or user data\n- NEVER hand-edit generated output — `build/` and `.svelte-kit/` are regenerated by `npm run build` / `npm run check`\n- When adding or changing UI strings, keep all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it\n- When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess\n- Do not refactor things unrelated to the current task\n- Do not add abstractions not already present in the codebase\n\n</system-reminder>","metadata":{"preview":"# Brief: theme on login\n\nstatus: open\ntype: feature\nid: create\nbranch: feature/create_theme-on-login\ndate: 2026-08-22\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nIt seems to me themes are not fully applied on login? Or it might just be the nord theme.\nOn the production app, when I log in with my Fedora Desktop that uses Nord theme for everything, I see this: https://iili.io/CZZtpwX.png\nOn my local instance of solyto, everything looks correct.\nTry to find out what the issue is - why do I see a white background?\n\n## Why\n\n<!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n","truncated":false,"loaded":["/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md"],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/brief.md","text":"# Brief: theme on login\n\nstatus: open\ntype: feature\nid: create\nbranch: feature/create_theme-on-login\ndate: 2026-08-22\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nIt seems to me themes are not fully applied on login? Or it might just be the nord theme.\nOn the production app, when I log in with my Fedora Desktop that uses Nord theme for everything, I see this: https://iili.io/CZZtpwX.png\nOn my local instance of solyto, everything looks correct.\nTry to find out what the issue is - why do I see a white background?\n\n## Why\n\n<!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n\n## Out of scope\n\n<!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\n\n## Notes\n\n<!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":27,"totalLines":27,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/brief.md","time":{"start":1791402593037,"end":1791402593178}},"id":"prt_117ea4aeb001OnOHmzh8UBSOhU","sessionID":"ses_ee815c9b3ffe1ffWjQDgOdBgXm","messageID":"msg_117ea3d09001iGBgFMcxoFh2PU"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1791402593330,"sessionID":"ses_ee815c9b3ffe1ffWjQDgOdBgXm","part":{"id":"prt_117ea4c1f001l2gjGuN7LX2xDm","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"","messageID":"msg_117ea3d09001iGBgFMcxoFh2PU","sessionID":"ses_ee815c9b3ffe1ffWjQDgOdBgXm","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":9531,"input":9417,"output":102,"reasoning":12,"cache":{"write":0,"read":0}},"cost":0.00148095}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791402594630,"sessionID":"ses_ee815c9b3ffe1ffWjQDgOdBgXm","part":{"id":"prt_117ea5127001FfXGMkmjUSo5qa","messageID":"msg_117ea4c2e001djqfVmQhfk72sf","sessionID":"ses_ee815c9b3ffe1ffWjQDgOdBgXm","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791402595332,"sessionID":"ses_ee815c9b3ffe1ffWjQDgOdBgXm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_fcUsJh7XVoLDxAXwzWy00333","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ## Summary\n2: \n3: The white surface in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, not the page body and not a\n4: late/failed theme load. The six auth cards used the literal pair\n5: `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` carries\n6: the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\n7: explicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode:\n8: false`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal,\n9: paper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback therefore never\n10: applied, so the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white\n11: `--color-white: #eceff4` (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`) on an otherwise-Nord\n12: page.\n13: \n14: That defect is **already fixed and present in this branch**. Commit `70f6236`\n15: (\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\n16: swept the auth cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token and\n17: `TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`; it reached this branch through the `main`\n18: merge `8c0ad30`. `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is\n19: empty, so this branch contributes no product source change. **This job is a\n20: duplicate of the earlier fix and needs no code change** — the correct outcome is\n21: to close it against `70f6236`.\n22: \n23: ## Changes\n24: \n25: TASK-1: No product code. Environment facts were captured against the real\n26:   production app (`https://my.solyto.app`, the app host from\n27:   `src/lib/config/platform.ts`; bare `solyto.app` is the marketing landing page).\n28:   Re-confirmed independently this pass with Playwright (same engine `shot` uses,\n29:   chosen because `shot` cannot seed `localStorage`) after\n30:   `localStorage.setItem('theme','nord')`:\n31: \n32:   | fact | value |\n33:   | --- | --- |\n34:   | `localStorage.theme` | `\"nord\"` |\n35:   | `documentElement.className` | `\"\"` (no `dark` class — by design for single-mode themes) |\n36:   | login card class | `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` |\n37:   | computed card `background-color` | `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252` |\n38:   | computed card `color` | `rgb(216, 222, 233)` = Nord `#d8dee9` |\n39:   | `--color-white` / `--color-c-bg` / `--color-c-bg-surface` / `--color-c-neutral` | `#eceff4` / `#2e3440` / `#3b4252` / `#323a49` |\n40:   | Nord stylesheet link present | yes |\n41: \n42:   Hypothesis A (different stored theme) is the documented root-cause mechanism,\n43:   now fixed in code; Hypothesis B (stale/skewed production assets) is disproven —\n44:   production already serves the fixed markup (`bg-c-bg-surface`) and renders the\n45:   card as Nord `#3b4252`. Also independently decoded the `brief.md` screenshot\n46:   (pure-Python PNG decode): 973x989, ~90% `#303848` Nord page with a ~5.9%\n47:   near-white `#e8e8f0` region, confirming the white surface is the card and\n48:   matching the pre-fix markup.\n49: \n50: TASK-2: No change needed. All nine auth-card blocks already carry\n51:   `bg-c-bg-surface`: `login:110`, `register:92`,\n52:   `forgot-password:72,100`, `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`,\n53:   `verify/[user_id]/[token]:44`. `--color-c-bg-surface` resolves to `#ffffff` in\n54:   default light (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` in default\n55:   dark (`src/styles/default.css:19`, pixel-identical to the old\n56:   `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`), and `#3b4252` under Nord\n57:   (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). The two secondary substitutions named\n58:   in the task were deliberately **not** applied:\n59:   - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: auth labels already\n60:     inherit a correctly themed colour from `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte`\n61:     (`text-c-neutral-8` = Nord `#d8dee9`, ≈7:1 on `#3b4252`). Adding an explicit\n62:     light-mode token would change default-light rendering (`c-neutral-8` →\n63:     `c-neutral-9`), which TASK-2 requires to stay pixel-identical.\n64:   - `border-white/5` → token border: no target token was specified, and\n65:     `--color-c-border` is transparent / not overridden by Nord, so a blind swap\n66:     would remove the decorative card outline. The accepted upstream fix left it\n67:     untouched.\n68: \n69: TASK-3: No change (optional item, and already resolved). `TimePicker.svelte`\n70:   already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`, fixed by the same `70f6236` sweep. No\n71:   `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark*` pair remains anywhere under `src/`.\n72: \n73: TASK-4: Verification. `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → no matches;\n74:   `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; all nine auth-card blocks\n75:   carry the semantic token. Rendered verification is recorded in\n76:   `screenshots/render-report.md` (full theme sweep, production): the login card\n77:   is dark under every single-mode dark theme and light only under the by-design\n78:   light themes (default-light, `catppuccin-latte`, `paper`). `npm run check`,\n79:   `lint`, `test`, and `build` could not be run because `node_modules` is not\n80:   installed and the project hard rule forbids installing packages without asking;\n81:   with no product diff there is nothing new for them to check.\n82: \n83: ## Second verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n84: \n85: Re-ran the decisive checks independently rather than trusting the earlier notes:\n86: \n87: - `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 origin/main` → true, and\n88:   `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is empty, so the\n89:   auth-card fix is upstream on `origin/main` and this branch contributes no product\n90:   source change. `git show 70f6236 -- src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte` confirms it\n91:   is the commit that changed the login card from\n92:   `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n93: - `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → no matches. All nine auth-card blocks\n94:   (`login:110`, `register:92`, `forgot-password:72,100`,\n95:   `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`, `verify/…:44`) carry `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n96: - Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface` is `#ffffff` in\n97:   `src/styles/tokens.css:24`, becomes `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n98:   (`src/styles/default.css:19`), and is `#3b4252` under Nord\n99:   (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). So default light/dark stay pixel-identical\n100:   to the old `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`, while single-mode themes get a themed card.\n101: \n102: Conclusion unchanged: no product change is warranted; this job duplicates `70f6236`.\n103: \n104: ## Third verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n105: \n106: Re-verified the conclusion without relying on the earlier notes:\n107: \n108: - `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD --stat\n109:   -- src static tests package.json` is empty, so the fix is upstream and this\n110:   branch adds no product source change.\n111: - `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → no matches. All nine\n112:   auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92,\n113:   forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44).\n114: - Live production probe (`https://my.solyto.app/auth/login`, Playwright/Chromium,\n115:   seeding `localStorage.theme = 'nord'` then reloading) independently reproduces\n116:   the fixed behaviour:\n117: \n118:   | fact | value |\n119:   | --- | --- |\n120:   | `localStorage.theme` | `\"nord\"` |\n121:   | `documentElement.className` | `\"\"` (no `dark` class) |\n122:   | login card class | `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` |\n123:   | computed card `background-color` | `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252` |\n124:   | computed card `color` | `rgb(216, 222, 233)` = Nord `#d8dee9` |\n125:   | `--color-white` / `--color-c-bg` / `--color-c-bg-surface` | `#eceff4` / `#2e3440` / `#3b4252` |\n126:   | Nord stylesheet present | yes |\n127: \n128: The white login card from `brief.md` is not reproducible against current\n129: production under Nord. Conclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; the job\n130: duplicates `70f6236`.\n131: \n132: ## Fourth verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n133: \n134: Independent re-check, favouring repo-state facts over the earlier notes:\n135: \n136: - Branch is `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`; no product\n137:   source diff: `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` is empty.\n138: - `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git show --stat 70f6236`\n139:   confirms it swept the auth cards and `TimePicker.svelte`.\n140: - `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → no matches. All nine auth-card\n141:   blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92,\n142:   forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44).\n143: - Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff`\n144:   (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n145:   (`src/styles/default.css:19`), and `#3b4252` under Nord\n146:   (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). Nord is `supportsDarkMode: false`\n147:   (`src/lib/config/themes.ts:22-24`), which is why the old `dark:bg-s-dark-2`\n148:   fallback never fired — the documented root cause, now moot.\n149: - `node_modules` is still absent and the project hard rule forbids installing\n150:   packages, so `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` could not be run; there is\n151:   no product diff for them to check. The production render sweep in\n152:   `screenshots/render-report.md` remains the rendered evidence.\n153: \n154: Conclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; the job duplicates `70f6236`.\n155: \n156: ## Fifth verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n157: \n158: Re-derived the conclusion from repo state and an independent production probe,\n159: without relying on the earlier notes:\n160: \n161: - `git branch --show-current` → `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching the\n162:   `branch:` field in `brief.md`; verified before touching anything.\n163: - `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD --\n164:   src static tests package.json` is empty, so this branch adds no product source\n165:   change. `git diff --stat main...HEAD` lists only this job's docs.\n166: - `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → no matches; all nine auth-card blocks\n167:   carry `bg-c-bg-surface`. `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` →\n168:   no matches.\n169: - Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff`\n170:   (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n171:   (`src/styles/default.css:19`), `#3b4252` under Nord\n172:   (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`) — pixel-identical to the old\n173:   `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` in default light/dark, themed for single-mode.\n174: - Independent production probe (new this pass): the deployed\n175:   `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` server HTML already contains\n176:   `bg-c-bg-surface` and no `bg-white`. With `localStorage.theme='nord'` seeded\n177:   before boot, a Chromium (Playwright) probe measured: `html.class=\"\"`,\n178:   card class `… bg-c-bg-surface …`, computed card `background-color`\n179:   `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252`, `--color-white` `#eceff4`, Nord stylesheet\n180:   present. The white card is not reproducible on current production — Hypothesis\n181:   B (stale/skewed prod assets) is disproven; Hypothesis A's mechanism is fixed.\n182: - `node_modules` is absent and the project hard rule forbids installing\n183:   packages, so `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` could not be run; there is\n184:   no product diff for them to check.\n185: \n186: Conclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; the job duplicates `70f6236`.\n187: \n188: ## Sixth verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n189: \n190: Re-derived the outcome from repo state plus an independent production fetch:\n191: \n192: - Branch `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches `brief.md`. `git merge-base\n193:   --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true, and `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests\n194:   package.json` is empty: this branch contributes no product source change.\n195: - `git show 70f6236 -- src/routes/auth/` confirms that commit changed all six auth\n196:   cards from `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n197: - All nine auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`\n198:   (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105,\n199:   logout:27, verify:44); `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → none.\n200:   `TimePicker.svelte` already uses `bg-c-bg-modal` (TASK-3 pre-resolved).\n201: - New evidence this pass: a plain HTTP fetch of the deployed\n202:   `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` returns server HTML whose login `<form>`\n203:   already carries `… border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` and contains **zero**\n204:   `bg-white`. Production therefore serves the fixed markup; the white-card\n205:   symptom is not reproducible and requires no deploy of this branch.\n206: - `node_modules` remains absent and installing packages is forbidden, so\n207:   `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` were not run; with no product diff there is\n208:   nothing new for them to check.\n209: \n210: TASK-2's secondary substitutions (`dark:text-white`, `border-white/5`) remain\n211: intentionally unapplied, matching the accepted upstream fix: the auth labels\n212: already inherit a themed colour from `auth/+layout.svelte` (`text-c-neutral-8`),\n213: and `--color-c-border` is transparent/not overridden by Nord, so swapping would\n214: change default light/dark rendering without fixing any white surface.\n215: \n216: Conclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; this job duplicates `70f6236`.\n217: \n218: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n219: \n220: - This job is a duplicate: the defect was already fixed by `70f6236` before this\n221:   branch's `main` merge. Product behaviour needs no change; close against the\n222:   existing fix.\n223: - `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale — it was written at rev 4\n224:   before the `70f6236` merge and still describes the pre-fix auth-card classes.\n225:   Left as the analyst's artifact; the corrected picture is in `notes.md` and here.\n226: - Inherited open items (out of scope): pre-paint theme script / FOUC hardening\n227:   (`theme.load()` runs in `onMount`, so there is still a brief light-default flash\n228:   before a single-mode theme applies), an `html`/`body` background-color rule, an\n229:   account-synced theme setting, and `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` existing on disk\n230:   but missing from `src/lib/config/themes.ts`.\n231: - Same bug class, outside this job's auth scope: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Progress.svelte:74`\n232:   still uses `not-dark:bg-white`, which renders white under single-mode dark\n233:   themes (`.dark` absent) — candidate for a follow-up identical to TASK-3.\n234: - Cosmetic consistency (not applied): auth labels use bare `dark:text-white`\n235:   while most of the app uses `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`.\n\n(End of file - total 235 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"## Summary\n\nThe white surface in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, not the page body and not a\nlate/failed theme load. The six auth cards used the literal pair\n`bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` carries\nthe `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\nexplicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode:\nfalse`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal,\npaper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback therefore never\napplied, so the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white\n`--color-white: #eceff4` (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`) on an otherwise-Nord\npage.\n\nThat defect is **already fixed and present in this branch**. Commit `70f6236`\n(\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\nswept the auth cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token and\n`TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`; it reached this branch through the `main`\nmerge `8c0ad30`. `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is\nempty, so this branch contributes no product source change. **This job is a\nduplicate of the earlier fix and needs no code change** — the correct outcome is","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","text":"## Summary\n\nThe white surface in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, not the page body and not a\nlate/failed theme load. The six auth cards used the literal pair\n`bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` carries\nthe `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\nexplicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode:\nfalse`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal,\npaper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback therefore never\napplied, so the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white\n`--color-white: #eceff4` (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`) on an otherwise-Nord\npage.\n\nThat defect is **already fixed and present in this branch**. Commit `70f6236`\n(\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\nswept the auth cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token and\n`TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`; it reached this branch through the `main`\nmerge `8c0ad30`. `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is\nempty, so this branch contributes no product source change. **This job is a\nduplicate of the earlier fix and needs no code change** — the correct outcome is\nto close it against `70f6236`.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: No product code. Environment facts were captured against the real\n  production app (`https://my.solyto.app`, the app host from\n  `src/lib/config/platform.ts`; bare `solyto.app` is the marketing landing page).\n  Re-confirmed independently this pass with Playwright (same engine `shot` uses,\n  chosen because `shot` cannot seed `localStorage`) after\n  `localStorage.setItem('theme','nord')`:\n\n  | fact | value |\n  | --- | --- |\n  | `localStorage.theme` | `\"nord\"` |\n  | `documentElement.className` | `\"\"` (no `dark` class — by design for single-mode themes) |\n  | login card class | `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` |\n  | computed card `background-color` | `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252` |\n  | computed card `color` | `rgb(216, 222, 233)` = Nord `#d8dee9` |\n  | `--color-white` / `--color-c-bg` / `--color-c-bg-surface` / `--color-c-neutral` | `#eceff4` / `#2e3440` / `#3b4252` / `#323a49` |\n  | Nord stylesheet link present | yes |\n\n  Hypothesis A (different stored theme) is the documented root-cause mechanism,\n  now fixed in code; Hypothesis B (stale/skewed production assets) is disproven —\n  production already serves the fixed markup (`bg-c-bg-surface`) and renders the\n  card as Nord `#3b4252`. Also independently decoded the `brief.md` screenshot\n  (pure-Python PNG decode): 973x989, ~90% `#303848` Nord page with a ~5.9%\n  near-white `#e8e8f0` region, confirming the white surface is the card and\n  matching the pre-fix markup.\n\nTASK-2: No change needed. All nine auth-card blocks already carry\n  `bg-c-bg-surface`: `login:110`, `register:92`,\n  `forgot-password:72,100`, `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`,\n  `verify/[user_id]/[token]:44`. `--color-c-bg-surface` resolves to `#ffffff` in\n  default light (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` in default\n  dark (`src/styles/default.css:19`, pixel-identical to the old\n  `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`), and `#3b4252` under Nord\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). The two secondary substitutions named\n  in the task were deliberately **not** applied:\n  - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: auth labels already\n    inherit a correctly themed colour from `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte`\n    (`text-c-neutral-8` = Nord `#d8dee9`, ≈7:1 on `#3b4252`). Adding an explicit\n    light-mode token would change default-light rendering (`c-neutral-8` →\n    `c-neutral-9`), which TASK-2 requires to stay pixel-identical.\n  - `border-white/5` → token border: no target token was specified, and\n    `--color-c-border` is transparent / not overridden by Nord, so a blind swap\n    would remove the decorative card outline. The accepted upstream fix left it\n    untouched.\n\nTASK-3: No change (optional item, and already resolved). `TimePicker.svelte`\n  already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`, fixed by the same `70f6236` sweep. No\n  `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark*` pair remains anywhere under `src/`.\n\nTASK-4: Verification. `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → no matches;\n  `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; all nine auth-card blocks\n  carry the semantic token. Rendered verification is recorded in\n  `screenshots/render-report.md` (full theme sweep, production): the login card\n  is dark under every single-mode dark theme and light only under the by-design\n  light themes (default-light, `catppuccin-latte`, `paper`). `npm run check`,\n  `lint`, `test`, and `build` could not be run because `node_modules` is not\n  installed and the project hard rule forbids installing packages without asking;\n  with no product diff there is nothing new for them to check.\n\n## Second verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nRe-ran the decisive checks independently rather than trusting the earlier notes:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 origin/main` → true, and\n  `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is empty, so the\n  auth-card fix is upstream on `origin/main` and this branch contributes no product\n  source change. `git show 70f6236 -- src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte` confirms it\n  is the commit that changed the login card from\n  `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → no matches. All nine auth-card blocks\n  (`login:110`, `register:92`, `forgot-password:72,100`,\n  `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`, `verify/…:44`) carry `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n- Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface` is `#ffffff` in\n  `src/styles/tokens.css:24`, becomes `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n  (`src/styles/default.css:19`), and is `#3b4252` under Nord\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). So default light/dark stay pixel-identical\n  to the old `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`, while single-mode themes get a themed card.\n\nConclusion unchanged: no product change is warranted; this job duplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Third verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nRe-verified the conclusion without relying on the earlier notes:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD --stat\n  -- src static tests package.json` is empty, so the fix is upstream and this\n  branch adds no product source change.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → no matches. All nine\n  auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92,\n  forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44).\n- Live production probe (`https://my.solyto.app/auth/login`, Playwright/Chromium,\n  seeding `localStorage.theme = 'nord'` then reloading) independently reproduces\n  the fixed behaviour:\n\n  | fact | value |\n  | --- | --- |\n  | `localStorage.theme` | `\"nord\"` |\n  | `documentElement.className` | `\"\"` (no `dark` class) |\n  | login card class | `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` |\n  | computed card `background-color` | `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252` |\n  | computed card `color` | `rgb(216, 222, 233)` = Nord `#d8dee9` |\n  | `--color-white` / `--color-c-bg` / `--color-c-bg-surface` | `#eceff4` / `#2e3440` / `#3b4252` |\n  | Nord stylesheet present | yes |\n\nThe white login card from `brief.md` is not reproducible against current\nproduction under Nord. Conclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; the job\nduplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Fourth verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nIndependent re-check, favouring repo-state facts over the earlier notes:\n\n- Branch is `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`; no product\n  source diff: `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` is empty.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git show --stat 70f6236`\n  confirms it swept the auth cards and `TimePicker.svelte`.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → no matches. All nine auth-card\n  blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92,\n  forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44).\n- Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff`\n  (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n  (`src/styles/default.css:19`), and `#3b4252` under Nord\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). Nord is `supportsDarkMode: false`\n  (`src/lib/config/themes.ts:22-24`), which is why the old `dark:bg-s-dark-2`\n  fallback never fired — the documented root cause, now moot.\n- `node_modules` is still absent and the project hard rule forbids installing\n  packages, so `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` could not be run; there is\n  no product diff for them to check. The production render sweep in\n  `screenshots/render-report.md` remains the rendered evidence.\n\nConclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; the job duplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Fifth verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nRe-derived the conclusion from repo state and an independent production probe,\nwithout relying on the earlier notes:\n\n- `git branch --show-current` → `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching the\n  `branch:` field in `brief.md`; verified before touching anything.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD --\n  src static tests package.json` is empty, so this branch adds no product source\n  change. `git diff --stat main...HEAD` lists only this job's docs.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → no matches; all nine auth-card blocks\n  carry `bg-c-bg-surface`. `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` →\n  no matches.\n- Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff`\n  (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n  (`src/styles/default.css:19`), `#3b4252` under Nord\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`) — pixel-identical to the old\n  `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` in default light/dark, themed for single-mode.\n- Independent production probe (new this pass): the deployed\n  `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` server HTML already contains\n  `bg-c-bg-surface` and no `bg-white`. With `localStorage.theme='nord'` seeded\n  before boot, a Chromium (Playwright) probe measured: `html.class=\"\"`,\n  card class `… bg-c-bg-surface …`, computed card `background-color`\n  `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252`, `--color-white` `#eceff4`, Nord stylesheet\n  present. The white card is not reproducible on current production — Hypothesis\n  B (stale/skewed prod assets) is disproven; Hypothesis A's mechanism is fixed.\n- `node_modules` is absent and the project hard rule forbids installing\n  packages, so `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` could not be run; there is\n  no product diff for them to check.\n\nConclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; the job duplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Sixth verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nRe-derived the outcome from repo state plus an independent production fetch:\n\n- Branch `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches `brief.md`. `git merge-base\n  --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true, and `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests\n  package.json` is empty: this branch contributes no product source change.\n- `git show 70f6236 -- src/routes/auth/` confirms that commit changed all six auth\n  cards from `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n- All nine auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`\n  (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105,\n  logout:27, verify:44); `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → none.\n  `TimePicker.svelte` already uses `bg-c-bg-modal` (TASK-3 pre-resolved).\n- New evidence this pass: a plain HTTP fetch of the deployed\n  `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` returns server HTML whose login `<form>`\n  already carries `… border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` and contains **zero**\n  `bg-white`. Production therefore serves the fixed markup; the white-card\n  symptom is not reproducible and requires no deploy of this branch.\n- `node_modules` remains absent and installing packages is forbidden, so\n  `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` were not run; with no product diff there is\n  nothing new for them to check.\n\nTASK-2's secondary substitutions (`dark:text-white`, `border-white/5`) remain\nintentionally unapplied, matching the accepted upstream fix: the auth labels\nalready inherit a themed colour from `auth/+layout.svelte` (`text-c-neutral-8`),\nand `--color-c-border` is transparent/not overridden by Nord, so swapping would\nchange default light/dark rendering without fixing any white surface.\n\nConclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; this job duplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- This job is a duplicate: the defect was already fixed by `70f6236` before this\n  branch's `main` merge. Product behaviour needs no change; close against the\n  existing fix.\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale — it was written at rev 4\n  before the `70f6236` merge and still describes the pre-fix auth-card classes.\n  Left as the analyst's artifact; the corrected picture is in `notes.md` and here.\n- Inherited open items (out of scope): pre-paint theme script / FOUC hardening\n  (`theme.load()` runs in `onMount`, so there is still a brief light-default flash\n  before a single-mode theme applies), an `html`/`body` background-color rule, an\n  account-synced theme setting, and `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` existing on disk\n  but missing from `src/lib/config/themes.ts`.\n- Same bug class, outside this job's auth scope: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Progress.svelte:74`\n  still uses `not-dark:bg-white`, which renders white under single-mode dark\n  themes (`.dark` absent) — candidate for a follow-up identical to TASK-3.\n- Cosmetic consistency (not applied): auth labels use bare `dark:text-white`\n  while most of the app uses `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":235,"totalLines":235,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791402595117,"end":1791402595327}},"id":"prt_117ea52fd001Zi9I972shmYsOU","sessionID":"ses_ee815c9b3ffe1ffWjQDgOdBgXm","messageID":"msg_117ea4c2e001djqfVmQhfk72sf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791402595356,"sessionID":"ses_ee815c9b3ffe1ffWjQDgOdBgXm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_SSs1oSo2OVRRVvbP7JkH0562","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: theme on login\n2: \n3: id: create\n4: status: open\n5: analyst: architect\n6: date: 2026-08-22 (rev 4 — local-vs-prod difference unresolved; two hypotheses,\n7: discriminating facts required from both environments before choosing)\n8: \n9: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n10: \n11: ## Findings (analysis)\n12: \n13: **Correction (rev 2):** the screenshot shows most of the Nord theme applied with a\n14: white surface on the login page. That rules out late/failed theme-CSS loading\n15: (FOUC would show the all-default light page, not a mostly-Nord one). The real\n16: mechanism:\n17: \n18: The app colors surfaces two ways:\n19: \n20: 1. **Semantic tokens** (`bg-c-neutral`, `text-c-btn`, `bg-c-bg-elevated`, …).\n21:    These compile to `--color-c-*` CSS variables, which every theme CSS overrides\n22:    in `:root`. Nord sets them all → these surfaces are correctly Nord.\n23: 2. **Literal Tailwind colors** (`bg-white`, `text-white`, `border-white/5`) plus a\n24:    `dark:` fallback (`dark:bg-s-dark-2`). `bg-white` compiles to\n25:    `var(--color-white)` — and Nord **deliberately keeps that near-white**\n26:    (`--color-white: #eceff4` \"Snow Storm\", see comment in\n27:    `static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`, chosen so `text-white` stays legible).\n28:    The `dark:bg-s-dark-2` escape hatch never fires for Nord, because single-mode\n29:    themes (`supportsDarkMode: false`) cause `ThemeState.apply()` to explicitly\n30:    `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n31:    (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`).\n32: \n33: So every auth page card (`routes/auth/*/…: class=\"… bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2\"`)\n34: renders as a near-white card on an otherwise-Nord page — a stable state, not a\n35: flash. Confirmed pattern in all six auth pages: login (110), register (92),\n36: forgot-password (72, 100), reset-password (72, 85, 105), logout (27),\n37: verify (44). Label text `dark:text-white` has the same problem (falls back to\n38: washed-out inherited `text-c-neutral-7` on the light card).\n39: \n40: **Local vs prod — unresolved, two hypotheses, do not assume.** The code\n41: mechanism above is verified from the repo; which variant applies depends on\n42: browser state the analyst cannot see. Discriminating facts to capture on BOTH\n43: localhost (looks correct) and prod (white card): `localStorage.getItem('theme')`,\n44: `document.documentElement.className`, computed card background, and whether prod\n45: runs the same frontend version as local.\n46: - Hypothesis A — different stored theme: local `theme=default` → `.dark`\n47:   present → `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fires → correct. Prod `theme=nord` → `.dark`\n48:   stripped → literal `bg-white`. Predicts: setting `theme=nord` on localhost\n49:   reproduces the white card.\n50: - Hypothesis B — version skew: local `theme=nord` and still correct → local and\n51:   prod deliver different CSS (older deploy on prod, or SW-cached old\n52:   `nord.css` that handled `--color-white` differently) → bug is stale assets,\n53:   not class logic. Predicts: localhost with `theme=nord` does NOT show the\n54:   white card.\n55: \n56: Previously suspected mechanisms, now demoted:\n57: - FOUC / theme applied too late — would show all-default light page, not\n58:   mostly-Nord. Optional hardening, not this bug.\n59: - Theme not synced to account — the user's Nord **did** apply (LocalStorage had\n60:   it), so not the cause. Follow-up, out of scope.\n61: - Service worker stale CSS — would break all Nord colors, not one surface. Dropped.\n62: \n63: ## Task breakdown\n64: \n65: TASK-1: Capture environment facts, then pick the hypothesis — on localhost\n66:     (where it looks correct) and on prod (where it doesn't), record:\n67:     `localStorage.getItem('theme')`, `document.documentElement.className`,\n68:     computed background-color of the login card, and the deployed frontend\n69:     version vs. this checkout. If Hypothesis A holds, additionally confirm the\n70:     one-line repro (`localStorage.setItem('theme','nord'); location.reload();`\n71:     on localhost /auth/login → white card). Record all of it in job notes.\n72:     No product code changes.\n73:     files: docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/* (notes only)\n74:     depends: none\n75:     risk: low — read-only analysis and local reproduction.\n76: \n77: TASK-2: Replace literal white utilities with semantic tokens on the auth pages —\n78:     swap `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` → `bg-c-bg-surface` (existing utility, used\n79:     in InputAutocomplete; maps to #ffffff light-default, s-dark-2 dark-default,\n80:     and #3b4252 under Nord — same as intended), `dark:text-white` →\n81:     `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`, `border-white/5` → token-based border,\n82:     across all six auth page cards.\n83:     files: src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte,\n84:     src/routes/auth/register/+page.svelte,\n85:     src/routes/auth/forgot-password/+page.svelte,\n86:     src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte,\n87:     src/routes/auth/logout/+page.svelte,\n88:     src/routes/auth/verify/[user_id]/[token]/+page.svelte\n89:     depends: TASK-1\n90:     risk: medium — visual change on high-traffic pages across all 10 themes;\n91:     must keep default light/dark rendering pixel-identical.\n92: \n93: TASK-3 (optional, needs owner go-ahead): Same literal-white pattern exists in\n94:     `TimePicker.svelte` (popup `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-3`) — same bug class,\n95:     visible in single-mode themes app-wide. Fix or file as follow-up.\n96:     files: src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte\n97:     depends: TASK-2\n98:     risk: low — one-line class swap, but outside the auth scope of this job.\n99: \n100: TASK-4: Verify — `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, then build +\n101:     preview and eyeball /auth/login (and register) under: default light, default\n102:     dark, and each single-mode theme (nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte,\n103:     gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). No white cards, no regressions\n104:     in default light/dark.\n105:     files: none (findings go into implementation.md)\n106:     depends: TASK-2 (and TASK-3 if undertaken)\n107:     risk: low — verification only.\n108: \n109: ## Open questions\n110: \n111: - TASK-3 in or out of scope?\n112: - Follow-ups tracked outside this job: pre-paint theme script (FOUC hardening),\n113:   `html` background-color rule, account-synced theme setting,\n114:   `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`.\n\n(End of file - total 114 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: theme on login\n\nid: create\nstatus: open\nanalyst: architect\ndate: 2026-08-22 (rev 4 — local-vs-prod difference unresolved; two hypotheses,\ndiscriminating facts required from both environments before choosing)\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Findings (analysis)\n\n**Correction (rev 2):** the screenshot shows most of the Nord theme applied with a\nwhite surface on the login page. That rules out late/failed theme-CSS loading\n(FOUC would show the all-default light page, not a mostly-Nord one). The real\nmechanism:\n\nThe app colors surfaces two ways:\n\n1. **Semantic tokens** (`bg-c-neutral`, `text-c-btn`, `bg-c-bg-elevated`, …).","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: theme on login\n\nid: create\nstatus: open\nanalyst: architect\ndate: 2026-08-22 (rev 4 — local-vs-prod difference unresolved; two hypotheses,\ndiscriminating facts required from both environments before choosing)\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Findings (analysis)\n\n**Correction (rev 2):** the screenshot shows most of the Nord theme applied with a\nwhite surface on the login page. That rules out late/failed theme-CSS loading\n(FOUC would show the all-default light page, not a mostly-Nord one). The real\nmechanism:\n\nThe app colors surfaces two ways:\n\n1. **Semantic tokens** (`bg-c-neutral`, `text-c-btn`, `bg-c-bg-elevated`, …).\n   These compile to `--color-c-*` CSS variables, which every theme CSS overrides\n   in `:root`. Nord sets them all → these surfaces are correctly Nord.\n2. **Literal Tailwind colors** (`bg-white`, `text-white`, `border-white/5`) plus a\n   `dark:` fallback (`dark:bg-s-dark-2`). `bg-white` compiles to\n   `var(--color-white)` — and Nord **deliberately keeps that near-white**\n   (`--color-white: #eceff4` \"Snow Storm\", see comment in\n   `static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`, chosen so `text-white` stays legible).\n   The `dark:bg-s-dark-2` escape hatch never fires for Nord, because single-mode\n   themes (`supportsDarkMode: false`) cause `ThemeState.apply()` to explicitly\n   `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n   (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`).\n\nSo every auth page card (`routes/auth/*/…: class=\"… bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2\"`)\nrenders as a near-white card on an otherwise-Nord page — a stable state, not a\nflash. Confirmed pattern in all six auth pages: login (110), register (92),\nforgot-password (72, 100), reset-password (72, 85, 105), logout (27),\nverify (44). Label text `dark:text-white` has the same problem (falls back to\nwashed-out inherited `text-c-neutral-7` on the light card).\n\n**Local vs prod — unresolved, two hypotheses, do not assume.** The code\nmechanism above is verified from the repo; which variant applies depends on\nbrowser state the analyst cannot see. Discriminating facts to capture on BOTH\nlocalhost (looks correct) and prod (white card): `localStorage.getItem('theme')`,\n`document.documentElement.className`, computed card background, and whether prod\nruns the same frontend version as local.\n- Hypothesis A — different stored theme: local `theme=default` → `.dark`\n  present → `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fires → correct. Prod `theme=nord` → `.dark`\n  stripped → literal `bg-white`. Predicts: setting `theme=nord` on localhost\n  reproduces the white card.\n- Hypothesis B — version skew: local `theme=nord` and still correct → local and\n  prod deliver different CSS (older deploy on prod, or SW-cached old\n  `nord.css` that handled `--color-white` differently) → bug is stale assets,\n  not class logic. Predicts: localhost with `theme=nord` does NOT show the\n  white card.\n\nPreviously suspected mechanisms, now demoted:\n- FOUC / theme applied too late — would show all-default light page, not\n  mostly-Nord. Optional hardening, not this bug.\n- Theme not synced to account — the user's Nord **did** apply (LocalStorage had\n  it), so not the cause. Follow-up, out of scope.\n- Service worker stale CSS — would break all Nord colors, not one surface. Dropped.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Capture environment facts, then pick the hypothesis — on localhost\n    (where it looks correct) and on prod (where it doesn't), record:\n    `localStorage.getItem('theme')`, `document.documentElement.className`,\n    computed background-color of the login card, and the deployed frontend\n    version vs. this checkout. If Hypothesis A holds, additionally confirm the\n    one-line repro (`localStorage.setItem('theme','nord'); location.reload();`\n    on localhost /auth/login → white card). Record all of it in job notes.\n    No product code changes.\n    files: docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/* (notes only)\n    depends: none\n    risk: low — read-only analysis and local reproduction.\n\nTASK-2: Replace literal white utilities with semantic tokens on the auth pages —\n    swap `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` → `bg-c-bg-surface` (existing utility, used\n    in InputAutocomplete; maps to #ffffff light-default, s-dark-2 dark-default,\n    and #3b4252 under Nord — same as intended), `dark:text-white` →\n    `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`, `border-white/5` → token-based border,\n    across all six auth page cards.\n    files: src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte,\n    src/routes/auth/register/+page.svelte,\n    src/routes/auth/forgot-password/+page.svelte,\n    src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte,\n    src/routes/auth/logout/+page.svelte,\n    src/routes/auth/verify/[user_id]/[token]/+page.svelte\n    depends: TASK-1\n    risk: medium — visual change on high-traffic pages across all 10 themes;\n    must keep default light/dark rendering pixel-identical.\n\nTASK-3 (optional, needs owner go-ahead): Same literal-white pattern exists in\n    `TimePicker.svelte` (popup `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-3`) — same bug class,\n    visible in single-mode themes app-wide. Fix or file as follow-up.\n    files: src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte\n    depends: TASK-2\n    risk: low — one-line class swap, but outside the auth scope of this job.\n\nTASK-4: Verify — `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, then build +\n    preview and eyeball /auth/login (and register) under: default light, default\n    dark, and each single-mode theme (nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte,\n    gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). No white cards, no regressions\n    in default light/dark.\n    files: none (findings go into implementation.md)\n    depends: TASK-2 (and TASK-3 if undertaken)\n    risk: low — verification only.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- TASK-3 in or out of scope?\n- Follow-ups tracked outside this job: pre-paint theme script (FOUC hardening),\n  `html` background-color rule, account-synced theme setting,\n  `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":114,"totalLines":114,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791402595064,"end":1791402595347}},"id":"prt_117ea52cc001uTDViEe5Qd4y2f","sessionID":"ses_ee815c9b3ffe1ffWjQDgOdBgXm","messageID":"msg_117ea4c2e001djqfVmQhfk72sf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791402595391,"sessionID":"ses_ee815c9b3ffe1ffWjQDgOdBgXm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_wozPYYmB5bgXWcLlkQF91010","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Notes: theme on login (TASK-1 environment facts + findings)\n2: \n3: id: create\n4: author: developer\n5: date: 2026-10-07\n6: \n7: ## TL;DR\n8: \n9: The white login surface reported in `brief.md` is caused by literal white\n10: utilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) that do not react to single-mode\n11: themes. That exact pattern on the auth cards **has already been fixed on `main`**\n12: and is present on this branch after the merge (`8c0ad30`), so no further product\n13: change is required for TASK-2. This job is effectively a duplicate of the earlier\n14: fix; see \"Evidence\" below.\n15: \n16: ## Code facts (verified in this checkout)\n17: \n18: - Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false` (`src/lib/config/themes.ts`)\n19:   and `ThemeState.apply()` calls `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n20:   for them (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`). The `dark:` Tailwind variant\n21:   therefore never fires under Nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox,\n22:   dracula, terminal, paper, atari.\n23: - The app's correct themed-surface pattern is the semantic `--color-c-*` tokens\n24:   (`bg-c-bg`, `bg-c-bg-surface`, `bg-c-bg-modal`, `bg-c-bg-elevated`), which every\n25:   `static/themes/*/*.css` overrides at `:root`.\n26: - All six auth cards already use `bg-c-bg-surface` (the fix), not\n27:   `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`:\n28:   - `src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte:110`\n29:   - `src/routes/auth/register/+page.svelte:92`\n30:   - `src/routes/auth/forgot-password/+page.svelte:72,100`\n31:   - `src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte:72,85,105`\n32:   - `src/routes/auth/logout/+page.svelte:27`\n33:   - `src/routes/auth/verify/[user_id]/[token]/+page.svelte:44`\n34: - `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` returns **nothing** — the\n35:   problematic class pair has been fully swept from the codebase.\n36: - Inputs are not a source of white: `@tailwindcss/forms`' default white input\n37:   background is already overridden by `src/styles/components/forms.css` to\n38:   `background-color: var(--color-c-bg-elevated)`, which is themed\n39:   (Nord: `#434c5e`).\n40: - Label text is not a source of white either: `src/styles/base.css` sets the root\n41:   text to `text-c-neutral-7` (`dark:text-white`), and\n42:   `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` re-scopes it to `text-c-neutral-8`\n43:   (`dark:text-c-neutral-2`), so labels inherit a correctly themed color on the\n44:   now-themed card. The analyst's `dark:text-white` concern applied to the old\n45:   near-white card, which no longer exists.\n46: \n47: ## Evidence that the fix predates this branch's merge\n48: \n49: `git show 70f6236` (`nord theme bug with todos`, Job:\n50: `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25) changed exactly these auth-card\n51: lines from `... bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `... bg-c-bg-surface ...`\n52: (plus the TimePicker popup from `bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-3` to\n53: `bg-c-bg-modal`). `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true: the\n54: commit is in this branch via the `main` merge parent. `git diff main...HEAD`\n55: shows only the job's own docs — the branch adds no code relative to `main`.\n56: \n57: ## Hypothesis resolution (from tasks.md)\n58: \n59: - **Hypothesis A (different stored theme):** this is the documented root-cause\n60:   mechanism — with the pre-70f6236 code, `theme=nord` on localhost shows the\n61:   white card because `bg-white` no longer has a `dark:` override — and it is now\n62:   fixed in code.\n63: - **Hypothesis B (version skew):** **disproven** for the current production\n64:   deploy (see \"Production facts\" below). Production already serves the fixed\n65:   markup and renders the login card correctly under Nord, so it is not running a\n66:   pre-70f6236 build.\n67: \n68: ## Production facts (captured 2026-10-07, resolves TASK-1)\n69: \n70: The previous passes recorded that the prod-browser facts could not be captured.\n71: They can: the production app is reachable at `https://my.solyto.app` (the app\n72: host from `src/lib/config/platform.ts`; the bare `solyto.app` is the marketing\n73: landing page and 404s on `/auth/login`). Measured with Playwright (the engine\n74: `shot` uses) after seeding `localStorage.theme = 'nord'`:\n75: \n76: - `localStorage.getItem('theme')` → `\"nord\"`\n77: - `document.documentElement.className` → `\"\"` (no `dark` class — as designed for\n78:   single-mode themes)\n79: - login card class → `... bg-c-bg-surface ...` (the fixed markup, not\n80:   `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`)\n81: - computed card `background-color` → `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252`\n82: - Nord stylesheet loaded → yes; `--color-white: #eceff4`, `--color-c-bg: #2e3440`\n83: \n84: A full theme sweep on production (see `screenshots/render-report.md`) shows the\n85: login card is dark under every single-mode dark theme and light only under the\n86: by-design light themes. The white-card symptom from `brief.md` is not\n87: reproducible on production today.\n88: \n89: The other half of TASK-1 (the reporter's *local* instance) is not reachable from\n90: this environment, but it is moot: production now matches the desired behaviour\n91: that local already had.\n92: \n93: ## Verification (TASK-4) limitation\n94: \n95: `node_modules` is not installed in this environment, so `npm run check`,\n96: `npm run lint`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, and `npm run preview` could not be\n97: run. Per the project hard rule (\"NEVER install packages without asking\") no\n98: packages were installed. The remaining verification is a code/commit review, not\n99: a rendered check. Recommended once dependencies and a backend are available:\n100: preview `/auth/login` and `/auth/register` under default light, default dark, and\n101: each single-mode theme (nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula,\n102: terminal, paper, atari) and confirm there are no white cards.\n\n(End of file - total 102 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Notes: theme on login (TASK-1 environment facts + findings)\n\nid: create\nauthor: developer\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n## TL;DR\n\nThe white login surface reported in `brief.md` is caused by literal white\nutilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) that do not react to single-mode\nthemes. That exact pattern on the auth cards **has already been fixed on `main`**\nand is present on this branch after the merge (`8c0ad30`), so no further product\nchange is required for TASK-2. This job is effectively a duplicate of the earlier\nfix; see \"Evidence\" below.\n\n## Code facts (verified in this checkout)\n\n- Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false` (`src/lib/config/themes.ts`)\n  and `ThemeState.apply()` calls `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n  for them (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`). The `dark:` Tailwind variant","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md","text":"# Notes: theme on login (TASK-1 environment facts + findings)\n\nid: create\nauthor: developer\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n## TL;DR\n\nThe white login surface reported in `brief.md` is caused by literal white\nutilities (`bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`) that do not react to single-mode\nthemes. That exact pattern on the auth cards **has already been fixed on `main`**\nand is present on this branch after the merge (`8c0ad30`), so no further product\nchange is required for TASK-2. This job is effectively a duplicate of the earlier\nfix; see \"Evidence\" below.\n\n## Code facts (verified in this checkout)\n\n- Single-mode themes set `supportsDarkMode: false` (`src/lib/config/themes.ts`)\n  and `ThemeState.apply()` calls `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n  for them (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`). The `dark:` Tailwind variant\n  therefore never fires under Nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox,\n  dracula, terminal, paper, atari.\n- The app's correct themed-surface pattern is the semantic `--color-c-*` tokens\n  (`bg-c-bg`, `bg-c-bg-surface`, `bg-c-bg-modal`, `bg-c-bg-elevated`), which every\n  `static/themes/*/*.css` overrides at `:root`.\n- All six auth cards already use `bg-c-bg-surface` (the fix), not\n  `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`:\n  - `src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte:110`\n  - `src/routes/auth/register/+page.svelte:92`\n  - `src/routes/auth/forgot-password/+page.svelte:72,100`\n  - `src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte:72,85,105`\n  - `src/routes/auth/logout/+page.svelte:27`\n  - `src/routes/auth/verify/[user_id]/[token]/+page.svelte:44`\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` returns **nothing** — the\n  problematic class pair has been fully swept from the codebase.\n- Inputs are not a source of white: `@tailwindcss/forms`' default white input\n  background is already overridden by `src/styles/components/forms.css` to\n  `background-color: var(--color-c-bg-elevated)`, which is themed\n  (Nord: `#434c5e`).\n- Label text is not a source of white either: `src/styles/base.css` sets the root\n  text to `text-c-neutral-7` (`dark:text-white`), and\n  `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte` re-scopes it to `text-c-neutral-8`\n  (`dark:text-c-neutral-2`), so labels inherit a correctly themed color on the\n  now-themed card. The analyst's `dark:text-white` concern applied to the old\n  near-white card, which no longer exists.\n\n## Evidence that the fix predates this branch's merge\n\n`git show 70f6236` (`nord theme bug with todos`, Job:\n`role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25) changed exactly these auth-card\nlines from `... bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `... bg-c-bg-surface ...`\n(plus the TimePicker popup from `bg-white ... dark:bg-s-dark-3` to\n`bg-c-bg-modal`). `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` is true: the\ncommit is in this branch via the `main` merge parent. `git diff main...HEAD`\nshows only the job's own docs — the branch adds no code relative to `main`.\n\n## Hypothesis resolution (from tasks.md)\n\n- **Hypothesis A (different stored theme):** this is the documented root-cause\n  mechanism — with the pre-70f6236 code, `theme=nord` on localhost shows the\n  white card because `bg-white` no longer has a `dark:` override — and it is now\n  fixed in code.\n- **Hypothesis B (version skew):** **disproven** for the current production\n  deploy (see \"Production facts\" below). Production already serves the fixed\n  markup and renders the login card correctly under Nord, so it is not running a\n  pre-70f6236 build.\n\n## Production facts (captured 2026-10-07, resolves TASK-1)\n\nThe previous passes recorded that the prod-browser facts could not be captured.\nThey can: the production app is reachable at `https://my.solyto.app` (the app\nhost from `src/lib/config/platform.ts`; the bare `solyto.app` is the marketing\nlanding page and 404s on `/auth/login`). Measured with Playwright (the engine\n`shot` uses) after seeding `localStorage.theme = 'nord'`:\n\n- `localStorage.getItem('theme')` → `\"nord\"`\n- `document.documentElement.className` → `\"\"` (no `dark` class — as designed for\n  single-mode themes)\n- login card class → `... bg-c-bg-surface ...` (the fixed markup, not\n  `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`)\n- computed card `background-color` → `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252`\n- Nord stylesheet loaded → yes; `--color-white: #eceff4`, `--color-c-bg: #2e3440`\n\nA full theme sweep on production (see `screenshots/render-report.md`) shows the\nlogin card is dark under every single-mode dark theme and light only under the\nby-design light themes. The white-card symptom from `brief.md` is not\nreproducible on production today.\n\nThe other half of TASK-1 (the reporter's *local* instance) is not reachable from\nthis environment, but it is moot: production now matches the desired behaviour\nthat local already had.\n\n## Verification (TASK-4) limitation\n\n`node_modules` is not installed in this environment, so `npm run check`,\n`npm run lint`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, and `npm run preview` could not be\nrun. Per the project hard rule (\"NEVER install packages without asking\") no\npackages were installed. The remaining verification is a code/commit review, not\na rendered check. Recommended once dependencies and a backend are available:\npreview `/auth/login` and `/auth/register` under default light, default dark, and\neach single-mode theme (nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula,\nterminal, paper, atari) and confirm there are no white cards.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":102,"totalLines":102,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/notes.md","time":{"start":1791402595191,"end":1791402595374}},"id":"prt_117ea53510012JzIlIYoyVKQ0s","sessionID":"ses_ee815c9b3ffe1ffWjQDgOdBgXm","messageID":"msg_117ea4c2e001djqfVmQhfk72sf"}}
