{"type":"text","timestamp":1791402631109,"sessionID":"ses_ee815c9b3ffe1ffWjQDgOdBgXm","part":{"id":"prt_117ead89c0015jhKjoyDOla4X4","messageID":"msg_117eacf95001JNUMsSeBySOanE","sessionID":"ses_ee815c9b3ffe1ffWjQDgOdBgXm","type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nWorked the job in `/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login`. Branch `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches `brief.md` — verified before touching anything.\n\n**Outcome: no product change is warranted — the reported bug is already fixed upstream.**\n\nThe white login surface from `brief.md` was the auth **card**, not the page body: the six auth cards used literal `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, which `ThemeState.apply()` explicitly removes for every single-mode theme (`nord`, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). Under Nord the card therefore stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4` on an otherwise-Nord page. That was fixed by commit `70f6236`, which swept the auth cards to the themed `bg-c-bg-surface` token and `TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`.\n\nIndependent verification this session:\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true, and → true against `origin/main`.\n- `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` is empty — the branch contributes no product source.\n- All nine auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`; `grep 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none. Remaining `bg-white` hits elsewhere are unrelated decorative elements.\n- `auth/+layout.svelte` background uses the themed `bg-c-neutral`, so no literal white surface remains on the auth route.\n- `node_modules` is absent and installing packages is forbidden, so `check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` could not run; with no product diff there is nothing new to check.\n\nI appended a concise \"Seventh verification pass\" note to `implementation.md`, then committed all session artifacts. Worktree is clean (`git status` empty). TASK-1/2/3/4 are all satisfied or already satisfied upstream; the remaining action is a reviewer decision to close this as a duplicate of `70f6236`.\n\nNo human input was required.","time":{"start":1791402629276,"end":1791402631100}}}
