{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791402726612,"sessionID":"ses_ee81510f6ffe8VjspqJHaAXAwV","part":{"id":"prt_117ec54d100169aT0073MOHPCt","messageID":"msg_117ec50b40016WAbekBzOQSADl","sessionID":"ses_ee81510f6ffe8VjspqJHaAXAwV","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1791402730441,"sessionID":"ses_ee81510f6ffe8VjspqJHaAXAwV","part":{"id":"prt_117ec59930014tvdk5vJ4FXgfT","messageID":"msg_117ec50b40016WAbekBzOQSADl","sessionID":"ses_ee81510f6ffe8VjspqJHaAXAwV","type":"text","text":"Worktree is clean. Here's my summary.\n\n## Outcome: the job is a confirmed duplicate — no product change warranted\n\n**Branch check:** I'm on `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching the `branch:` field in `brief.md`. ✅\n\n### What the bug was\n\nThe white surface in `brief.md` is the **auth card**, not the page background and not a late/failed theme load. The old markup used the literal pair `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` carries the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`) explicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). Under Nord the themed fallback never applied, so the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4` on an otherwise-Nord page.\n\n### Why no change is needed\n\nThe fix is already **on `main`** (`origin/main` too) in commit **`70f6236`** (\"nord theme bug with todos\"), which reached this branch via the `main` merge. I verified independently:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `... origin/main` → true.\n- `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` → **empty** (the branch adds only this job's docs).\n- All nine auth-card blocks use `bg-c-bg-surface`; `TimePicker.svelte` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → **no matches**.\n\n### New hard evidence this pass\n\nI downloaded the `brief.md` screenshot and decoded the PNG pixels myself:\n- 973×989; ~90% `#353d4a` (Nord page `--color-c-neutral`) and ~5.9% near-white `#ebeef4` with bounding box x=374–693, y=339–618 — a **centred card**, not the page body.\n- So the reported symptom is the pre-fix white login card, **not** a FOUC/whole-page white flash.\n\n### Verification limits\n\n`node_modules` is absent and the project hard rule forbids installing packages without asking, so `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` could not run. With no product diff there is nothing new for them to check; rendered evidence remains the production theme sweep in `screenshots/render-report.md`.\n\nI appended this pass to `implementation.md` and committed it (`cb84cfd`). Per the hard rules I did **not** apply TASK-2's cosmetic `dark:text-white`/`border-white/5` swaps: they would alter default light/dark rendering (which TASK-2 requires to stay pixel-identical) without fixing any white surface, and the accepted upstream fix deliberately left them.\n\nThe stale `tasks.md` (rev 4, written before the `70f6236` merge) still describes the pre-fix classes; I left it as the analyst's artifact and documented the corrected picture in `implementation.md`.","time":{"start":1791402727827,"end":1791402730434}}}
