{"type":"text","timestamp":1791402797327,"sessionID":"ses_ee8138cadffeUjQ3UhBnx4VAiK","part":{"id":"prt_117ed610000137Zhe3JpDtioHA","messageID":"msg_117ed5a48001xIuAriik02gMQI","sessionID":"ses_ee8138cadffeUjQ3UhBnx4VAiK","type":"text","text":"Done. Here's a concise summary of the work.\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe job is a **confirmed duplicate of the already-merged fix `70f6236`** (\"nord theme bug with todos\", 2026-08-25). No product change is warranted.\n\n## What I found (independently re-verified)\n\n- **Branch matches**: `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`.\n- **No product diff**: `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` and `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- …` are both empty; `70f6236` is an ancestor of both `HEAD` and `origin/main`. The fix arrived via the `main` merge `8c0ad30`.\n- **Root cause (now moot)**: the six auth cards used `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2`. For single-mode themes (`supportsDarkMode: false`, e.g. Nord), `ThemeState.apply()` removes the `dark` class (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`), so the `dark:` fallback never fired, leaving the card at Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`.\n- **Already fixed in code**: all nine auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`; `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` returns nothing. `TimePicker.svelte` (TASK-3) already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\n- **Production checked directly**: `curl https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` (HTTP 200) returns server HTML whose login `<form>` already has `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` with **zero** `bg-white`. So Hypothesis B (stale prod assets) is disproven and the reported white card is not reproducible.\n- `node_modules` is absent and installing packages is forbidden by the project hard rule, so `npm run check/lint/test/build` could not be run; with no product diff there is nothing product-side to check.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Appended a \"Ninth verification pass\" section to `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md` with the above evidence.\n- Committed the auto-maintained `session.log`/`tokens.json` artifacts; worktree is clean.\n\nTASK-2's secondary substitutions (`dark:text-white`, `border-white/5`) were intentionally not applied — the auth layout already provides a themed label colour (`text-c-neutral-8`), and no target token was specified for the border; changing them would alter default light/dark rendering without fixing any white surface. The accepted upstream fix left them as-is.","time":{"start":1791402795264,"end":1791402797318}}}
