{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791402853349,"sessionID":"ses_ee811cfd0ffeNdNZtEb6sCTynU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_pKq6bdO1kUauwXHBsGOw0573","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: theme on login\n2: \n3: id: create\n4: status: open\n5: analyst: architect\n6: date: 2026-08-22 (rev 4 — local-vs-prod difference unresolved; two hypotheses,\n7: discriminating facts required from both environments before choosing)\n8: \n9: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n10: \n11: ## Findings (analysis)\n12: \n13: **Correction (rev 2):** the screenshot shows most of the Nord theme applied with a\n14: white surface on the login page. That rules out late/failed theme-CSS loading\n15: (FOUC would show the all-default light page, not a mostly-Nord one). The real\n16: mechanism:\n17: \n18: The app colors surfaces two ways:\n19: \n20: 1. **Semantic tokens** (`bg-c-neutral`, `text-c-btn`, `bg-c-bg-elevated`, …).\n21:    These compile to `--color-c-*` CSS variables, which every theme CSS overrides\n22:    in `:root`. Nord sets them all → these surfaces are correctly Nord.\n23: 2. **Literal Tailwind colors** (`bg-white`, `text-white`, `border-white/5`) plus a\n24:    `dark:` fallback (`dark:bg-s-dark-2`). `bg-white` compiles to\n25:    `var(--color-white)` — and Nord **deliberately keeps that near-white**\n26:    (`--color-white: #eceff4` \"Snow Storm\", see comment in\n27:    `static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`, chosen so `text-white` stays legible).\n28:    The `dark:bg-s-dark-2` escape hatch never fires for Nord, because single-mode\n29:    themes (`supportsDarkMode: false`) cause `ThemeState.apply()` to explicitly\n30:    `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n31:    (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`).\n32: \n33: So every auth page card (`routes/auth/*/…: class=\"… bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2\"`)\n34: renders as a near-white card on an otherwise-Nord page — a stable state, not a\n35: flash. Confirmed pattern in all six auth pages: login (110), register (92),\n36: forgot-password (72, 100), reset-password (72, 85, 105), logout (27),\n37: verify (44). Label text `dark:text-white` has the same problem (falls back to\n38: washed-out inherited `text-c-neutral-7` on the light card).\n39: \n40: **Local vs prod — unresolved, two hypotheses, do not assume.** The code\n41: mechanism above is verified from the repo; which variant applies depends on\n42: browser state the analyst cannot see. Discriminating facts to capture on BOTH\n43: localhost (looks correct) and prod (white card): `localStorage.getItem('theme')`,\n44: `document.documentElement.className`, computed card background, and whether prod\n45: runs the same frontend version as local.\n46: - Hypothesis A — different stored theme: local `theme=default` → `.dark`\n47:   present → `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fires → correct. Prod `theme=nord` → `.dark`\n48:   stripped → literal `bg-white`. Predicts: setting `theme=nord` on localhost\n49:   reproduces the white card.\n50: - Hypothesis B — version skew: local `theme=nord` and still correct → local and\n51:   prod deliver different CSS (older deploy on prod, or SW-cached old\n52:   `nord.css` that handled `--color-white` differently) → bug is stale assets,\n53:   not class logic. Predicts: localhost with `theme=nord` does NOT show the\n54:   white card.\n55: \n56: Previously suspected mechanisms, now demoted:\n57: - FOUC / theme applied too late — would show all-default light page, not\n58:   mostly-Nord. Optional hardening, not this bug.\n59: - Theme not synced to account — the user's Nord **did** apply (LocalStorage had\n60:   it), so not the cause. Follow-up, out of scope.\n61: - Service worker stale CSS — would break all Nord colors, not one surface. Dropped.\n62: \n63: ## Task breakdown\n64: \n65: TASK-1: Capture environment facts, then pick the hypothesis — on localhost\n66:     (where it looks correct) and on prod (where it doesn't), record:\n67:     `localStorage.getItem('theme')`, `document.documentElement.className`,\n68:     computed background-color of the login card, and the deployed frontend\n69:     version vs. this checkout. If Hypothesis A holds, additionally confirm the\n70:     one-line repro (`localStorage.setItem('theme','nord'); location.reload();`\n71:     on localhost /auth/login → white card). Record all of it in job notes.\n72:     No product code changes.\n73:     files: docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/* (notes only)\n74:     depends: none\n75:     risk: low — read-only analysis and local reproduction.\n76: \n77: TASK-2: Replace literal white utilities with semantic tokens on the auth pages —\n78:     swap `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` → `bg-c-bg-surface` (existing utility, used\n79:     in InputAutocomplete; maps to #ffffff light-default, s-dark-2 dark-default,\n80:     and #3b4252 under Nord — same as intended), `dark:text-white` →\n81:     `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`, `border-white/5` → token-based border,\n82:     across all six auth page cards.\n83:     files: src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte,\n84:     src/routes/auth/register/+page.svelte,\n85:     src/routes/auth/forgot-password/+page.svelte,\n86:     src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte,\n87:     src/routes/auth/logout/+page.svelte,\n88:     src/routes/auth/verify/[user_id]/[token]/+page.svelte\n89:     depends: TASK-1\n90:     risk: medium — visual change on high-traffic pages across all 10 themes;\n91:     must keep default light/dark rendering pixel-identical.\n92: \n93: TASK-3 (optional, needs owner go-ahead): Same literal-white pattern exists in\n94:     `TimePicker.svelte` (popup `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-3`) — same bug class,\n95:     visible in single-mode themes app-wide. Fix or file as follow-up.\n96:     files: src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte\n97:     depends: TASK-2\n98:     risk: low — one-line class swap, but outside the auth scope of this job.\n99: \n100: TASK-4: Verify — `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, then build +\n101:     preview and eyeball /auth/login (and register) under: default light, default\n102:     dark, and each single-mode theme (nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte,\n103:     gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). No white cards, no regressions\n104:     in default light/dark.\n105:     files: none (findings go into implementation.md)\n106:     depends: TASK-2 (and TASK-3 if undertaken)\n107:     risk: low — verification only.\n108: \n109: ## Open questions\n110: \n111: - TASK-3 in or out of scope?\n112: - Follow-ups tracked outside this job: pre-paint theme script (FOUC hardening),\n113:   `html` background-color rule, account-synced theme setting,\n114:   `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`.\n\n(End of file - total 114 lines)\n</content>\n\n<system-reminder>\nInstructions from: /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md\n# solyto frontend\n\n<!--\nThis is your project context, loaded by the agent at the start of every session.\nmanigot is vendor-agnostic: it runs Claude Code or OpenCode against the same\nproject (`mg --profile claude-pro` vs `mg --profile zai`/`--profile\nopencode-go`), and this one file serves both — manigot mounts it read-only\nwherever the selected tool looks for it\n(/workspace/AGENTS.md for OpenCode, /workspace/.claude/CLAUDE.md for Claude\nCode). Those mount paths are read-only: to change this context, edit this\nfile (docs/AGENTS.md), never the mount paths.\nThe same global agents are available under @name either way, and custom\nproject agents in docs/agents/ work under both tools — write them in the\nbuilt-in format (name:, description:, tools: Read, Grep, ...), no per-tool\nformat needed. To make a custom agent read-only under OpenCode, add a\n`permission:` frontmatter block (the built-in format manigot's conversion\npasses through to OpenCode's schema — see the manigot README's agent section);\nthe read-only built-in agents' blocks deny the destructive git commands\n(worktree management, branch -d/-D, reset, checkout, push, ...).\nCustom agents that must commit (like the built-in developer/reviewer/quality)\ndeclare `commit: true` in their frontmatter; agents that never commit declare\n`commit: false` and get a read-only git mount. The default — no agent named,\nfile missing, or marker absent/unknown — is a writable git mount, so a\ncommitting agent is never broken by a missing marker.\nAgent sessions also restrict git to reading history and making commits (the\nsession git shim): worktree management, branch deletes, resets, checkouts,\npushes, and the other destructive subcommands are refused.\nKeep this file tool-neutral — write it for \"the agent\", not for one vendor.\n-->\n\nThe client for [solyto.app](https://solyto.app): a free, private, all-in-one personal management app — todos, notes, calendar, contacts, media libraries, check-in, finances, feeds, time tracking, clipboard, and dev-requests in one place. This repo is the frontend only: a SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 single-page app that runs on the web, as an installable PWA, or as a native desktop/mobile shell. There is no backend or database here — every piece of data comes from the solyto REST API, which lives in a separate repository.\n\n## Stack\n- Backend: none in this repo — pure client-side SPA. Consumes the solyto REST API at `/api/v1` (`api.solyto.app` in prod, `http://localhost:8000` in dev; configurable per hostname in `src/lib/config/platform.ts`).\n- Frontend: SvelteKit 2, Svelte 5 (runes, `$state`), TypeScript (strict), Vite 7, Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`, adapter-node (outputs to `build/`).\n- Database: none — persistence is owned by the backend. The client only stores auth tokens, theme, and preferences in LocalStorage (`src/lib/services/LocalStorageService.ts`).\n- Key packages: `@tiptap/*` (notes rich-text editor), `echarts` (statistics charts), `@simplewebauthn/browser` (passkey login), `marked` + `dompurify` (markdown), `@lucide/svelte` (icons), `svelte-dnd-action` / `svelte-gestures` (drag & drop, swipe), `canvas-confetti`, `@fontsource/*`, `@vvo/tzdb`.\n\n## Architecture\n- `src/routes/` — SvelteKit file-based routes, all client-rendered (no `+page.server.ts`/`+server.ts` anywhere). The root `+layout.svelte` bootstraps every state store via `setContext`, guards unauthenticated access (redirect to `/auth/login` or `/setup`), and renders the navbar/footer shells. Feature routes: `/todos`, `/notes`, `/calendar`, `/contacts`, `/check-in`, `/finances`, `/feeds`, `/time-tracking`, `/clipboard`, `/dev-requests`, `/libraries/{books,movies,music,games,links,quotes,recipes,plants}`, plus `/settings`, `/admin`, `/profile`, `/auth/*`, `/setup`, `/share`.\n- `src/lib/state/` — one Svelte 5 runes class per domain (`Auth`, `Todos`, `Notes`, `Calendars`, `BookLibrary`, ...). Instances are created in `+layout.svelte` and shared through Svelte context (`setContext`/`getContext`); each store fetches via `ApiService` and holds the result in reactive `$state`.\n- `src/lib/services/` — `ApiService` (fetch wrapper over the REST API: Bearer auth, JSON, `%s`/`%d` URL placeholders, FormData uploads) and pure domain services (`TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`, `TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`, `LibraryFilterService`, `WealthStatisticsService`, ...) that are unit-tested.\n- `src/lib/config/` — `apiRoutes.ts` (all endpoints, composed from `getApiUrl()` + `/api/v1`), `platform.ts` (web vs. desktop vs. mobile via `PUBLIC_DESKTOP`/`PUBLIC_MOBILE`, API URL resolution), `themes.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `urls.ts`, `features.ts`.\n- `src/lib/components/` — feature components plus shared `ui/` (buttons, modals, navbar), `forms/` (inputs, pickers, toggles), and `charts/` (echarts wrappers). Several features keep separate desktop/mobile view variants (e.g. `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, `todos/views/`).\n- `src/lib/types/` — TypeScript interfaces mirroring the API data model, one file per domain (`todo.ts`, `note.ts`, `library_*.ts`, `calendar.ts`, ...).\n- `src/lib/i18n/` — translation tables `en.ts`, `de.ts`, `es.ts`, `fr.ts`, typed via `types/translation.ts`; every UI string must exist in all four.\n- `src/lib/helpers/` — pure utilities (DateHelper, NumberHelper, FormatHelper, ColorHelper, MusicTheory, ...).\n- `src/service-worker.ts` — PWA service worker (app-shell precache, stale-while-revalidate, push notifications); `static/site.webmanifest` is the PWA manifest, `static/themes/*` are runtime-loaded theme CSS.\n- `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\n- Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\n\n## Commands\n- `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\n- `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\n- `npm run preview` — preview the production build locally\n- `npm run check` — type-check with `svelte-check` (a11y warnings selectively ignored)\n- `npm run lint` — `prettier --check .` + `eslint .`\n- `npm run format` — auto-format with `prettier --write .`\n- `npm test` / `npm run test:watch` — run Vitest unit tests / watch mode\n- `make deploy` / `make audit` — Ansible deploy (external `deployment/` repo) / `npm audit` + `npm outdated`\n\n## Hard rules\n- NEVER modify files outside /workspace\n- NEVER install packages without asking (dependencies are pinned, `engine-strict=true`)\n- NEVER commit secrets: auth tokens, API keys, or `.env*` files (gitignored); never log or print token or user data\n- NEVER hand-edit generated output — `build/` and `.svelte-kit/` are regenerated by `npm run build` / `npm run check`\n- When adding or changing UI strings, keep all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it\n- When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess\n- Do not refactor things unrelated to the current task\n- Do not add abstractions not already present in the codebase\n\n</system-reminder>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: theme on login\n\nid: create\nstatus: open\nanalyst: architect\ndate: 2026-08-22 (rev 4 — local-vs-prod difference unresolved; two hypotheses,\ndiscriminating facts required from both environments before choosing)\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Findings (analysis)\n\n**Correction (rev 2):** the screenshot shows most of the Nord theme applied with a\nwhite surface on the login page. That rules out late/failed theme-CSS loading\n(FOUC would show the all-default light page, not a mostly-Nord one). The real\nmechanism:\n\nThe app colors surfaces two ways:\n\n1. **Semantic tokens** (`bg-c-neutral`, `text-c-btn`, `bg-c-bg-elevated`, …).","truncated":false,"loaded":["/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md"],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: theme on login\n\nid: create\nstatus: open\nanalyst: architect\ndate: 2026-08-22 (rev 4 — local-vs-prod difference unresolved; two hypotheses,\ndiscriminating facts required from both environments before choosing)\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Findings (analysis)\n\n**Correction (rev 2):** the screenshot shows most of the Nord theme applied with a\nwhite surface on the login page. That rules out late/failed theme-CSS loading\n(FOUC would show the all-default light page, not a mostly-Nord one). The real\nmechanism:\n\nThe app colors surfaces two ways:\n\n1. **Semantic tokens** (`bg-c-neutral`, `text-c-btn`, `bg-c-bg-elevated`, …).\n   These compile to `--color-c-*` CSS variables, which every theme CSS overrides\n   in `:root`. Nord sets them all → these surfaces are correctly Nord.\n2. **Literal Tailwind colors** (`bg-white`, `text-white`, `border-white/5`) plus a\n   `dark:` fallback (`dark:bg-s-dark-2`). `bg-white` compiles to\n   `var(--color-white)` — and Nord **deliberately keeps that near-white**\n   (`--color-white: #eceff4` \"Snow Storm\", see comment in\n   `static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`, chosen so `text-white` stays legible).\n   The `dark:bg-s-dark-2` escape hatch never fires for Nord, because single-mode\n   themes (`supportsDarkMode: false`) cause `ThemeState.apply()` to explicitly\n   `document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')`\n   (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`).\n\nSo every auth page card (`routes/auth/*/…: class=\"… bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2\"`)\nrenders as a near-white card on an otherwise-Nord page — a stable state, not a\nflash. Confirmed pattern in all six auth pages: login (110), register (92),\nforgot-password (72, 100), reset-password (72, 85, 105), logout (27),\nverify (44). Label text `dark:text-white` has the same problem (falls back to\nwashed-out inherited `text-c-neutral-7` on the light card).\n\n**Local vs prod — unresolved, two hypotheses, do not assume.** The code\nmechanism above is verified from the repo; which variant applies depends on\nbrowser state the analyst cannot see. Discriminating facts to capture on BOTH\nlocalhost (looks correct) and prod (white card): `localStorage.getItem('theme')`,\n`document.documentElement.className`, computed card background, and whether prod\nruns the same frontend version as local.\n- Hypothesis A — different stored theme: local `theme=default` → `.dark`\n  present → `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fires → correct. Prod `theme=nord` → `.dark`\n  stripped → literal `bg-white`. Predicts: setting `theme=nord` on localhost\n  reproduces the white card.\n- Hypothesis B — version skew: local `theme=nord` and still correct → local and\n  prod deliver different CSS (older deploy on prod, or SW-cached old\n  `nord.css` that handled `--color-white` differently) → bug is stale assets,\n  not class logic. Predicts: localhost with `theme=nord` does NOT show the\n  white card.\n\nPreviously suspected mechanisms, now demoted:\n- FOUC / theme applied too late — would show all-default light page, not\n  mostly-Nord. Optional hardening, not this bug.\n- Theme not synced to account — the user's Nord **did** apply (LocalStorage had\n  it), so not the cause. Follow-up, out of scope.\n- Service worker stale CSS — would break all Nord colors, not one surface. Dropped.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Capture environment facts, then pick the hypothesis — on localhost\n    (where it looks correct) and on prod (where it doesn't), record:\n    `localStorage.getItem('theme')`, `document.documentElement.className`,\n    computed background-color of the login card, and the deployed frontend\n    version vs. this checkout. If Hypothesis A holds, additionally confirm the\n    one-line repro (`localStorage.setItem('theme','nord'); location.reload();`\n    on localhost /auth/login → white card). Record all of it in job notes.\n    No product code changes.\n    files: docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/* (notes only)\n    depends: none\n    risk: low — read-only analysis and local reproduction.\n\nTASK-2: Replace literal white utilities with semantic tokens on the auth pages —\n    swap `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` → `bg-c-bg-surface` (existing utility, used\n    in InputAutocomplete; maps to #ffffff light-default, s-dark-2 dark-default,\n    and #3b4252 under Nord — same as intended), `dark:text-white` →\n    `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`, `border-white/5` → token-based border,\n    across all six auth page cards.\n    files: src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte,\n    src/routes/auth/register/+page.svelte,\n    src/routes/auth/forgot-password/+page.svelte,\n    src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte,\n    src/routes/auth/logout/+page.svelte,\n    src/routes/auth/verify/[user_id]/[token]/+page.svelte\n    depends: TASK-1\n    risk: medium — visual change on high-traffic pages across all 10 themes;\n    must keep default light/dark rendering pixel-identical.\n\nTASK-3 (optional, needs owner go-ahead): Same literal-white pattern exists in\n    `TimePicker.svelte` (popup `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-3`) — same bug class,\n    visible in single-mode themes app-wide. Fix or file as follow-up.\n    files: src/lib/components/forms/TimePicker.svelte\n    depends: TASK-2\n    risk: low — one-line class swap, but outside the auth scope of this job.\n\nTASK-4: Verify — `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, then build +\n    preview and eyeball /auth/login (and register) under: default light, default\n    dark, and each single-mode theme (nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte,\n    gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). No white cards, no regressions\n    in default light/dark.\n    files: none (findings go into implementation.md)\n    depends: TASK-2 (and TASK-3 if undertaken)\n    risk: low — verification only.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- TASK-3 in or out of scope?\n- Follow-ups tracked outside this job: pre-paint theme script (FOUC hardening),\n  `html` background-color rule, account-synced theme setting,\n  `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":114,"totalLines":114,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791402853176,"end":1791402853313}},"id":"prt_117ee431c001vtSpLxQmgfEgY9","sessionID":"ses_ee811cfd0ffeNdNZtEb6sCTynU","messageID":"msg_117ee35da001s2D1z3awTcSxOJ"}}
