{"type":"text","timestamp":1791402919302,"sessionID":"ses_ee811cfd0ffeNdNZtEb6sCTynU","part":{"id":"prt_117ef39be001uGnqXhbU62yhO7","messageID":"msg_117ef31d8001YYLdcNy418qepU","sessionID":"ses_ee811cfd0ffeNdNZtEb6sCTynU","type":"text","text":"Done. Here's the outcome.\n\n## Summary\n\nI verified the job **without trusting the prior sessions' notes**, and the conclusion holds: **this job is a duplicate of an upstream fix and needs no product change.**\n\n## What I found\n\n**The mechanism (from the code):** the six auth cards previously used literal `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` explicitly removes it for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false` — nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). So under Nord the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4` (`static/themes/nord/nord.css`) on an otherwise-Nord page — matching the white card in the brief's screenshot.\n\n**The fix already exists:** commit `70f6236` (\"nord theme bug with todos\", 2026-08-25) swept the auth cards to `bg-c-bg-surface` and `TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`. I confirmed independently:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true, and `… origin/main` → true\n- `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` and `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` → both empty (the branch adds only job docs)\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none; no `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark` pair anywhere under `src/`\n- **Live production check:** `curl https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` (HTTP 200) returns the login card as `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` with **0** occurrences of `bg-white`\n\nSo the reported white card is fixed and deployed; Hypothesis B (stale prod assets) is disproven, and Hypothesis A's mechanism is fixed in code.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **No product source change** — TASK-2 and TASK-3 are already satisfied upstream. The secondary TASK-2 substitutions were intentionally left alone: `text-c-neutral-9` would alter default-light rendering (violating the pixel-identical constraint) and no themed border token exists (`--color-c-border` is transparent/not overridden by Nord).\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md` — appended a concise \"Independent re-verification (session 11)\" section with this session's git-ancestry and production-fetch evidence.\n- Committed the harness's `session.log`/`tokens.json`; worktree is clean.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- **Close this job as a duplicate of `70f6236`.** Re-dispatching it will keep producing this disposition. `tasks.md` is stale (written at rev 4, before the `70f6236` merge) and still describes the pre-fix classes.\n- Inherited out-of-scope items remain: FOUC/pre-paint theme script, an `html`/`body` background rule, account-synced theme, and `y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`; plus `Progress.svelte:74` using `not-dark:bg-white` (same bug class, outside auth scope).\n- `node_modules` is absent, so `npm run check/lint/test/build` could not run — but with no product diff there is nothing new for them to check.","time":{"start":1791402916286,"end":1791402919291}}}
