{"type":"text","timestamp":1791403044256,"sessionID":"ses_ee810ab2affetaqz6CUQ7YEjao","part":{"id":"prt_117f124ad001BefHpH26MU4P21","messageID":"msg_117f11796001DdryadBz9Cexe6","sessionID":"ses_ee810ab2affetaqz6CUQ7YEjao","type":"text","text":"Done. The worktree is clean.\n\n## Summary\n\nI worked the job `/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login` (branch `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching the `branch:` in `brief.md`).\n\n**Outcome: no product change is warranted — the defect is already fixed upstream.**\n\nWhat I verified myself this session (not just trusting the prior notes):\n\n- **Branch check** — on `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`.\n- **TASK-1 (facts/root cause)** — the white surface is the auth **card**, caused by literal `bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark-2`; the `dark:` fallback never fires for single-mode themes because `ThemeState.apply()` strips the `dark` class (`static/themes/nord/nord.css` keeps `--color-white: #eceff4`). That mechanism is real but **already fixed**.\n- **TASK-2/TASK-3 (code)** — all nine auth-card blocks already use the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface`, and `TimePicker.svelte` already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`. `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → **no matches**. The fix commit `70f6236` is an ancestor of both `HEAD` and `main`; `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` is empty.\n- **Independent production probe** — fetched `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` (HTTP 200, server HTML contains `bg-c-bg-surface`, **0×** `bg-white`), then a fresh Playwright run seeding `localStorage.theme='nord'`: `html.class=\"\"`, card class `… bg-c-bg-surface …`, computed card bg `rgb(59,66,82)` = Nord `#3b4252`, text `#d8dee9`, `--color-white=#eceff4`. The white card from the brief is not reproducible.\n- **TASK-4** — `npm run check/lint/test/build` cannot run: `node_modules` is absent and the project hard rule forbids installing packages without asking. With no product diff there is nothing new for them to check. Rendered evidence lives in `screenshots/` + `render-report.md`.\n\n**TASK-2's secondary substitutions were intentionally not applied** (they would regress default light/dark, which the task requires to stay pixel-identical): `dark:text-white` labels already inherit a themed colour from `auth/+layout.svelte`, and `border-white/5` is a decorative outline with no safe token replacement.\n\nI committed the session artifacts and left the tree clean. The existing `implementation.md` already contains the full Summary/Changes/Known-issues write-up and is committed.\n\nNo human input was required to reach this conclusion.","time":{"start":1791403041965,"end":1791403044245}}}
