{"type":"text","timestamp":1791403122253,"sessionID":"ses_ee80ec14fffeW7X1cFTEN3rYf7","part":{"id":"prt_117f254e9001lrYbEtygAe1tVJ","messageID":"msg_117f249e6001u5oSKsJkWaOXzy","sessionID":"ses_ee80ec14fffeW7X1cFTEN3rYf7","type":"text","text":"Done. Worktree is clean.\n\n## Outcome\n\nThis job is a **duplicate of an existing upstream fix**. No product code change was warranted, so I made none.\n\n**What I verified independently (not just trusting the 11 prior passes):**\n\n- Branch is `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` **and** `… origin/main` → both true. `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` and `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` are both **empty** — this branch adds no product source change.\n- The bug in the brief (a near-white auth card on an otherwise-Nord page) was the `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` pattern: `ThemeState.apply()` strips the `dark` class for single-mode themes, so the `dark:` fallback never fires and `--color-white` stays near-white under Nord. Commit `70f6236` swept every auth card to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n- Current state: `grep bg-white src/routes/auth/` → none; all nine auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`. `TimePicker.svelte` already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`, so optional TASK-3 is resolved. No `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark` pair remains anywhere under `src/`.\n- Token mapping: `--color-c-bg-surface` = `#ffffff` (light), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark` (pixel-identical to the old classes), `#3b4252` under Nord — so default light/dark are unchanged and single-mode themes get a themed surface.\n\n**TASK-2's two secondary substitutions** (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`, `border-white/5` → token) were deliberately **not** applied: they don't fix any white surface and would change default-light rendering, which TASK-2 explicitly requires to stay pixel-identical.\n\n**Limitations:** `node_modules` is absent and package installation is forbidden, so `npm run check/lint/test/build` could not run (nothing new for them to check). A direct `curl` of `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` returned HTTP 200 with an empty body from this environment, so I could not re-measure production this pass; repo evidence plus the prior passes' production measurements stand.\n\nCommitted:\n- `4dce78d` — session-12 re-verification appended to `implementation.md`, no product change\n- a final `chore: sync session log` commit; `git status` is clean\n\n**Recommendation to the operator:** close this job as a duplicate of `70f6236`. Re-dispatching it will keep producing this same disposition — the task list is stale (written at rev 4, before that fix merged).","time":{"start":1791403119849,"end":1791403122244}}}
