{"type":"text","timestamp":1791403224302,"sessionID":"ses_ee80d9132ffeyj8uurXC1sNTLo","part":{"id":"prt_117f3e39000193z2rnqjYtY6No","messageID":"msg_117f3da71001fPQEIMQ3wH8Z34","sessionID":"ses_ee80d9132ffeyj8uurXC1sNTLo","type":"text","text":"All tasks are complete and the worktree is clean. Here's the outcome.\n\n## Summary\n\nI read `brief.md`, confirmed the branch is `feature/create_theme-on-login` (matches the brief), and re-verified the job independently rather than trusting the 12 prior sessions.\n\n**Finding: this job is a duplicate of an existing fix — no product code change is warranted.**\n\nThe white surface in the brief is the auth **card**, caused by the literal pair `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`) removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false`, e.g. Nord). So under Nord the `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback never applied and the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`.\n\nThat defect was already fixed by commit `70f6236` (\"nord theme bug with todos\", 2026-08-25), which swept all auth cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token and `TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`. It is present in this branch via the `main` merge.\n\nEvidence gathered this session:\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` and `… origin/main` → both true.\n- `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` → empty; the branch adds only job docs.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none; all nine auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`; no `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark` pair remains under `src/`.\n- Fresh production fetch: `curl https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` → HTTP 200, **0** `bg-white`, **1** `bg-c-bg-surface`, login `<form>` class exactly `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …`.\n\nTASK-1 (capture facts / pick hypothesis), TASK-2 (semantic tokens), TASK-3 (optional TimePicker) are all satisfied upstream; TASK-4's npm checks couldn't run because `node_modules` is absent and installing packages is forbidden by the project rules — with no product diff there is nothing for them to check. The pre-paint/FOUC hardening remains a tracked follow-up, explicitly out of scope in `tasks.md`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md` — appended a concise Session 13 re-verification recording the above.\n- Committed the job's harness files (`session.log`, `tokens.json`). No `src/`, `static/`, `tests/`, or `package.json` changes.\n\nRecommendation: close this job as a duplicate of `70f6236`. Re-dispatching it will keep producing this same disposition.","time":{"start":1791403221904,"end":1791403224293}}}
