uth-card blocks carry\n404:   `bg-c-bg-surface`. `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → none (the\n405:   remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative: `IconPlate`/`IconBar` dots and button\n406:   hover states, none in a `… dark:bg-s-dark` pair). `TimePicker.svelte` uses\n407:   `bg-c-bg-modal`, so TASK-3 is resolved.\n408: - Fresh production fetch this pass:\n409:   `curl https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` → HTTP 200, **0** occurrences of\n410:   `bg-white`, **1** of `bg-c-bg-surface`, and the login `<form>` class is exactly\n411:   `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …`. Production serves the fixed\n412:   markup; the `brief.md` white card is not reproducible.\n413: - `node_modules` is absent and installing packages is forbidden, so\n414:   `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` cannot be run; there is no product diff\n415:   for them to check.\n416: \n417: Conclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; this job duplicates `70f6236`.\n\n(End of file - total 417 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"## Summary\n\nThe white surface in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, not the page body and not a\nlate/failed theme load. The six auth cards used the literal pair\n`bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` carries\nthe `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\nexplicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode:\nfalse`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal,\npaper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback therefore never\napplied, so the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white\n`--color-white: #eceff4` (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`) on an otherwise-Nord\npage.\n\nThat defect is **already fixed and present in this branch**. Commit `70f6236`\n(\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\nswept the auth cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token and\n`TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`; it reached this branch through the `main`\nmerge `8c0ad30`. `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is\nempty, so this branch contributes no product source change. **This job is a\nduplicate of the earlier fix and needs no code change** — the correct outcome is","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","text":"## Summary\n\nThe white surface in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, not the page body and not a\nlate/failed theme load. The six auth cards used the literal pair\n`bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` carries\nthe `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\nexplicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode:\nfalse`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal,\npaper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback therefore never\napplied, so the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white\n`--color-white: #eceff4` (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`) on an otherwise-Nord\npage.\n\nThat defect is **already fixed and present in this branch**. Commit `70f6236`\n(\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\nswept the auth cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token and\n`TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`; it reached this branch through the `main`\nmerge `8c0ad30`. `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is\nempty, so this branch contributes no product source change. **This job is a\nduplicate of the earlier fix and needs no code change** — the correct outcome is\nto close it against `70f6236`.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: No product code. Environment facts were captured against the real\n  production app (`https://my.solyto.app`, the app host from\n  `src/lib/config/platform.ts`; bare `solyto.app` is the marketing landing page).\n  Re-confirmed independently this pass with Playwright (same engine `shot` uses,\n  chosen because `shot` cannot seed `localStorage`) after\n  `localStorage.setItem('theme','nord')`:\n\n  | fact | value |\n  | --- | --- |\n  | `localStorage.theme` | `\"nord\"` |\n  | `documentElement.className` | `\"\"` (no `dark` class — by design for single-mode themes) |\n  | login card class | `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` |\n  | computed card `background-color` | `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252` |\n  | computed card `color` | `rgb(216, 222, 233)` = Nord `#d8dee9` |\n  | `--color-white` / `--color-c-bg` / `--color-c-bg-surface` / `--color-c-neutral` | `#eceff4` / `#2e3440` / `#3b4252` / `#323a49` |\n  | Nord stylesheet link present | yes |\n\n  Hypothesis A (different stored theme) is the documented root-cause mechanism,\n  now fixed in code; Hypothesis B (stale/skewed production assets) is disproven —\n  production already serves the fixed markup (`bg-c-bg-surface`) and renders the\n  card as Nord `#3b4252`. Also independently decoded the `brief.md` screenshot\n  (pure-Python PNG decode): 973x989, ~90% `#303848` Nord page with a ~5.9%\n  near-white `#e8e8f0` region, confirming the white surface is the card and\n  matching the pre-fix markup.\n\nTASK-2: No change needed. All nine auth-card blocks already carry\n  `bg-c-bg-surface`: `login:110`, `register:92`,\n  `forgot-password:72,100`, `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`,\n  `verify/[user_id]/[token]:44`. `--color-c-bg-surface` resolves to `#ffffff` in\n  default light (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` in default\n  dark (`src/styles/default.css:19`, pixel-identical to the old\n  `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`), and `#3b4252` under Nord\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). The two secondary substitutions named\n  in the task were deliberately **not** applied:\n  - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: auth labels already\n    inherit a correctly themed colour from `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte`\n    (`text-c-neutral-8` = Nord `#d8dee9`, ≈7:1 on `#3b4252`). Adding an explicit\n    light-mode token would change default-light rendering (`c-neutral-8` →\n    `c-neutral-9`), which TASK-2 requires to stay pixel-identical.\n  - `border-white/5` → token border: no target token was specified, and\n    `--color-c-border` is transparent / not overridden by Nord, so a blind swap\n    would remove the decorative card outline. The accepted upstream fix left it\n    untouched.\n\nTASK-3: No change (optional item, and already resolved). `TimePicker.svelte`\n  already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`, fixed by the same `70f6236` sweep. No\n  `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark*` pair remains anywhere under `src/`.\n\nTASK-4: Verification. `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → no matches;\n  `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; all nine auth-card blocks\n  carry the semantic token. Rendered verification is recorded in\n  `screenshots/render-report.md` (full theme sweep, production): the login card\n  is dark under every single-mode dark theme and light only under the by-design\n  light themes (default-light, `catppuccin-latte`, `paper`). `npm run check`,\n  `lint`, `test`, and `build` could not be run because `node_modules` is not\n  installed and the project hard rule forbids installing packages without asking;\n  with no product diff there is nothing new for them to check.\n\n## Second verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nRe-ran the decisive checks independently rather than trusting the earlier notes:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 origin/main` → true, and\n  `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is empty, so the\n  auth-card fix is upstream on `origin/main` and this branch contributes no product\n  source change. `git show 70f6236 -- src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte` confirms it\n  is the commit that changed the login card from\n  `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → no matches. All nine auth-card blocks\n  (`login:110`, `register:92`, `forgot-password:72,100`,\n  `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`, `verify/…:44`) carry `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n- Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface` is `#ffffff` in\n  `src/styles/tokens.css:24`, becomes `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n  (`src/styles/default.css:19`), and is `#3b4252` under Nord\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). So default light/dark stay pixel-identical\n  to the old `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`, while single-mode themes get a themed card.\n\nConclusion unchanged: no product change is warranted; this job duplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Third verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nRe-verified the conclusion without relying on the earlier notes:\n\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD --stat\n  -- src static tests package.json` is empty, so the fix is upstream and this\n  branch adds no product source change.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → no matches. All nine\n  auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92,\n  forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44).\n- Live production probe (`https://my.solyto.app/auth/login`, Playwright/Chromium,\n  seeding `localStorage.theme = 'nord'` then reloading) independently reproduces\n  the fixed behaviour:\n\n  | fact | value |\n  | --- | --- |\n  | `localStorage.theme` | `\"nord\"` |\n  | `documentElement.className` | `\"\"` (no `dark` class) |\n  | login card class | `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` |\n  | computed card `background-color` | `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252` |\n  | computed card `color` | `rgb(216, 222, 233)` = Nord `#d8dee9` |\n  | `--color-white` / `--color-c-bg` / `--color-c-bg-surface` | `#eceff4` / `#2e3440` / `#3b4252` |\n  | Nord stylesheet present | yes |\n\nThe white login card from `brief.md` is not reproducible against current\nproduction under Nord. Conclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; the job\nduplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Fourth verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nIndependent re-check, favouring repo-state facts over the earlier notes:\n\n- Branch is `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching `brief.md`; no product\n  source diff: `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` is empty.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git show --stat 70f6236`\n  confirms it swept the auth cards and `TimePicker.svelte`.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → no matches. All nine auth-card\n  blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92,\n  forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44).\n- Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff`\n  (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n  (`src/styles/default.css:19`), and `#3b4252` under Nord\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). Nord is `supportsDarkMode: false`\n  (`src/lib/config/themes.ts:22-24`), which is why the old `dark:bg-s-dark-2`\n  fallback never fired — the documented root cause, now moot.\n- `node_modules` is still absent and the project hard rule forbids installing\n  packages, so `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` could not be run; there is\n  no product diff for them to check. The production render sweep in\n  `screenshots/render-report.md` remains the rendered evidence.\n\nConclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; the job duplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Fifth verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nRe-derived the conclusion from repo state and an independent production probe,\nwithout relying on the earlier notes:\n\n- `git branch --show-current` → `feature/create_theme-on-login`, matching the\n  `branch:` field in `brief.md`; verified before touching anything.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD --\n  src static tests package.json` is empty, so this branch adds no product source\n  change. `git diff --stat main...HEAD` lists only this job's docs.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → no matches; all nine auth-card blocks\n  carry `bg-c-bg-surface`. `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` →\n  no matches.\n- Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff`\n  (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n  (`src/styles/default.css:19`), `#3b4252` under Nord\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`) — pixel-identical to the old\n  `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2` in default light/dark, themed for single-mode.\n- Independent production probe (new this pass): the deployed\n  `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` server HTML already contains\n  `bg-c-bg-surface` and no `bg-white`. With `localStorage.theme='nord'` seeded\n  before boot, a Chromium (Playwright) probe measured: `html.class=\"\"`,\n  card class `… bg-c-bg-surface …`, computed card `background-color`\n  `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252`, `--color-white` `#eceff4`, Nord stylesheet\n  present. The white card is not reproducible on current production — Hypothesis\n  B (stale/skewed prod assets) is disproven; Hypothesis A's mechanism is fixed.\n- `node_modules` is absent and the project hard rule forbids installing\n  packages, so `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` could not be run; there is\n  no product diff for them to check.\n\nConclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; the job duplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Sixth verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nRe-derived the outcome from repo state plus an independent production fetch:\n\n- Branch `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches `brief.md`. `git merge-base\n  --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true, and `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests\n  package.json` is empty: this branch contributes no product source change.\n- `git show 70f6236 -- src/routes/auth/` confirms that commit changed all six auth\n  cards from `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` to `bg-c-bg-surface`.\n- All nine auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`\n  (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105,\n  logout:27, verify:44); `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → none.\n  `TimePicker.svelte` already uses `bg-c-bg-modal` (TASK-3 pre-resolved).\n- New evidence this pass: a plain HTTP fetch of the deployed\n  `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` returns server HTML whose login `<form>`\n  already carries `… border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` and contains **zero**\n  `bg-white`. Production therefore serves the fixed markup; the white-card\n  symptom is not reproducible and requires no deploy of this branch.\n- `node_modules` remains absent and installing packages is forbidden, so\n  `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` were not run; with no product diff there is\n  nothing new for them to check.\n\nTASK-2's secondary substitutions (`dark:text-white`, `border-white/5`) remain\nintentionally unapplied, matching the accepted upstream fix: the auth labels\nalready inherit a themed colour from `auth/+layout.svelte` (`text-c-neutral-8`),\nand `--color-c-border` is transparent/not overridden by Nord, so swapping would\nchange default light/dark rendering without fixing any white surface.\n\nConclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; this job duplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Seventh verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nIndependent re-check from repo/remote state, not the earlier notes:\n\n- Branch `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches the `branch:` field in\n  `brief.md`; checked before touching anything.\n- `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` is empty, and\n  `git diff --stat main...HEAD` lists only this job's own docs. The branch adds no\n  product source change.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true **and**\n  `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 origin/main` → true, so the fix is on\n  `origin/main`, not only in this worktree.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → no matches; all nine auth-card blocks\n  carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (`login:110`, `register:92`, `forgot-password:72,100`,\n  `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`, `verify/…:44`). The remaining\n  `bg-white` hits under `src/` are unrelated decorative dots/toggle knobs (plus\n  the already-known `Progress.svelte:74` `not-dark:bg-white` follow-up).\n- The `auth/+layout.svelte` page background uses the themed `bg-c-neutral`, and\n  the login card `bg-c-bg-surface`, so no literal white surface remains on the\n  auth route.\n- `node_modules` is still absent and the project hard rule forbids installing\n  packages, so `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` cannot be run; with no\n  product diff there is nothing new for them to check.\n\nConclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; the job duplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Eighth verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nIndependently re-derived, and added one piece of hard evidence the earlier\npasses had only asserted — a direct pixel decode of the `brief.md` screenshot\n(`https://iili.io/CZZtpwX.png`, downloaded with `curl`):\n\n- PNG is 973x989. Dominant colour `#353d4a` (≈89.9%) matches Nord\n  `--color-c-neutral` (the page), `#454d5e`/`#4d576a` (≈2.9%) match Nord\n  `--color-c-bg-elevated`/`--color-c-btn` (inputs/button).\n- The only large near-white region is `#ebeef4` (≈5.9%) with bounding box\n  x=374..693, y=339..618 (319x279) — a centred card, not the page body. This is\n  the pre-fix login card: white surface with themed dark inputs, exactly the\n  `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` failure mode. It is **not** a FOUC/whole-page\n  flash (the page is Nord, not default-light).\n- Repo state: `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true and\n  `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 origin/main` → true;\n  `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` is empty. All\n  nine auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`; `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ |\n  grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → no matches; `TimePicker.svelte` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\n- Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff`\n  (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n  (`src/styles/default.css:19`), `#3b4252` under Nord\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`) — default light/dark pixel-identical to\n  the old classes, themed for single-mode themes.\n\n`node_modules` is still absent and installing packages is forbidden, so\n`npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` cannot be run; there is no product diff for\nthem to check. Conclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; this job\nduplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Ninth verification pass (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nIndependently re-derived from repo, remote, and a direct production fetch:\n\n- Branch `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches the `branch:` field in\n  `brief.md`; checked before touching anything.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true and\n  `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 origin/main` → true;\n  `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` and\n  `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` are both empty.\n  The fix is upstream on `origin/main` and this branch adds no product source change.\n- `git show 70f6236 -- src/routes/auth/login/+page.svelte` confirms it changed\n  `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` → `bg-c-bg-surface` (the same sweep touched\n  `TimePicker.svelte` and the other auth cards).\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → no matches; `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ |\n  grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → no matches. All nine auth-card blocks carry\n  `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72,100,\n  reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify/…:44). The only remaining\n  `bg-white` under `src/lib/components/forms/` is Toggle's decorative knob, not\n  the `… dark:bg-s-dark` pair.\n- New evidence this pass: a direct HTTP fetch of the deployed app\n  (`curl https://my.solyto.app/auth/login`, HTTP 200) returns server HTML whose\n  login `<form>` already carries `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …`\n  with **zero** occurrences of `bg-white`. Production serves the fixed markup, so\n  the `brief.md` white-card symptom is not reproducible and needs no deploy of\n  this branch.\n- Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff`\n  (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n  (`src/styles/default.css:19`), `#3b4252` under Nord\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34`, `supportsDarkMode: false`).\n- `node_modules` is absent and the project hard rule forbids installing packages,\n  so `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` cannot be run; with no product diff\n  there is nothing product-side for them to check.\n\nConclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; the job duplicates `70f6236`.\n\n## Final disposition (tenth developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nRe-verified from repo/remote state before touching anything; result unchanged:\n\n- Branch `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches the `branch:` field in\n  `brief.md`.\n- `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` and\n  `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` are both empty: the\n  branch adds only this job's docs.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true and\n  `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 origin/main` → true.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → no matches; the nine auth-card blocks\n  carry `bg-c-bg-surface`. `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` →\n  no matches. Remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative (icon dots, toggle knob,\n  score bar) plus the already-known `Progress.svelte:74` follow-up.\n\nNo product code was changed this pass or by any earlier pass. **This job should\nbe closed as a duplicate of `70f6236`;** re-dispatching it will keep producing\nthis same disposition.\n\n## Independent re-verification (developer session 11, 2026-10-07)\n\nFresh check, favouring live production and git ancestry over the prior notes:\n\n- Branch `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches `brief.md`.\n  `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` and\n  `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` are both empty;\n  `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` and `… origin/main` are both true.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none; `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ |\n  grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → none. `login:110` / `register:92` carry\n  `border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface`.\n- Direct production fetch (`curl https://my.solyto.app/auth/login`, HTTP 200)\n  returns the login card as\n  `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` with **0** occurrences of\n  `bg-white`. The reported white card is fixed in the deployed app.\n\nConclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; close as a duplicate of\n`70f6236`.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- This job is a duplicate: the defect was already fixed by `70f6236` before this\n  branch's `main` merge. Product behaviour needs no change; close against the\n  existing fix.\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale — it was written at rev 4\n  before the `70f6236` merge and still describes the pre-fix auth-card classes.\n  Left as the analyst's artifact; the corrected picture is in `notes.md` and here.\n- Inherited open items (out of scope): pre-paint theme script / FOUC hardening\n  (`theme.load()` runs in `onMount`, so there is still a brief light-default flash\n  before a single-mode theme applies), an `html`/`body` background-color rule, an\n  account-synced theme setting, and `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` existing on disk\n  but missing from `src/lib/config/themes.ts`.\n- Same bug class, outside this job's auth scope: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Progress.svelte:74`\n  still uses `not-dark:bg-white`, which renders white under single-mode dark\n  themes (`.dark` absent) — candidate for a follow-up identical to TASK-3.\n- Cosmetic consistency (not applied): auth labels use bare `dark:text-white`\n  while most of the app uses `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`.\n\n## Session 12 re-verification (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nIndependently re-derived before touching anything; outcome unchanged:\n\n- Branch `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches the `branch:` field in\n  `brief.md`.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` and `… origin/main` are both true;\n  `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` and\n  `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` are both empty.\n  This branch adds no product source change.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none; all nine auth-card blocks carry\n  `bg-c-bg-surface`. `TimePicker.svelte` already uses `bg-c-bg-modal` (line 63),\n  so TASK-3 is resolved. No `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark` pair remains under `src/`.\n- Token mapping re-confirmed: `--color-c-bg-surface: #ffffff`\n  (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark`\n  (`src/styles/default.css:19`), `#3b4252` under Nord\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34`) with `supportsDarkMode: false`.\n- `node_modules` is absent and installing packages is forbidden, so\n  `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` cannot be run. A direct `curl` of\n  `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` returned HTTP 200 with an empty body from\n  this environment, so production could not be re-measured this pass; the prior\n  passes' production measurements plus this repo evidence stand.\n\nConclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; close as a duplicate of\n`70f6236`.\n\n## Session 13 re-verification (fresh developer session, 2026-10-07)\n\nIndependently re-derived before touching anything; outcome unchanged:\n\n- Branch `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches the `branch:` field in\n  `brief.md`.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` and `… origin/main` are both true;\n  `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` is empty. This branch\n  adds no product source change.\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none; all nine auth-card blocks carry\n  `bg-c-bg-surface`. `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → none (the\n  remaining `bg-white` hits are decorative: `IconPlate`/`IconBar` dots and button\n  hover states, none in a `… dark:bg-s-dark` pair). `TimePicker.svelte` uses\n  `bg-c-bg-modal`, so TASK-3 is resolved.\n- Fresh production fetch this pass:\n  `curl https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` → HTTP 200, **0** occurrences of\n  `bg-white`, **1** of `bg-c-bg-surface`, and the login `<form>` class is exactly\n  `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …`. Production serves the fixed\n  markup; the `brief.md` white card is not reproducible.\n- `node_modules` is absent and installing packages is forbidden, so\n  `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` cannot be run; there is no product diff\n  for them to check.\n\nConclusion unchanged: no product change warranted; this job duplicates `70f6236`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":417,"totalLines":417,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791403236726,"end":1791403236784}},"id":"prt_117f41d1f0017FDviM7SCV3Foh","sessionID":"ses_ee80c05d7ffeQtKgWe3a1KvmLS","messageID":"msg_117f41561001pha0GLeahSH3ph"}}
