{"type":"text","timestamp":1791403287675,"sessionID":"ses_ee80c05d7ffeQtKgWe3a1KvmLS","part":{"id":"prt_117f4da5f001OUJpZNE5mnKlQw","messageID":"msg_117f4cd2b001brgkFUFyfhkPKO","sessionID":"ses_ee80c05d7ffeQtKgWe3a1KvmLS","type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nVerified and finalized the `create_theme-on-login` job. **No product change is warranted** — the reported white login card is a duplicate of an already-shipped fix.\n\n### What the issue was\nThe six auth cards used the literal pair `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, but `ThemeState.apply()` removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false` — nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). Under Nord the fallback therefore never applied, leaving the card at Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4` on an otherwise-Nord page — a stable state, not a FOUC.\n\n### Disposition\nThis was fixed by commit `70f6236` (\"nord theme bug with todos\"), which swept all auth cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token and `TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`; it reached this branch through the `main` merge.\n\nIndependent checks this session:\n- Branch `feature/create_theme-on-login` matches `brief.md`.\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true; `git diff main...HEAD --stat -- src static tests package.json` empty.\n- All nine auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`; `bg-white` + `dark:bg-s-dark` pair fully gone from `src/`; `TimePicker.svelte:63` uses `bg-c-bg-modal`.\n- Token mapping: `--color-c-bg-surface` = `#ffffff` light, `var(--color-s-dark-2)` dark, `#3b4252` Nord — pixel-identical to the old classes in default light/dark.\n- Live production `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` → HTTP 200, **0** `bg-white`, **1** `bg-c-bg-surface`; card class exactly `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …`. The white card is not reproducible on current production.\n\n### Changes (docs only; no product code)\n- Appended a \"Session 14 re-verification\" note to `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md`.\n- Committed session artifacts. Worktree is clean; branch `feature/create_theme-on-login`.\n\n### Known issues / follow-ups\n- `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` could not run: `node_modules` is absent and the project hard rule forbids installing packages without asking. With no product diff there is nothing new for them to check.\n- Unchanged follow-ups from earlier passes: pre-paint/FOUC hardening, account-synced theme, `y2k.css` missing from `themes.ts`, and `Progress.svelte:74` `not-dark:bg-white`.\n- **Process note:** this job has now been re-dispatched 14 times and each session reaches the same conclusion. It is a duplicate of `70f6236` and should be closed; re-dispatching will keep producing this same no-change disposition.","time":{"start":1791403285087,"end":1791403287671}}}
