{"type":"text","timestamp":1791403378165,"sessionID":"ses_ee80b0aaeffeENAG6arx60QMRy","part":{"id":"prt_117f63d350017dvV3mPwWR7cW9","messageID":"msg_117f634230016AAhbwXh3hdkST","sessionID":"ses_ee80b0aaeffeENAG6arx60QMRy","type":"text","text":"I've completed the job. Here's the summary:\n\n## Outcome\n\nI independently re-verified the job and found that **no product code change is warranted** — the defect described in `brief.md` was already fixed upstream.\n\n**Root cause:** The auth cards used `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` fallback only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, but `ThemeState.apply()` explicitly removes that class for single-mode themes (`supportsDarkMode: false`, incl. Nord). So under Nord the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`, producing a stable white card on an otherwise-Nord login page — not a FOUC.\n\n**Already fixed by commit `70f6236`** (\"nord theme bug with todos\", 2026-08-25), which swept all auth cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token (and `TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`). It reached this branch via the `main` merge. Verified:\n- `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is empty\n- `70f6236` is an ancestor of both `HEAD` and `origin/main`\n- All nine auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`; no `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark` pair remains under `src/`\n- Live production (`https://my.solyto.app/auth/login`) serves `bg-c-bg-surface`, renders the card as Nord `#3b4252`, with 0 occurrences of `bg-white`\n\nI deliberately did **not** apply TASK-2's secondary substitutions (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`, `border-white/5` → token border): they would alter default light/dark rendering (which the task requires stay pixel-identical) and remove the decorative border, without fixing any white surface. TASK-3 was resolved by the same upstream sweep.\n\n**Verification limitation:** `node_modules` is absent and installing packages is forbidden, so `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build` could not be run; with no product diff there is nothing new for them to check. Rendered evidence is in `screenshots/render-report.md` (production theme sweep).\n\nI consolidated the redundant 14-pass implementation log into a single clean `implementation.md` and committed it as `09b02a0`, then committed the harness session artifacts. The job should be **closed as a duplicate of `70f6236`**.","time":{"start":1791403375925,"end":1791403378153}}}
