{"type":"text","timestamp":1791403846318,"sessionID":"ses_ee807ed1bffe4UkwEg8B3sEwmb","part":{"id":"prt_117fd44d3001FiPMSvDVwA2ode","messageID":"msg_117fd27b1001532tgiAi5gEIpP","sessionID":"ses_ee807ed1bffe4UkwEg8B3sEwmb","type":"text","text":"Worktree is clean, both commits landed, branch untouched otherwise. Here's the summary of this session.\n\n## Result\n\nThis job (`create_theme-on-login` on branch `feature/create_theme-on-login`) is a **duplicate of an already-merged fix — no product code change is needed**. I independently re-verified this rather than trusting the prior notes.\n\n### Root cause (the brief's question)\nThe white surface in the screenshot was the **login card**, not a late/failed theme load. The six auth cards used the literal pair `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`) explicitly strips that class for single-mode themes (`supportsDarkMode: false` — nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). So under Nord the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4` (comment in `static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`) — a stable white card on an otherwise-Nord page.\n\n### Why no change was needed\nCommit `70f6236` (\"nord theme bug with todos\", 2026-08-25) already swept all six auth cards to the semantic token `bg-c-bg-surface` and `TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`, and it reached this branch via the `main` merge. Verified independently this session:\n\n- `70f6236` is an ancestor of both `HEAD` and `origin/main`; `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is empty.\n- All six auth cards carry `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72+100, reset-password:72+85+105, logout:27, verify:44); **0** `bg-white` in `src/routes/auth/`; **0** `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark*` pairs left in `src/`.\n- `--color-c-bg-surface` maps to `#ffffff` light / `var(--color-s-dark-2)` dark / `#3b4252` Nord — pixel-identical to the old pair in default themes.\n- Live prod (`https://my.solyto.app/auth/login`) serves HTTP 200 with `bg-c-bg-surface` and **0** `bg-white`; `/themes/nord/nord.css` serves the correct token overrides. The white card is not reproducible.\n- TASK-2's secondary substitutions (`dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 …`, `border-white/5` → token) were deliberately **not** applied: labels already inherit a correctly themed colour (≈7:1 contrast under Nord), the border has no specified replacement token (`--color-c-border` is transparent under Nord), and both swaps would change default light rendering, which TASK-2 requires to stay pixel-identical.\n- TASK-4 runtime checks (`npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build`) can't run — `node_modules` is absent and installing is forbidden without asking (unattended session).\n\n### Commits\n- `0331a9d` — implementation.md: final re-verification note (prod re-checked live; conclusion unchanged)\n- `04dfb1f` — chore: sync session artifacts (session.log, tokens.json)\n\nWorktree is clean; no pushes, merges, or other branches touched. `verdict.md` remains for the reviewer to fill.","time":{"start":1791403836628,"end":1791403846312}}}
