{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791403858390,"sessionID":"ses_ee80287fdffeBZlXIz12YKGjBW","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_VZTEDEHhbw7P3jmYGf2f2085","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git status && echo \"=== LOG ===\" && git log --oneline -15"},"output":"On branch feature/create_theme-on-login\nChanges not staged for commit:\n  (use \"git add <file>...\" to update what will be committed)\n  (use \"git restore <file>...\" to discard changes in working directory)\n\tmodified:   docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log\n\tmodified:   docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tokens.json\n\nno changes added to commit (use \"git add\" and/or \"git commit -a\")\n=== LOG ===\nb9f918c [create] chore: commit all\n04dfb1f [create] chore: sync session artifacts\n0331a9d [create] implementation: final re-verification, no product change (duplicate of 70f6236)\n4ce49c6 [create] chore: commit all\nb2f9dde [create] chore: sync session artifacts (independent re-verification, duplicate of 70f6236)\n79d367f [create] chore: commit all\ncb11c52 [create] chore: sync session log\n09b02a0 [create] implementation: add summary\n27335a8 [create] chore: commit all\nb08a3e0 [create] chore: sync session artifacts\n0b1041e [create] implementation: session 14 re-verification, no product change (duplicate of 70f6236)\n5169e89 [create] chore: commit all\n4d9cb68 [create] implementation: session 13 re-verification, no product change (duplicate of 70f6236)\na259b99 [create] chore: commit all\n67bfeb4 [create] chore: sync session log\n","metadata":{"output":"On branch feature/create_theme-on-login\nChanges not staged for commit:\n  (use \"git add <file>...\" to update what will be committed)\n  (use \"git restore <file>...\" to discard changes in working directory)\n\tmodified:   docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log\n\tmodified:   docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tokens.json\n\nno changes added to commit (use \"git add\" and/or \"git commit -a\")\n=== LOG ===\nb9f918c [create] chore: commit all\n04dfb1f [create] chore: sync session artifacts\n0331a9d [create] implementation: final re-verification, no product change (duplicate of 70f6236)\n4ce49c6 [create] chore: commit all\nb2f9dde [create] chore: sync session artifacts (independent re-verification, duplicate of 70f6236)\n79d367f [create] chore: commit all\ncb11c52 [create] chore: sync session log\n09b02a0 [create] implementation: add summary\n27335a8 [create] chore: commit all\nb08a3e0 [create] chore: sync session artifacts\n0b1041e [create] implementation: session 14 re-verification, no product change (duplicate of 70f6236)\n5169e89 [create] chore: commit all\n4d9cb68 [create] implementation: session 13 re-verification, no product change (duplicate of 70f6236)\na259b99 [create] chore: commit all\n67bfeb4 [create] chore: sync session log\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git status && echo \"=== LOG ===\" && git log --oneline -15","time":{"start":1791403858070,"end":1791403858224}},"id":"prt_117fd9861001NKYT04jCtdqRib","sessionID":"ses_ee80287fdffeBZlXIz12YKGjBW","messageID":"msg_117fd9151001d6ax01nb2QupfJ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791403858432,"sessionID":"ses_ee80287fdffeBZlXIz12YKGjBW","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_1UWuToQllKgpPtZVTB4M5193","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ## Summary\n2: \n3: The white surface reported in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, not the page body\n4: and not a late/failed theme load. The six auth cards used the literal pair\n5: `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` carries\n6: the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\n7: explicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode:\n8: false`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal,\n9: paper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback therefore never\n10: applied, so the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white\n11: `--color-white: #eceff4` (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`) on an otherwise-Nord\n12: page — a stable state, not a flash.\n13: \n14: That defect is **already fixed and present in this branch**. Commit `70f6236`\n15: (\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\n16: swept the auth cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token and\n17: `TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`; it reached this branch through the `main`\n18: merge `8c0ad30`. `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is\n19: empty, so this branch contributes no product source change. **This job is a\n20: duplicate of the earlier fix and needs no code change** — the correct outcome is\n21: to close it against `70f6236`.\n22: \n23: ## Changes\n24: \n25: TASK-1: No product code. Environment facts were captured against the real\n26:   production app (`https://my.solyto.app`, the app host from\n27:   `src/lib/config/platform.ts`; bare `solyto.app` is the marketing landing page).\n28:   After seeding `localStorage.setItem('theme','nord')` and booting the page:\n29: \n30:   | fact | value |\n31:   | --- | --- |\n32:   | `localStorage.theme` | `\"nord\"` |\n33:   | `documentElement.className` | `\"\"` (no `dark` class — by design for single-mode themes) |\n34:   | login card class | `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` |\n35:   | computed card `background-color` | `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252` |\n36:   | computed card `color` | `rgb(216, 222, 233)` = Nord `#d8dee9` |\n37:   | `--color-white` / `--color-c-bg` / `--color-c-bg-surface` | `#eceff4` / `#2e3440` / `#3b4252` |\n38:   | Nord stylesheet present | yes |\n39: \n40:   Hypothesis A (different stored theme) is the documented root-cause mechanism,\n41:   now fixed in code; Hypothesis B (stale/skewed production assets) is disproven —\n42:   production already serves the fixed markup (`bg-c-bg-surface`) and renders the\n43:   card as Nord `#3b4252`. The `brief.md` screenshot decodes to a 973x989 Nord page\n44:   with one near-white centred region (≈5.9%), i.e. the pre-fix card, matching the\n45:   `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` failure mode rather than a FOUC (the surrounding\n46:   page is Nord, not default-light).\n47: \n48: TASK-2: No change needed. All nine auth-card blocks already carry\n49:   `bg-c-bg-surface`: `login:110`, `register:92`,\n50:   `forgot-password:72,100`, `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`,\n51:   `verify/[user_id]/[token]:44`. `--color-c-bg-surface` resolves to `#ffffff` in\n52:   default light (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` in default\n53:   dark (`src/styles/default.css:19`, pixel-identical to the old\n54:   `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`), and `#3b4252` under Nord\n55:   (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). The two secondary substitutions named\n56:   in the task were deliberately **not** applied:\n57:   - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: auth labels already\n58:     inherit a correctly themed colour from `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte`\n59:     (`text-c-neutral-8` = Nord `#d8dee9`, ≈7:1 on `#3b4252`). Adding an explicit\n60:     light-mode token would change default-light rendering (`c-neutral-8` →\n61:     `c-neutral-9`), which TASK-2 requires to stay pixel-identical.\n62:   - `border-white/5` → token border: no target token was specified, and\n63:     `--color-c-border` is transparent / not overridden by Nord, so a blind swap\n64:     would remove the decorative card outline. The accepted upstream fix left it\n65:     untouched.\n66: \n67: TASK-3: No change (optional item, and already resolved). `TimePicker.svelte`\n68:   already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`, fixed by the same `70f6236` sweep. No\n69:   `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark*` pair remains anywhere under `src/`.\n70: \n71: TASK-4: Verification.\n72:   - Repo: `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true **and**\n73:     `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 origin/main` → true;\n74:     `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` is empty. All nine\n75:     auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`; `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/`\n76:     → none; `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → none. The\n77:     remaining `bg-white` hits under `src/` are decorative (icon dots, toggle knob,\n78:     score bar) plus the known `Progress.svelte:74` follow-up.\n79:   - Production: `curl https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` → HTTP 200, **0**\n80:     occurrences of `bg-white`, **1** of `bg-c-bg-surface`; the login card class is\n81:     exactly `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface px-8 pt-6 pb-8 shadow-sm\n82:     md:min-w-80`. The white card from `brief.md` is not reproducible.\n83:   - Rendered sweep (production, recorded in `screenshots/render-report.md`): the\n84:     login card is dark under every single-mode dark theme and light only under the\n85:     by-design light themes (default-light, `catppuccin-latte`, `paper`).\n86:   - Limitation: `node_modules` is not installed, and the project hard rule forbids\n87:     installing packages without asking, so `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build`\n88:     could not be run. With no product diff there is nothing new for them to check.\n89:   - Final independent re-verification (2026-10-07, same day as the prod capture\n90:     above): all git/grep checks re-run and pass (`70f6236` ancestor of HEAD and\n91:     `origin/main`; `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` empty;\n92:     no `bg-white` in `src/routes/auth/`; no `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark*` pair in\n93:     `src/`; TimePicker on `bg-c-bg-modal`). Production re-checked live:\n94:     `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` serves HTTP 200 with `bg-c-bg-surface`\n95:     present and **0** `bg-white` occurrences, and\n96:     `/themes/nord/nord.css` serves `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252` /\n97:     `--color-white: #eceff4`. Conclusion unchanged: duplicate of `70f6236`,\n98:     no product change needed.\n99: \n100: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n101: \n102: - This job is a duplicate: the defect was already fixed by `70f6236` before this\n103:   branch's `main` merge. Product behaviour needs no change; close against the\n104:   existing fix.\n105: - `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale — it was written at rev 4\n106:   before the `70f6236` merge and still describes the pre-fix auth-card classes.\n107:   Left as the analyst's artifact; the corrected picture is here.\n108: - Inherited open items (out of scope): pre-paint theme script / FOUC hardening\n109:   (`theme.load()` runs in `onMount`, so there is still a brief light-default flash\n110:   before a single-mode theme applies), an `html`/`body` background-color rule, an\n111:   account-synced theme setting, and `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` existing on disk\n112:   but missing from `src/lib/config/themes.ts`.\n113: - Same bug class, outside this job's auth scope: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Progress.svelte:74`\n114:   still uses `not-dark:bg-white`, which renders white under single-mode dark\n115:   themes (`.dark` absent) — candidate for a follow-up identical to TASK-3.\n116: - Cosmetic consistency (not applied): auth labels use bare `dark:text-white`\n117:   while most of the app uses `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`.\n\n(End of file - total 117 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"## Summary\n\nThe white surface reported in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, not the page body\nand not a late/failed theme load. The six auth cards used the literal pair\n`bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` carries\nthe `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\nexplicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode:\nfalse`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal,\npaper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback therefore never\napplied, so the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white\n`--color-white: #eceff4` (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`) on an otherwise-Nord\npage — a stable state, not a flash.\n\nThat defect is **already fixed and present in this branch**. Commit `70f6236`\n(\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\nswept the auth cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token and\n`TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`; it reached this branch through the `main`\nmerge `8c0ad30`. `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is\nempty, so this branch contributes no product source change. **This job is a\nduplicate of the earlier fix and needs no code change** — the correct outcome is","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","text":"## Summary\n\nThe white surface reported in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, not the page body\nand not a late/failed theme load. The six auth cards used the literal pair\n`bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` carries\nthe `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` (`src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts:81`)\nexplicitly removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode:\nfalse`: nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal,\npaper, atari). Under Nord the themed `dark:bg-s-dark-2` fallback therefore never\napplied, so the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white\n`--color-white: #eceff4` (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:47-48`) on an otherwise-Nord\npage — a stable state, not a flash.\n\nThat defect is **already fixed and present in this branch**. Commit `70f6236`\n(\"nord theme bug with todos\", Job `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos`, 2026-08-25)\nswept the auth cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token and\n`TimePicker.svelte` to `bg-c-bg-modal`; it reached this branch through the `main`\nmerge `8c0ad30`. `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is\nempty, so this branch contributes no product source change. **This job is a\nduplicate of the earlier fix and needs no code change** — the correct outcome is\nto close it against `70f6236`.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: No product code. Environment facts were captured against the real\n  production app (`https://my.solyto.app`, the app host from\n  `src/lib/config/platform.ts`; bare `solyto.app` is the marketing landing page).\n  After seeding `localStorage.setItem('theme','nord')` and booting the page:\n\n  | fact | value |\n  | --- | --- |\n  | `localStorage.theme` | `\"nord\"` |\n  | `documentElement.className` | `\"\"` (no `dark` class — by design for single-mode themes) |\n  | login card class | `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface …` |\n  | computed card `background-color` | `rgb(59, 66, 82)` = Nord `#3b4252` |\n  | computed card `color` | `rgb(216, 222, 233)` = Nord `#d8dee9` |\n  | `--color-white` / `--color-c-bg` / `--color-c-bg-surface` | `#eceff4` / `#2e3440` / `#3b4252` |\n  | Nord stylesheet present | yes |\n\n  Hypothesis A (different stored theme) is the documented root-cause mechanism,\n  now fixed in code; Hypothesis B (stale/skewed production assets) is disproven —\n  production already serves the fixed markup (`bg-c-bg-surface`) and renders the\n  card as Nord `#3b4252`. The `brief.md` screenshot decodes to a 973x989 Nord page\n  with one near-white centred region (≈5.9%), i.e. the pre-fix card, matching the\n  `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark-2` failure mode rather than a FOUC (the surrounding\n  page is Nord, not default-light).\n\nTASK-2: No change needed. All nine auth-card blocks already carry\n  `bg-c-bg-surface`: `login:110`, `register:92`,\n  `forgot-password:72,100`, `reset-password:72,85,105`, `logout:27`,\n  `verify/[user_id]/[token]:44`. `--color-c-bg-surface` resolves to `#ffffff` in\n  default light (`src/styles/tokens.css:24`), `var(--color-s-dark-2)` in default\n  dark (`src/styles/default.css:19`, pixel-identical to the old\n  `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`), and `#3b4252` under Nord\n  (`static/themes/nord/nord.css:34,73`). The two secondary substitutions named\n  in the task were deliberately **not** applied:\n  - `dark:text-white` → `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`: auth labels already\n    inherit a correctly themed colour from `src/routes/auth/+layout.svelte`\n    (`text-c-neutral-8` = Nord `#d8dee9`, ≈7:1 on `#3b4252`). Adding an explicit\n    light-mode token would change default-light rendering (`c-neutral-8` →\n    `c-neutral-9`), which TASK-2 requires to stay pixel-identical.\n  - `border-white/5` → token border: no target token was specified, and\n    `--color-c-border` is transparent / not overridden by Nord, so a blind swap\n    would remove the decorative card outline. The accepted upstream fix left it\n    untouched.\n\nTASK-3: No change (optional item, and already resolved). `TimePicker.svelte`\n  already uses `bg-c-bg-modal`, fixed by the same `70f6236` sweep. No\n  `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark*` pair remains anywhere under `src/`.\n\nTASK-4: Verification.\n  - Repo: `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` → true **and**\n    `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 origin/main` → true;\n    `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` is empty. All nine\n    auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`; `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/`\n    → none; `grep -rn 'bg-white' src/ | grep 'dark:bg-s-dark'` → none. The\n    remaining `bg-white` hits under `src/` are decorative (icon dots, toggle knob,\n    score bar) plus the known `Progress.svelte:74` follow-up.\n  - Production: `curl https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` → HTTP 200, **0**\n    occurrences of `bg-white`, **1** of `bg-c-bg-surface`; the login card class is\n    exactly `… border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface px-8 pt-6 pb-8 shadow-sm\n    md:min-w-80`. The white card from `brief.md` is not reproducible.\n  - Rendered sweep (production, recorded in `screenshots/render-report.md`): the\n    login card is dark under every single-mode dark theme and light only under the\n    by-design light themes (default-light, `catppuccin-latte`, `paper`).\n  - Limitation: `node_modules` is not installed, and the project hard rule forbids\n    installing packages without asking, so `npm run check`/`lint`/`test`/`build`\n    could not be run. With no product diff there is nothing new for them to check.\n  - Final independent re-verification (2026-10-07, same day as the prod capture\n    above): all git/grep checks re-run and pass (`70f6236` ancestor of HEAD and\n    `origin/main`; `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` empty;\n    no `bg-white` in `src/routes/auth/`; no `bg-white … dark:bg-s-dark*` pair in\n    `src/`; TimePicker on `bg-c-bg-modal`). Production re-checked live:\n    `https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` serves HTTP 200 with `bg-c-bg-surface`\n    present and **0** `bg-white` occurrences, and\n    `/themes/nord/nord.css` serves `--color-c-bg-surface: #3b4252` /\n    `--color-white: #eceff4`. Conclusion unchanged: duplicate of `70f6236`,\n    no product change needed.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- This job is a duplicate: the defect was already fixed by `70f6236` before this\n  branch's `main` merge. Product behaviour needs no change; close against the\n  existing fix.\n- `docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/tasks.md` is stale — it was written at rev 4\n  before the `70f6236` merge and still describes the pre-fix auth-card classes.\n  Left as the analyst's artifact; the corrected picture is here.\n- Inherited open items (out of scope): pre-paint theme script / FOUC hardening\n  (`theme.load()` runs in `onMount`, so there is still a brief light-default flash\n  before a single-mode theme applies), an `html`/`body` background-color rule, an\n  account-synced theme setting, and `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` existing on disk\n  but missing from `src/lib/config/themes.ts`.\n- Same bug class, outside this job's auth scope: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Progress.svelte:74`\n  still uses `not-dark:bg-white`, which renders white under single-mode dark\n  themes (`.dark` absent) — candidate for a follow-up identical to TASK-3.\n- Cosmetic consistency (not applied): auth labels use bare `dark:text-white`\n  while most of the app uses `text-c-neutral-9 dark:text-white`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":117,"totalLines":117,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791403858014,"end":1791403858420}},"id":"prt_117fd9834001EMMuTEkSD3Bd3k","sessionID":"ses_ee80287fdffeBZlXIz12YKGjBW","messageID":"msg_117fd9151001d6ax01nb2QupfJ"}}
