t\\nline 1452 NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT\\\\\\\" docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log | head -60\\\"},\\\"output\\\":\\\"/usr/bin/bash: line 1: rg: command not found\\\\n\\\",\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"output\\\":\\\"/usr/bin/bash: line 1: rg: command not found\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit\\\":0,\\\"truncated\\\":false},\\\"title\\\":\\\"cd /workspace && rg -n \\\\\\\"=== 2026.*developer|NEEDS-HUMAN-I\\nline 1455 NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT:[^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]{0,200}\\\\\\\" docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log | head -10\\\"},\\\"output\\\":\\\"=== 2026-10-07T12:48:03Z developer (attempt 1) ===\\\\n=== 2026-10-07T17:22:53Z developer (attempt 1) ===\\\\n=== 2026-10-07T17:22:53Z developer (attempt 1) ===\\\\n=== 2026-10-07T17:22:53Z developer (attemp\\nline 1458 NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log; echo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"=== last lines types ===\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; grep -o '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"[a-z-]*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"' docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log | sort | uniq -c\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"...output truncated...\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFull output save\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"step_finish\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"time\\n\",\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"cd /workspace && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport json,re\\nwith open('docs/jobs/create_theme-on-login/session.log') as f:\\n    for i,line in enumerate(f):\\n        if 'NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT' in line:\\n            # find context\\n            m=re.search(r'NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT.{0,300}', line)\\n            print('line',i, m.group(0)[:300] if m else '')\\nEOF\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791395732339,\"end\":1791395732439}},\"id\":\"prt_117819a26001Y1fXfY8mAxaNFv\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee880a7b0ffeIqckXNvh7zeCm7\",\"messageID\":\"msg_11781852d001sGRhvONtbT2qo0\"}}\n1793:{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791402195510,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee81c8321ffee0yUMADgf5p7WF\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_117e43086001ny95z3tq5H2Wxg\",\"messageID\":\"msg_117e427ac00124iLJoosp0pb3m\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee81c8321ffee0yUMADgf5p7WF\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Done. Worktree is clean and the branch is left in the correct state.\\n\\n## What I found\\n\\nThe job is a **verified duplicate** — the defect in `brief.md` (\\\"white background on login with Nord\\\") was already fixed on `main` before this branch merged, and this branch carries no product source change.\\n\\nEvidence I re-verified independently this pass:\\n\\n| Check | Result |\\n|---|---|\\n| `grep 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/ static/` | no matches |\\n| All 9 auth-card blocks | use `bg-c-bg-surface` (login:110, register:92, forgot-password:72,100, reset-password:72,85,105, logout:27, verify:44) |\\n| `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 HEAD` | true (the `role_nord-theme-bug-with-todos` fix is in history) |\\n| `git diff main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` | empty |\\n| `screenshots/render-report.md` | production login card = Nord `#3b4252`, no white pixels under any single-mode dark theme |\\n\\n**Root cause (already documented):** the older auth cards used the literal pair `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, but `ThemeState.apply()` removes it for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false`, e.g. Nord), so the themed fallback never applied and the card stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`. Commit `70f6236` swept these to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface` token.\\n\\nThe remaining `dark:text-white` labels on auth pages are correct as-is (they inherit the themed color when `.dark` is absent, and are white on the dark card when it is present); changing them would alter default-light rendering, which TASK-2 requires to keep pixel-identical.\\n\\n## Actions taken\\n\\n- No product code changed (none is needed).\\n- `implementation.md`, `notes.md`, and the render evidence were already present and accurate from prior passes, so I did not rewrite them.\\n- Committed the live `session.log` sync as `5c0a926`; `git status` is now clean.\\n\\n## Note\\n\\n`tasks.md` is stale (written at rev 4 before the `70f6236` merge) and still describes the pre-fix classes; the accurate picture is in `notes.md` / `implementation.md`. Also, this branch has accumulated a very long chain of identical no-op sessions — the job's correct outcome is to be **closed against `70f6236`**, not re-dispatched.\\n\\nI did not print `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT` because the job was completable: the analysis is conclusive and no code change is required. Verification commands (`npm run check/lint/test/build`) still can't run here because `node_modules` is absent and the project forbids installing packages without approval.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791402193030,\"end\":1791402195502}}}\n1843:{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791402263471,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee81bb8f2ffe5kGw8HEzVtimhV\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_117e53b89001lCuULogPKLPW6z\",\"messageID\":\"msg_117e52a0e001Vh61VhYfR5gABr\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee81bb8f2ffe5kGw8HEzVtimhV\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I've completed the job. Here's what I found and did.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThe white surface reported in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, and that defect is **already fixed upstream** — this branch requires no product change. It is effectively a duplicate of commit `70f6236` (`nord theme bug with todos`).\\n\\n## Why no code change\\n\\nThe auth cards used `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant only fires when `<html>` has the `dark` class, and `ThemeState.apply()` removes that class for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false` — nord, skyrim, catppuccin-mocha/-latte, gruvbox, dracula, terminal, paper, atari). Under Nord the card therefore stayed at Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4` on an otherwise-Nord page.\\n\\n`70f6236` swept those cards to the semantic `bg-c-bg-surface`. I verified independently:\\n\\n- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 70f6236 origin/main` → **true**, and `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- src/ static/ tests/ package.json` is **empty** — the fix is upstream, not contributed by this branch.\\n- `grep -rn 'bg-white.*dark:bg-s-dark' src/` → **no matches**; all nine auth-card blocks carry `bg-c-bg-surface`.\\n- Token mapping is correct and pixel-identical in default light/dark: `--color-c-bg-surface` = `#ffffff` (`tokens.css:24`) → `var(--color-s-dark-2)` under `html.dark` (`default.css:19`) → `#3b4252` under Nord (`nord.css:34,73`).\\n\\n## Tasks\\n\\n- **TASK-1** (analysis): confirmed Hypothesis A (different stored theme) is the root-cause mechanism and B (version skew) is disproven — production already serves the fixed markup and renders Nord `#3b4252`.\\n- **TASK-2**: no change needed — the swap is already present.\\n- **TASK-3**: skipped — already fixed by the same commit, and it's marked \\\"needs owner go-ahead\\\".\\n- **TASK-4**: verification recorded in `screenshots/render-report.md`; `npm run check/lint/test/build` still cannot run because `node_modules` is not installed and the project hard rule forbids installing packages without asking.\\n\\n## Committed\\n\\n`implementation.md` (with a second-pass verification section) plus the live session artifacts. `git status` is clean.\\n\\nNo `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT` — the correct outcome (close as duplicate) did not require a human decision.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791402261385,\"end\":1791402263464}}}\n--- tail ---\n-8 pt-6 pb-8 shadow-sm md:min-w-80 dark:bg-s-dark-2\\\"\\n+\\t\\tclass=\\\"mb-4 flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-lg border-2 border-white/5 bg-c-bg-surface px-8 pt-6 pb-8 shadow-sm md:min-w-80\\\"\\n \\t\\t{onsubmit}\\n \\t>\\n \\t\\t<label class=\\\"label\\\">\\ndiff --git a/src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte b/src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte\\nindex 5001c76..da594c2 100644\\n--- a/src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte\\n+++ b/src/routes/auth/reset-password/+page.svelte\\n@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@\\n \\n \\t{#if invalidLink || failed}\\n \\t\\t<div\\n-\\t