{"type":"text","timestamp":1791404085492,"sessionID":"ses_ee8011a3bffeV4KB1WLJty6CkA","part":{"id":"prt_1180106a8001V3EFFrT3bHKSVH","messageID":"msg_11800dce60015MoxyT4FuFaUF4","sessionID":"ses_ee8011a3bffeV4KB1WLJty6CkA","type":"text","text":"I've completed the investigation and committed the artifacts. Here's what I found — and why this needs a human decision.\n\n## Findings\n\n**Root cause (confirmed from primary evidence, not prior notes):**\nThe white surface in `brief.md` is the auth **card**, not the page body and not a failed/late theme load.\n- I decoded the linked screenshot (973×989): the only near-white region is a single **320×280 px** rectangle at (374,339)–(693,618), colour `#eceff4` — exactly the auth card's `md:min-w-80` (320 px) width — sitting on an otherwise-Nord `#353d4a` page. So it's a stable card, not a FOUC.\n- The old cards used `bg-white dark:bg-s-dark-2`. The `dark:` variant requires `.dark` on `<html>`, but `ThemeState.apply()` removes it for every single-mode theme (`supportsDarkMode: false` — Nord, Skyrim, Catppuccin, Gruvbox, Dracula, Terminal, Paper, Atari). Under Nord the fallback never fired, leaving Nord's deliberately near-white `--color-white: #eceff4`.\n\n**The fix already exists and is live:**\n- All nine auth-card blocks already use `bg-c-bg-surface`; `grep 'bg-white' src/routes/auth/` → none.\n- `70f6236` (\"nord theme bug with todos\", 2026-08-25) performed exactly this swap on all six auth cards; it is an ancestor of both `HEAD` and `origin/main`.\n- `git diff main...HEAD -- src static tests package.json` is **empty** — this branch contributes no product source.\n- Production: `curl https://my.solyto.app/auth/login` → HTTP 200, `bg-c-bg-surface ×1`, `bg-white ×0`, `dark:bg-s-dark-2 ×0`.\n- No remaining theme-unsafe surface on the auth pages (inputs use the themed `c-bg-elevated`; residual `bg-white` hits are decorative or the known `Progress.svelte` follow-up).\n- TASK-3 (`TimePicker`) is also already fixed (`bg-c-bg-modal`). The two secondary auth swaps the tasks requested (`dark:text-white`, `border-white/5`) were deliberately not applied — they would change default-light rendering, violating TASK-2's \"pixel-identical\" constraint.\n\n**Conclusion:** the six auth pages described in `tasks.md` are already correct; the job is a verified duplicate of `70f6236`. `implementation.md` now records this session's independent verification. Worktree is clean (commit `732b28d`).\n\nNo code change is possible or warranted, and resolving this job — closing it as a duplicate instead of the 19th re-dispatch — is a bookkeeping decision only a human/orchestrator can make.\n\nNEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT: This job is a verified duplicate of the already-merged, already-live fix `70f6236`; there is nothing left to implement, so a human must close it as a duplicate rather than re-dispatch it.","time":{"start":1791404082856,"end":1791404085485}}}
